1 NOTE {geni:about_me} -------------------- Gebeurenisse:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.	Graf von Ketteler bou na familiedispute die kasteel Hendringen Kettelberg
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.	Court Ketelshagen word in 1451 vermeld
2 CONT
2 CONT 3.	Die Von Ketel-familie was die stigters van Ketelhagen(Mecklenburg-Verpommern)
2 CONT
2 CONT 4..	Stamvaders:
2 CONT
2 CONT a.	Dietrich Ketteler jun. is Stammherr in Herdringen-1411 b.	Dietrich Ketteler dies and there are inheritance disputes. New Stammherr is Friedrich Ketteler
2 CONT
2 CONT 5.     Graf Von Ketel: Earliest named owner of estate of Ketelshagen, near Putbus, on the island of  Rugen, before 1451; approximate date of death based on possession of Ketelshagen by his sons in 1452. Date of birth a guess - cou
2 CONC ld be anywhere from 1370 to 1420. Graf, meaning Count, a title, not a first name.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source Asa K. Gage
2 CONT
2 CONT 6.   Volgens 2014 OneGreatFamily.com Web84 was Graf Von Ketel een of ander tyd met NN Von Montfort getroud. Geen dokumentasie bewyse kon daarvoor gevind word nie.
2 CONT
2 CONT 7.    Nageslag van Graf Friedrich von Keteler:
2 CONT
2 CONT .     .                      Graf von Keteler
2 CONT
2 CONT  Kinders:   i. Berthold           en        ii Konrad von Ketel
2 CONT
2 CONT ii.  Conrad{Cordt} Von Ketel------------------------------->Ouer broer: i. Berthold von Ketel  
2 CONT
2 CONT Conrad Von Ketel x Adelheid of Cobbenrobe,                                                                                                                      *Ketelshagen, Rugen, Pomerania, Denmark.                              
2 CONC                                                                                                           Also listed as Curdt(Cordt) von Ketel{Son of                                                                                
2 CONC                                                                                                                         Count Friedrich von Keteler}, date of birth a                                                                 
2 CONC                                                           guess, based on his part ownership of Ketels-                                                                                                                         hagen 
2 CONC in 1452 and subsequent sale of his half                                                                                                                           of the estate to Berndt Von Buggenhagen in                          
2 CONC                                                                                                      the middle of the 15th century. Source Asa K.                                                                                    
2 CONC                                           Gage.
2 CONT
2 CONT Inligting verskaf: Ds. MG Müller 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT      'Von' preffix and 'Graf' title was added to Curdt Ketels name after marriage to the Austrian daughter of Konrad 'Von' Montfort. • (Montfort, Bregenz incorporated into the duchy of Austria in 1451.) This is also when the Ketel
2 CONC  childrens names take on a Germanic flair. At the same time 'Ketels Grove' becomes 'Ketelshagen'
2 CONT  Curdt is the father of Curdt II and Berthold of Rugen Island, part of Denmark at the time. This family is not part of the Kettler line of Westphalia. Curths Grandfather is Chancillor Bishop Asulf Ketilsson, Bishop Ketill is menti
2 CONC oned in ceremony on Dec. 5 1305.with Bishop Erland Installing Canon Arne Sigurdsson as Bishop of Bergen, King Hakon V and Euphemia of Rugen present. King Hakon of Rugen proclaims he has taken the dowry of his Queen Euphemia of Rug
2 CONC en from Vitzlav, Prince of Rugen. Ketill Havardsson, Curths Great Grandfather was appointed as Chancillor to Prince of Rugen, Jaromar the II.  *(From Wikipedia: "The Archbishop of the Monarch Chancellor Ketill was enthralled, and 
2 CONC the peasants aroused against Christopher and his vassals, so that they devastated their castles and estates") This line goes back to  The Wends, Swedish Pomerania, as well as to Burislav Von Rugen through Curths mother Ragnhild Og
2 CONC mundarsdatter explaining why Curths family is said to have had holdings in Anklam Sweden. Anklam was "The Wends" in western Pomerania, Sweden. Curths Fathers line goes all the way back through Helgi Bjornarson Bunu, Brother of Ket
2 CONC il Flatnose(Bunu is a nickname that means 'Hard worker') I will put up more generations later. 
