1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT *[http://freepages.genealogy.rootsweb.com/~daysgoneby/p39.htm#i897 freepages.genealogy]
2 CONT * Berthold Von Ketel was born circa 1440 at Ketelshagen, Rugen, Pomerania, Denmark. He was the son of Graf Von *Ketel. Berthold Von Ketel married an unknown person. He died circa 1505.
2 CONT *Children of Berthold Von Ketel
2 CONT >#    Hennig Von Ketel b. b 1490
2 CONT >#        Bartelt Von Ketel b. b 1490
2 CONT >#        Heinrich Von Ketel b. b 1490
2 CONT >#        Anthonius Von Ketel+ b. c 1490, d. 1570
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Inligting: Verskaf Ds. MG Müller
2 CONT
2 CONT Gebeurtenisse:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.	On the Rügen Ketel, however, were mentioned in documents in 1451, when Berthold and Curth vK half of Ketelshagen at the instigation of the Pomeranian Duke "Warthislaws IX" to a Berndt v. Buggenhagen, proven son of Degner v. Bug
2 CONC genhagen sold.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.	The next documentary registration was then performed in 1505 by Berthold's death, were enfeoffed as his sons Hennig, Berthold, Henry(Heinrich) and Anthony with the remaining half of Ketelshagen.
2 CONT
2 CONT 3.	Until the beginning of the 30-year war. When it came to the permanent change of occupier with the first peoples disputes attracted hardship and misery, robbery and murder on the island. Reprisals were common and the inhabitants
2 CONC  left the island anxiously, as well as the family Ketel(Na 1608).(1-4:- from: www.bookcollection.de / Familiev.Ketel.htm by Ingrid Hesse-Werner) 
2 CONT
2 CONT 4      Children:  
2 CONT
2 CONT 	1. Anthonius Von Ketel, *Ketelshagen, Rugen, Pomerania, Denmark
2 CONT
2 CONT         2. Hennig Ketel
2 CONT
2 CONT  	3. Berthold Ketel
2 CONT
2 CONT + 	4. Heinrich Ketel(Ketel Hindrik)
2 CONT
2 CONT 5	Die Potgieter voorouers is deur Patrick van Griethuisen en Dr. Ludwich Edel nagevors en terug gevolg tot by Bernd Potgeiter wat trou met ‘n dogter van Heinrich Keteler. Hy kom van Essen, op die Ruhr, na Nordhorn wat in die Graaf
2 CONC skap Bentheim, Duitsland Geleё is. In 1546 is sy naam in die Burgersboek daar ingeskryf en in 1577 word hy nog daar in ‘n akte genome. Sy skoonpa, Hynrich Keteler, of ook Kettel Hinrik genoem, woon omstreeks 1500 tot 1537 in Ossen
2 CONC hoek-Genealogie van Hanekom
2 CONT
2 CONT 6	Charlemagne introduces Christianity with the sword. Founding of the scholten system. Emlichheim, Uelsen, Veldhausen and Nordhorn become church and court districts.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT This Family of Von Ketel in KetelsHAGEN on Rugen Island should not to be confused with the Kettler family of KetelBURG in Herringen and Westphalia. The Norse branch of the Ketel family had been on Rugen since it was still a pagan 
2 CONC stronghold in the 1100's. Boleslaw / Burislav I "Chrobny" "the Brave" Von Rugen, Prince of the Wends, King of Poland was the 9th Great Grandfather to Curth Von Ketel. Jaromar the 1st, Prince of Rugen, was married to Hildegard Knut
2 CONC sdotter of the House of Stenkil (Ketil) c1160. In 1169 Arch Bishop Absalon, of the Hvide Ketil clan led the conquest of Rugen and the destruction of the temple and it's idols and appointed other Bishops from the house of Ketil to 
2 CONC oversee the reformation and conversion of the people. Absalon incorporated Rugen into his diocese of Roskilde (Denmark. the Wends. Aklam nearby.) and brought Danish supremacy to Northern Germany that would last until 1225. Archbis
2 CONC hop Absalon was the son of Asser Rigg. (Asser is an adaptation of As-Ketil. ) Bishop Eskil (God-Ketil) who participated in the raid was charged with the conversion of the Pagans on Rugen. The Pagan Temples and properties were seiz
2 CONC ed by the Church and Allocated to the Bishops. This is the beginning of Ketel settlement on Rugen. In 1257 we find Bishop Asulf Ketil acting as Chancellor to Prince Jaromar the 2nd. The son of Bishop Asulf Ketil, Bishop Herleik As
2 CONC ulfsson is recorded with Prince Jaromar of Rugen, Eric of Pomerania and is related to Bogislav who officially awarded the land for Ketelshagen. It is Herleiks' son, Curth who is mentioned variously as Graf Von Ketel, Graf or Count
2 CONC , Curth of Ketelshagen. ( Curth married a daughter of German nobility, Von Montfort family. It is here the estate becomes known as Ketels 'hagen' and names and titles in the now 'Von' Ketel family take on a Germanic flair.) This b
2 CONC rings to us to 1451 when Curth sells 1/2 of Ketelshagen and in 1452 divides the remaining 1/2 between his sons Berthold and Conrad.
