1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * [http://freepages.genealogy.rootsweb.com/~daysgoneby/p39.htm#i876 .rootsweb.ancestry...]
2 CONT * '''Heinrich Von Ketel'''
2 CONT >>*M, #876, b. circa 1530
2 CONT *He was greatly honord as a member of the ancient patrician family and was a distinguished senator.1 Heinrich Von Ketel was born circa 1530 at Ketelshagen, Rugen, Pomerania, Denmark. He was the son of Jurgen Von Ketel I. Heinrich 
2 CONC Von Ketel ''married'' [http://freepages.genealogy.rootsweb.com/~daysgoneby/p39.htm#i878 '''Anna Schuttens''']. He was the first of the family to leave Rugen permanently and move across the strait to Stralsund. He became a senator 
2 CONC and burgomaster of Stralsund. A share of his father's feudal tenure was conferred on him by Duke Philip Julius of Pomerania. It is thought that Heinrich gave his share of Ketelshagen to his brother Claus.
2 CONT *''Child'' of Heinrich Von Ketel and Anna Schuttens
2 CONT >#    [http://freepages.genealogy.rootsweb.com/~daysgoneby/p39.htm#i846 '''Joachim Von Ketel'']'+ b. c 1550
2 CONT ----
