1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stockhausen_(westf%C3%A4lisches_Adelsgeschlecht)
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Ludwig II. von Stockhausen''', (* around 1565 , † 1636 ) was rent''' master of the Landdrost of the Duchy of Westphalia'''. '''Kaspar von Fürstenberg zu Bilstein and Richter zu Olpe, Drolshagen, Wenden, Calle and Remblinghausen
2 CONC '''. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1599 married it in''' Mülheim/Möhne Elisabeth of Hanxleden .''' 1603 was he of Propst Gottfried of Furstenberg with the Good Stockhausen invested. He died in Arnsberg and left a son .'''Ludwig III . by Stockhausen''' (* 1600 , † 1
2 CONC 672 ) lived 1641 - 1670 on the always still the pen Meschede lehnspflichtigen Good Stockhausen . He was an electoral knight at Calle and Remblinghausen and, through his wife '''Anna Johanna von Westphalen''', had larger estates in
2 CONC  Remblinghausen received. In the Thirty Years War came there to great distress, so that he 1641 - 1659, the farms in Olpe, Frenkhausen, West field and Calle sell had. Since this without approval of the pin Meschede took place, was
2 CONC  he sued and his descendants had to a Judgment of the law faculty in Marburg pay a fine of 500 Taler to the pen.
2 CONT
2 CONT -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
