1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Lendmann Guttorm Åsolvsson, paa Rein=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Guttorm, was the  son of  Åsulv Skulesson på Rein og Tora * Skoftesdotter.
2 CONT * Guttorm lived at Rein and seems to have lived very long. He was probably the head of Skule Tostesson's highly regarded family in 1183.
2 CONT * Guthorm Aasolvsen, paa Rein. Guthorm was a son of Aasolv Skuleson. In 1136 he attended the assembly in Trondheim, together with other ndheim, together with other leaders and chieftains when Sigurd III Mouth was proclaimed King o
2 CONC f Norway
2 CONT * Born possibly in Rein i Rissa, Fosen, Sør-Trøndelag, Norge 
2 CONT * He is referred to as one of the countrymen who, after Harald Gilles died in 1136, supported Harald's son, Sigurd Munn. He was Sigurd's guardian and got him elevated to the throne. Guttorm and his entire family were closely assoc
2 CONC iated with the Trønder Party around Sigurd Mund and Haakon 
2 CONT * Guttorm Asulfsson lived at Rein, Austria.
2 CONT * Lendmann. Lived from 1120 to 1183.
2 CONT * Guttorm lived on reindeer and seems to have lived very long. He was well in 1183, head of Skule Tostensson's highly-regarded ancestry. He is referred to as one of the loins men who, after Harald Gilles' death in 1136, supported 
2 CONC Harald's son, Sigurd the mouth. He was Sigurd's guardian and had him elevated to the throne. Guttorm and his entire ancestry were close to the Trøndelag party around Sigurd Mund and Haakon Herdebreid.
2 CONT
2 CONT From Snorre Sturlasson: Inges Saga: 1.... When the tithes came north to Trondheim that King Harald (Gille) was by Dage, Sigurd, son of King Harald, was taken to King there, And with this decision was Ottar birting, Peter Saue-Ulvs
2 CONC son and Brødrene Guttorm Åsolvsson from Rein and Ottar Balle and many other chieftains.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ð - http://xn--slkttrd-6wae.com/p8d028ebe.html
2 CONT
2 CONT =Married=
2 CONT
2 CONT Guttorm Åsolvson Rein F. Exp 1120, Rein on Rissa, Sør-Trøndelag.
2 CONT
2 CONT (1)  g. Eldrid, the daughter of Blindheim.
2 CONT
2 CONT (2)  g,1150, Sigrid Torkjellsdatter, d. after 1150.
2 CONT
2 CONT (3) g. Ingeborg's daughter Aure, F. Aure in the Sykulven, Møre og Romsdal.
2 CONT
2 CONT (4) g. Berljot on reindeer. Guttorm died in 1150.
2 CONT
2 CONT Married: 
2 CONT (1) ''' Eldrid Jonsdatter Smør, av Blindheim;''' Guttorm Åsolvsson of Rein was one of the loins men after Harald Gille Magnussons death in 1136 who supported his son Sigurd mouth Haraldsson. He was Sigurd Munn's body guard. Guttor
2 CONC m Åsolvsson of Rein had a brother Ottar Bale Åsulvsson, who was a mighty chieftain in Mid-Norway. Guttorm's wife, Eldrid was a daughter of Jon Smørbjalte.
2 CONT
2 CONT (2)''' Bergljot Svendsdatter på Rein;'''
2 CONT
2 CONT (3)  '''Sigrid Torkjellsdatter Fugl'''
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children with Eldrid Jonsdatter Smør, av Blindheim=
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/NORWEGIAN%20NOBILITY.htm Project MedLands,  NORWEGIAN Nobility]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''GUTTORM Asulfsson of Rein, son of ASULF Skulesson & his wife Thora Skoptisdotter.'''  Snorre names "Guthorm of Reine" as the son of "Asolf of Reine" & his wife[241].  Morkinskinna names “Ásólfr, the father of Guthormr at Rein” 
2 CONC as the son of “Skúli, the son of Jarl Tostig Godwinson”[242]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Guttorm & his --- wife had five children:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1.  '''RANGRID Guttormsdotter married firstly BJORN Byrdasven. Married secondly FREDERIK Kjona (-1164).''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Rangrid & her first husband BJORN Byrdasven had one child:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * a)  '''ELRID Bjornsdotter married firstly THORER Skindfeld, and  married secondly MAGNUS Erlingsson King of Norway, son of ERLING Ormsen "Skakke/the Sharp" Jarl in Norway & his wife Kristin Sigurdsdatter of Norway (1156-killed i
2 CONC n battle near Fimreite on Sognefjord 15 Jun 1184, bur Bergen, Christ's Church).'''
2 CONT * 2.        ''' INGERID  married GUTTORM Ostmansson.'''
2 CONT * 3.         '''GUDRUD'''
2 CONT * 4.         '''ASULF Guttormsson'''
2 CONT * 5.         '''BAARD Guttormsson of Rein''' (-1194).  Snorre names Bard as son of "Guthorm of Reine"[241].  Morkinskinna names “Guthormr at Rein” as father of “Bárdr, the father of King Ingi and Skúli jarl 242].  '''married first
2 CONC ly ULFHILD Palsdatter .  m secondly (after 15 Jun 1184) as her second husband, CECILIA Sigurdsdatter, divorced wife of FOLKVID Lagmand in Värmland, illegitimate daughter of SIGURD Haraldsson "Mund" Joint King of Norway & his mistr
2 CONC ess --- (-1185).'''  The Saga of King Sverre records that King Sverre arranged the marriage of "his sister Cecilia" to "Bard Guthormsson of Rein"[243], dated from the context to just after the death of King Magnus [15 Jun 1184].  
2 CONC m thirdly Ragnrid Erlingsdatter .  
2 CONT
