2 CONT Ancestral File Number:<AFN> progenitor-a
2 CONT
2 CONT BIOGRAPHY: Pierre JOURDAN, gebore 1663, van Cabriere was 'n Franse Hugenoot wat op 24 jarige ouderdom op die Berg China na SA gekom het in 1688. Hy was 'n broer van Jean Jourdan. Hy was getroud in 1696 met Anna FOUCHE, wat in 1713
2 CONC oorlede is. Pierre het hertrou in 1721 met Maria Verdeau, gebore 1700, d/v Hercule Verdeau. Pierre het gewoon op die plaas Cabriere (1694), Franschoek, en is oorlede op 28 Okt 1723 en het 6 kinders nagelaat, almal uit sy eerste hu
2 CONC welik:
2 CONT
2 CONT BIOGRAPHY: 1. Anna ~ 30 Des 1698 x Louis Fourie 2. Johanna x A de Nicker xx JD Hieber 3. Pierre ~ 6 Des 1700 4. Joseph ~ 30 Okt 1701 x Maria Magdalena le Roux, erf later die plaas Cabriere 5. Susanna ~ omtrent 1703 x Jan Jourdan 6
2 CONC . Marie ~ 23 Aug 1705 x 1 Feb 1722 Johannes Pretorius s/v Dirk xx David Sultania.
2 CONT
2 CONT BIOGRAPHY: According to Lorna Newcomb, who checked CJ 782 Ref 48. Pieter Joubert sent his slave Anthoni to Pieter Jordaan to borrow an axe. Anna Jordaan, aged about fourteen, was then raped by Anthoni. The document is dated 29 Jun
2 CONC e 1713.
2 CONT
2 CONT BIOGRAPHY: Verwysings: De Villiers/Pama Heese/Lombard Verwysingsmateriaal, Boksburg biblioteek Verwysingsmateriaal, Springs LDS FHC biblioteek
2 CONT
2 CONT BIOGRAPHY: Saamgestel deur: Martina Louw (nee van Breda) Kennethl@xtra.co.nz
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT He was a burger of Drakenstein, Cape. On 17 Nov., 1722 he w as exempted from miletary service due to a physical defec t ("Resolusies van die Politieke raad Deel VI 1720-1723") O n the 13th March, 1731 an incident, in which Hans wa
2 CONC s invol ved, wasdiscussed in the political council. Ten Bushmen (s ons of Grebenau) stole cattle from the farmar Hans Jurgen P otgieter after which they were followed and found by 12 bur gers. The bushmen started shooting arrows a
2 CONC t the burgers (" Resolusies vandiePolitieke raad Deel VI 1729-1734").  In the de la Fonteine report, comentary is given that coul d make a living from his cattle and farm, but not without d ebt (1732). It his also mentioned that F
2 CONC rederick Huppenaa r (son of his sister) livedwithhim as servant. On 13 April , 1738, after his death, his wife Cornelia remarried Cornel is van Rooyen from Gorinchem, Netherlands.
2 CONT
