1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Gudrun Tordsdotter=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Daughter of Tord Folesson and Ålov Einarsdotter 
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/photo/view?album_type=photos_of_me&id=6000000001205369626&photo_id=6000000010119783253&position=1 Giske-ætta]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/NORWEGIAN%20NOBILITY.htm#ThoraMAsulfSkulesson Project MedLands, Norway Nobility]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''OGMUND Thorbergsson''' His name is confirmed by Snorre naming his son "Skopte Ogmundson, a grandson of Thorberg"[46].  m ---.  The name of Ogmund´s wife is not known.  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Ogmund & his wife had one child'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * a)         '''SKOPTI Ogmundsson of Giske''' (-Rome 1103).  Snorre names "Skopte Ogmundson, a grandson of Thorberg", when recording that he "dwelt at Giske in Sunmore"[47].  Snorre records that Skopte Ogmundson travelled from Nor
2 CONC way with his sons Ogmund, Fin and Thord, that Skopte died in Rome, and that his sons also died during the journey[48].  '''married GUDRUN, daughter of THORD Folason & his wife''' ---.  Snorre names "Gudrun, a daughter of Thord Fol
2 CONC ason" as the wife of "Skopte Ogmundson"[49].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Skopti & his wife Gudrun had four children'''
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>* i)          '''OGMUND''' (-[1103]).  Snorre names (in order) "Ogmund, Fin, Thord and Thora" as children of "Skopte Ogmundson" & his wife[50].  Snorre records that Skopte Ogmundson travelled from Norway with his sons Ogmund, 
2 CONC Fin and Thord, that Skopte died in Rome, and that his sons also died during the journey[51]. 
2 CONT >>>>* ii)         '''FINN''' (-[1103]).  Snorre names (in order) "Ogmund, Fin, Thord and Thora" as children of "Skopte Ogmundson" & his wife[52].  Snorre records that Skopte Ogmundson travelled from Norway with his sons Ogmund, Fi
2 CONC n and Thord, that Skopte died in Rome, and that his sons also died during the journey[53]. 
2 CONT >>>>* iii)        '''TORD''' (-Sicily [1103]).  Snorre names (in order) "Ogmund, Fin, Thord and Thora" as children of "Skopte Ogmundson" & his wife[54].  Snorre records that Skopte Ogmundson travelled from Norway with his sons Ogm
2 CONC und, Fin and Thord, that his sons all died during the journey, Tord dying last in Sicily[55]. 
2 CONT >>>>* iv)       '''THORA Skoptisdatter'''  Snorre names (in order) "Ogmund, Fin, Thord and Thora" as children of "Skopte Ogmundson" & his wife, specifying that Thora married "Asolf Skulason"[56].  In an earlier Saga, Snorre names 
2 CONC "Thora, a daughter of Skopte Ogmundson" as the wife of "Asolf of Reine"[57].  m ASULF Skulesson of Rein, son of SKULI Tostesson & his wife Gudrun Nefsteinsdatter. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Gudrun Tordsdatter. Født før 1031.
2 CONT
2 CONT Cappelen's Norges Historie oppgis at Bård Guttormsson på Rein i Trøndelag blandt sine forfedre talte folk som Sigurd Syr, Toste jarl, Torberg Arnesson, Tord Folesson, Erling Skjalgsson, Einar Tambarskjelve og Håkon jarl den gamle.
2 CONC  Det fremgår ikke her eller hos Snorre Sturlasson hvori slektskapet med Einar Tambarskjelve består. I C. M. Munthe: «Norske slegtsmerker» og i «Rosensverdslektens forfedre» oppføres Tord Folessons hustru, Ålov å være datter til Ei
2 CONC nar Tambarskjelve. Det henvises ikke til hvilke kilder som har vært anvendt. 1
2 CONT
