1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Svend Thrugotsen''', known under both his Patronymic Thrugotsen and his Matronymic, Thorgunna, Thrugun, Trund, which is: Thorgunnasen, Thrugunsen and Trundsen. (If you throw too many balls to any juggler, then h
2 CONC e will sooner or later fail and drop some balls and this have happens to some of the children in this family), but not only was Svend known by all those names, he was also called Thorkil. His mother outlived his father by many yea
2 CONC rs, thus mentioned as "Langliva Mater dicta", she died february 8, but the year are unknown. According to the Knytlinga Saga: [https://www.geni.com/people/Knud-IV-den-hellige-konge-af-Danmark/6000000007219540254 Canute the Holy] c
2 CONC ourtiers and dearest friends; Svend and his brother Astrad accompanied Canute when the rebellion in Jutland broke out; during the battle in St. Albans priory in Odense  they defended him valiantly. After Canute's death in July 10,
2 CONC  1086, Sven and Astrad traveled to Flanders, where they met with [https://www.geni.com/people/Robert-I-count-of-Flanders/6000000002441720163 Count Balduin] and obtained the release of King Canute's brother [https://www.geni.com/pe
2 CONC ople/Oluf-I-Hunger-King-of-Denmark/347868854190012671 Oluf], who then returned to Denmark and was hailed as king.
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://heimskringla.no/wiki/Knytlinga_Saga_(C.C.Rafn)_ Knytlingasaga]
2 CONT
