2 CONT * '''Dating: 1318 November 12'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Öde Tanne sells to the prioress Margareta in S: t Johannes kloster in Kalmar 1/6 attung and 2 penningland in "Wangersclæwæ" (Vångerslät in Åby?). Present witnesses were Henrik Glysing, Harald Stubbe, Sven By, Peter "Cabbæ" and Alg
2 CONC ot, parish priest in Åby.
2 CONT
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/photo/view/6000000003827765237?album_type=photos_of_me&photo_id=6000000178118304007 '''Seal: Henrik Glysing,'''] Harald Stubbe, Sven By, Peter Cabbæ and Algot, parish priest in Åby.
2 CONT
2 CONT == SDHK No: [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?ValdSortering=DatumStigande&PageSize=20&Sokord=Kristina&EndastDigitaliserat=False&FacettLimits=IfjiTQ%3A0&AvanceradSok=True&page=53&FacettState=undefined%3Ac%7C&postid=sdhk_2394&tab=post#ta
2 CONC b '''2394''']
2 CONT
2 CONT Henrik Glysing gives to the nunnery in Kalmar as married for his daughter Kristina a farm in "Risine" and land in Övre Rinkaby (in Hossmo parish, S. Möre district?).
2 CONT
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/photo/view/6000000003827765237?album_type=photos_of_me&photo_id=6000000178117603204 '''Seal:  Mr. Karl Elinasson, bailiff in Kalmar, Mr. Hemming Ödgislesson and Gustav Elinasson.''']
2 CONT
2 CONT ==SDHK No: [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=Henrik+Glysing&EndastDigitaliserat=false&Fritext=Henrik+Glysing&AvanceradSok=True&page=1&postid=sdhk_1659&tab=post&FacettState=undefined%3ac%7c#tab '''1659''']
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Dating 1295 June 17 of issue Nykoping'''
2 CONT
2 CONT King Birger of Sweden announces that his father King Magnus once pledged the estate "snytærstad" to Mr. Henrik Glysing for 114 marks of lithe silver cologneous weight and then donated this mortgaged yard to the holy Klara's monast
2 CONC ery in Stockholm (regarding which gift Birger claims to have seen his father's letter) but then died, before he was able to redeem the estate, and the sisters in the monastery have subsequently redeemed it for the above sum. The i
2 CONC ssuer now approves and affirms with regard to his father's promises and wishes the gift of said estate to said monastery.
2 CONT
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/photo/view?album_type=photos_of_me&id=6000000003827765237&photo_id=6000000130281391853&position=1 '''Seal: The issuer and his marshal Tyrgils Knutsson.''']
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Letter Text'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Sweort Goths, by the grace of God, King of all the Byrgerus shall inspect these present letters, greetings and all good. ' The present document that we would be known to all that happy memory, Lord & father once King Swede Court a
2 CONC  town called snowy town pawned master Henry, called the sliding per cent, the Monastery of St. Clare in Stockholm, upon which the gift and letter of the master and the father has witnessed Seal his seal. Since the passage of time,
2 CONC  Oswald said owner and father, before said court reduced the call master, prevented by death, the sisters are famous monastery the curia from said Sir Henry glysing to use & rights of the monastery, for such a sum of money, to wit
2 CONC : one hundred and fourteen marks of pure gold and silver in Cologne examination by weight, redeemed supramemorati and then we have to hedge the father and our prayers and holy desires of acumerees this gift to ratify & -. disposit
2 CONC ion of ours, confirm and present writing. Jn at which the witness is this, the seals, our beloved Marsalchi our lord, lord Thyrgillus Knutson & that is to say, in the presence of healthy affixed. Date of Nycopia. In the Year of ou
2 CONC r Lord. Millesimo. ducentesimo. Ninety-fifth. In the St. Botolph Abbot. the hedge of calling to mind of a lord and of our father; disposition of ours, confirm and present writing. Jn at which the witness is this, the seals, our be
2 CONC loved Marsalchi our lord, lord Thyrgillus Knutson & that is to say, in the presence of healthy affixed. Date of Nycopia. In the Year of our Lord. Millesimo. ducentesimo. Ninety-fifth. In the St. Botolph Abbot. the hedge of calling
2 CONC  to mind of a lord and of our father; disposition of ours, confirm and present writing. Jn at which the witness is this, the seals, our beloved Marsalchi our lord, lord Thyrgillus Knutson & that is to say, in the presence of healt
2 CONC hy affixed. Date of Nycopia. In the Year of our Lord. Millesimo. ducentesimo. Ninety-fifth. In the St. Botolph Abbot. healthy seal affixed. Date of Nycopia. In the Year of our Lord. Millesimo. ducentesimo. Ninety-fifth. In the St.
2 CONC  Botolph Abbot. healthy seal affixed. Date of Nycopia. In the Year of our Lord. Millesimo. ducentesimo. Ninety-fifth. In the St. Botolph Abbot.
2 CONT
2 CONT * Seal: Pieces of seal 1, 2. in green wax hang on red and green silk nods.
2 CONT * Printed:  DS 1132, , Clara Minne, no. 25 Literature and notes.  See 12950609 (SDHK No. 1658 DS 1131) and 12950617 (SDHK No. 1660).
2 CONT
2 CONT ==SDHK No: [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=Henrik+Glysing&EndastDigitaliserat=false&Fritext=Henrik+Glysing&AvanceradSok=True&page=1&postid=sdhk_1658&tab=post&FacettState=undefined%3Ac%7C#tab '''1658''']
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Dating 1295 June 9 of issue Stockholm'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Henrik Glysing announces that he has left and handed over to the clearances in Stockholm the estate "Snytarstad", which King Magnus once pledged to him for 114 marks of soldered silver but the king also donated to the said clearan
2 CONC ces, which has now fully replaced the issuer for the above sum. Witnesses were the brothers Ture and Nils Kettilssons, who also sealed together with the issuer. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''letter text'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Shall inspect these present letters sent to all, Henry was called Glysing, greetings and all good. ' The present document that all concerned that we Court cutter city, which us a great happy memory once King Swede famous for a cer
2 CONC tain sum of money, one hundred fourteen Marchis clean and examine the silver in weight Cologne, impignoraute, dimisisseusib, Lord King, the court gave the agency the sum of the money from these sisters are fully satisfied. Jn witn
2 CONC ess whereof the seals of the illustrious men, the Lord of lords, the majority of trustworthy men who, when they Thurirs Ketilsson & then present, in adderant of Nicholas ffratris supra, together with the seal, are affixed to the p
2 CONC resence of our God. Date Stockholm. In the Year of our Lord. 1000 °. 200 ° .XC ° .v. Jdus fifth of June.
2 CONT
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/photo/view/6000000003827765237?album_type=photos_of_me&photo_id=6000000178123680944 '''Seal: 3 PCs. (More or less injured; see also lit Oh. Comm. 1): The seal in green wax: o 1, 2 and 3, more and less damag
2 CONC ed, on red and green silk threads''']
2 CONT
2 CONT * DS 1131 Nordberg, Clara Minne, n. 24, Literature and notes, No. 1 1: ture Kettilssons (Sv. Sig. 3, 80), no. 2: Knights NILS Kettilssons (Sv. Sig. 3, 94), no. 3: Henrik Glysing's (Sv. Sig. 3: 95).
2 CONT
2 CONT * [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=Henrik+Glysing&EndastDigitaliserat=false&Fritext=Henrik+Glysing&AvanceradSok=True&page=1&postid=sdhk_1658&tab=post&FacettState=undefined%3Ac%7C#tab Cf. 12950617 '''(SDHK no. 1659 DS 1132 and S
2 CONC DHK no. 1660)''']
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://sok.riksarkivet.se/sbl/Mobil/Artikel/13096 Glysing Family]
2 CONT
2 CONT Glysing, a medieval Holstein nobility, one branch of which came to belong to the Swedish High Savior. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The knight Henrik G, who was still alive in 1324, had lent King Magnus Ladulås (related to a daughter of the Count of Holstein) 114 marks of pure silver against mortgages in Uppland. He belonged to King Birger's vows both at the c
2 CONC onciliation with the dukes in 1308 and at the division of the kingdom in 1310. Later he appears exclusively in local records related to the Kalmar area.
2 CONT
2 CONT Henrik's son was possibly Kettil G, after his maternal lineage also called Puke G (d 1363 or 1364), who carried the same weapon. This is probably dubbed a knight at King Magnus Eriksson's coronation in 1336 and became councilor no
2 CONC  later than 1344. During the civil war between Magnus and his son Erik, G is mentioned among the latter's 30 seal witnesses in his grant letter 1356 in southern Halland for the Mecklenburg dukes Henrik and Albrekt dy, but it canno
2 CONC t be proved that he took part in the uprising. Prominent are G's distinguished family connections and connection to Småland, where his grandmother's father and brothers were lawyers in Tiohärad. His estate was thus in Småland and 
2 CONC Östergötland, and two of his sisters were married to the councilors Sune Jonsson (Båt) and Gustav Nilsson (Bielke), successively lawyers in Tiohärad.
2 CONT
2 CONT The family died out in Sweden on the male side with Kettil G's son Erik G (lived 1369), who during the civil war of the 1360s was active on Öland on behalf of King Albrekt. On the women's side, he died in 1413 with Erik G's sister
2 CONC  Katarina G: sdtr, who first, like one of his sisters, was married to a son of Saint Birgitta. After he died in Naples in 1372, she remarried one of the Germans who came with King Albrekt, the knight Johan Moltke, who fell in Väst
2 CONC ergötland against Queen Margaret in 1389. One of their daughters married the queen Kristiern Nilsson (Vaasa) in his first marriage.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Sources=
