2 CONT • notarized, Feb 1, 1519. Francis of Hoerde to Boke acknowledged his father Johann Hoberg to Waldenburg payment of 1,000 gold florins, which he has as a dowry for his wife Anna, Johanns daughter received.
2 CONT
2 CONT • notarized, 27 Mar 1543. Before the Electoral Cologne Judge Johann Ryssinck to Geseke Maes sold by Stormede Jacob Knyppinckstein and his wife Heyle a due annually on Martini pension of 0.5 bushels of corn, barley and half rye've 
2 CONC Geseker measure of 25 rh. Gulden from his possession in and around Geseke, which he holds by the heirs of + Franz von Hörde. It also lays a "desire letter" of Anne of Hoberch, widow of Franz von Hörde to this sale before. To guara
2 CONC ntor is the seller of Rotger Maes Stormede and Jacob Schulte tho Schwelde. The judge sealed with his official seal."
2 CONT
2 CONT Ref: https://isphording.info/html/genealogie/maindatabase02/8817.html
