1 NAME Claas (Claus) /Vechtman/
2 GIVN Claas (Claus)
2 SURN Vechtman
2 NICK Nicolaus Vechtermann
1 NAME Claas (Claus) Vechtman
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1635
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1708
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Bronne:
2 CONT
2 CONT German Personlia at the Cape 1652 -1802 - Dr J Hoge
2 CONT
2 CONT Claus Vechtmann from Meran in Tyrol. Burger and woodcutter(1667). Sentenced (1667) to do 3 years' hard labour for stabbing a man during a brawl. (C J 125:83) Married 10.5.1670 Beeltjie Frederiks of Amsterdam. One son Claas. (Monst
2 CONC errollen Vrye Lieden of 1667;CH 1123 p 6; Will 1.52) His son was a smith at Stellenbosch. Adam Tas (p 22) calls him "De kreuele Vulkaan.
2 CONT
2 CONT Judi Marais-Meyer
2 CONT ----
2 CONT He seems to have originally been in service of https://www.geni.com/people/Jacob-Cloete/6000000001423954088 because he is listed as follows in the 1667 Cape Muster roll:
2 CONT Jacob Cloeten, van Ceulen
2 CONT '''do. knechts'''    { Jan van Gorcum, van Rotterdam
2 CONT '''{ Claes Vechtman, van Tirole'''
2 CONT { Jacob Cornelisz [Sem], van Amsterdam
2 CONT ----
2 CONT [https://www.ancestors.co.za/database/slavefreeholdfarms-view.php?q=12 He was granted the farm "Varietas"]
2 CONT District Area	Cape Peninsula
2 CONT Year	1670
2 CONT Transfer1	Original Grant from Old Cape or Old Stellenbosch Freeholds Volumes
2 CONT Transfer1 Date	No Date
2 CONT Morgen	13.295
2 CONT Farm Name	Varietas
2 CONT Property Type	Plaas en Hofstede (Farm)
2 CONT Property Number	16
2 CONT Buyer Surname	Vegtman
2 CONT Buyer Names	Claas
2 CONT Purchase Price Comments	Normal Transaction
2 CONT Comments	Diagram or New Plan
2 CONT Map Coordinates	219282
