1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Jacobus Steyn b1 About version 20140708
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Brief summary: '''
2 CONT
2 CONT Parents: Unknown father X Maria Losëe. Two theories about his father. First: Probably Douwe Gerbrandt Steyn SV. Second and possible: Some other person.
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth: Cabo (dist of Cape Town), South Africa before 29 August 1683. He was born before his mother married Douwe Gerbrandt Steyn in 1685.
2 CONT
2 CONT Baptism: NG Kerk Cape Town, South Africa 29 August 1683.
2 CONT
2 CONT X Stellenbosch 24 October 1706 Maria Potgieter *bef.31 August 1687 ≈31 August 1687
2 CONT
2 CONT They had 11 children:
2 CONT
2 CONT c1 Maria ≈14 August 1707
2 CONT
2 CONT c2 Douwe ≈27 January 1709
2 CONT
2 CONT c3 Hermanus ≈12 July 1711
2 CONT
2 CONT c4 Sibella ≈7 October 1714; died young 
2 CONT
2 CONT c5 Emerentia  ≈21 March 1717
2 CONT
2 CONT c6 Jacobus ≈15 October 1719; twins with c7; died young
2 CONT
2 CONT c7 Sibella ≈15 October 1719; twins with c6
2 CONT
2 CONT c8 Jacobus ≈25 April 1723
2 CONT
2 CONT c9 Paulus ≈1 October 1724
2 CONT
2 CONT c10 Maria ≈21 September 1727
2 CONT
2 CONT c11 Anna ≈21 August 1729
2 CONT
2 CONT The two main Steyn branches come from c3 Hermanus and c8 Jacobus
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Jacobus Steijn involved in buying and selling slaves:''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1712.02.12 Lijsbeth f U SELLER: Beeletje Fredericks BUYER:Jacob Steijn
2 CONT
2 CONT 1715.03.25 Scipio m Malaba AGE: 22 SELLER:Willem Helot BUYER:Jacob Steijn
2 CONT
2 CONT 1715.03.27 Anthonij m Cochin AGE:18 SELLER:Willem Helot BUYER:Jacob Steijn
2 CONT
2 CONT 1721.11.29 Cupido m Bengal SELLER: Cornelis Valk BUYER:Jacob Steijn
2 CONT
2 CONT 1724.04.27 Carel m Batavi SELLER: Jacob Steijn BUYER: Anthonij Lombard
2 CONT
2 CONT 1724.08.21 Truij f Creole SELLER: Jacob Steijn BUYER: Hans Jurgen Potgieter
2 CONT
2 CONT 1724.08.21 Jager m Bogies SELLER:Jacob Steijn BUYER: Hans Potgieter
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Jacobus in the Cape Muster Roll:''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1703 page 35: Jacobus Steijn https://www.eggsa.org/sarecords/index.php/muster-rolls/cape-archive...
2 CONT
2 CONT 1712 page 257: Jacobus Steijn & Maria Harmense https://www.eggsa.org/sarecords/index.php/muster-rolls/cape-archive...
2 CONT
2 CONT 1713 page 280: Jacobus Steijn & Maria Potgieter https://www.eggsa.org/sarecords/index.php/muster-rolls/cape-archive...
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: communications from Marie Vermeulen-Boshoff
2 CONT
2 CONT '''NOTE: '''
2 CONT
2 CONT Reliable dates of birth of his children are found in recent publications only. Older publications about the Steyn family tree have big mix-ups.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Other information'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Jacobus was still alive in 1733 as he and his wife were listed in the Monsterrol 1733:    ''''t Caabse District    'Jacobus Stijn & Maria Potgieter'''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT -----------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Genealogical DNA Test will resolve the questions about the biological father of Jacobus Steyn'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Jacobus is the biological progenitor (stamvader) of the largest Steyn family in South Africa. He officially became part of the family of Douwe Gerbrandt Steyn in 1685 age 2 when Douwe married  his mother.  No-one is exactly sure w
2 CONC ho his father was. Throughout his lifetime he used the surname Steijn and is mentioned in the will of Douwe Gerbrandt Steyn as the ‘voorzoon’ (son born before marriage) of Maria Losëe but treated as the son of Douwe. 
2 CONT
2 CONT There has also been some speculation that his father might have been the father of Alexandrina (Sandrina) Maxwell, whose husband is thought to have bought Maria as slave.
2 CONT
2 CONT If enough STEYN descendants have their genealogical DNA tested with http://www.familytreedna.com/ or a similar company, we will not only be able to trace our common ancestry, but we might also be able to discover who the biologica
2 CONC l father of Jacobus was. Until now that has been a mystery, but with genealogical DNA testing, we might be able to solve the puzzle since the number of males in the Cape at the time were very limited.
2 CONT
2 CONT So: if at all possible, please do the test with familytreedna
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Owned the property 'Welgemeend' which is where Kamp Street is in Cape Town now.
2 CONT
2 CONT Was a butcher and brewer of brandy.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a free burgher.
2 CONT
2 CONT De la Fontaine describes him as a poor man. 
2 CONT
