1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Among the Cape inventories, is one for Maria Steijn:
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Reference no.: MOOC8/4.70
2 CONT
2 CONT 22 November 1724
2 CONT
2 CONT Staat ende inventaris mitsgr:s taxatie der goederen, naargelaten en met er dood ontruijmt door Maria Steijn, ten voordeele van haar naargelatenen man Hermanus Kriel ter eenre, en dogter Maria Kriel ter andere zijde, soo als als 't
2 CONC  door de ondergetek:de daartoe versogte goede mannen ter presentie van 't kinds grootvader Jacobus Steijn is gedaan, namentlijk
2 CONT
2 CONT deceased is Maria Steijn - her heirs are her surviving husband Hermanus Kriel and her daughter Maria Kriel - the inventory and valuation has been made in the presence of the child's grandfather Jacobus Steijn.
2 CONT
2 CONT This tells us that the Maria Steijn who married Hermanus Kriel was the daughter of Jacobus Steijn
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Maria STEYN *1707 was the first child of Jacobus 'Jacob' STEYN and Maria POTGIETER.
2 CONT
2 CONT She is sometimes confused with another Maria STEYN supposedly *1695 who is listed in some genealogies as a daughter of Douwe Gerbrandt STEYN and Maria LOZEE. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT According to the most reliable sources, this second Maria Steyn was not a daughter of Douwe Gerbrandt STEYN and Maria STEYN (LOZEE). There is no proof that she actually existed. Thanks to Richard Ball for the following information
2 CONC :
2 CONT
2 CONT The will of DGS names only four heirs (erfgenaame) his wife and three children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT soo verklaarde hij testateur tot sijne algheele en universeele egtgenaam te nomineeren en te institueeren, gelijk doet bij deesen, sijne huijsvrou Maria Lozee, in alle syne natelaten goederen, roerende en onroerende ... 
2 CONT
2 CONT dat sijn huijsvrouw gehouden blijden sal het bij haar verwekte dogtertje Anna Steijns behoorlijk op te voeden ... 
2 CONT
2 CONT En nog aan sijn testateurs voorsoon aga steijns een summe van f. 300:-: boven de sodanige summe van f.500 die hij reets van weegens hem testateur heeft genoten, en dat voor haar vaderlijck bewijs in plaatze en tot voldoening van d
2 CONC e legitime protie haarlieden na regten competeerende, haar voor soo veel daarinne [naeepe] institueerenen de bij deesen. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Verders heeft hij testateur nog gelegateert aan sijne praesente vrouws voorsoon Jacobus mede gen[aam]t Steijns een somme van geliucke drei hondert guldens alle caapze valuatie.
2 CONT
2 CONT that is - 
2 CONT
2 CONT his wife Maria Lozee
2 CONT
2 CONT his son Aage Steijns by a previous wife (voorsoon) 
2 CONT
2 CONT the son of his wife, Jacobus Steijns, presumably by another man (voorsoon) 
2 CONT
2 CONT his daughter by his present wife (specifically stated), Anna
2 CONT
2 CONT Almost certainly this means that he had no other living heirs at that time - Roman Dutch law did not permit a parent to omit any of his or her children from inheriting - we can therefore, barring other evidence to the contrary, as
2 CONC sume that at the time he made his will his only children were Aage and Anna (and possibly also Jacobus, though it seems very odd that he did not name him as one of his children if he was indeed the father). 
2 CONT
2 CONT In DeVilliers / Pama, Hermanus Steyn (see above) is assumed to have been a child of Jacobus, as is Maria (also a Paulus) - no source or reasons given.
2 CONT
2 CONT Chris Steyn adds: In Die Families van Ou Swellendam Deel I STEYN, there is a list of the children of DGS on page 2. Maria is not mentioned as a child of DGS.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
