1 OCCU Farmer & Member of Heemraad of Swellendam 
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *FATHER OF [https://www.geni.com/people/Hermanus-Steyn/5085290053380026129?through=4502642009600079382 PRESIDENT HERMANUS STEYN]
2 CONT
2 CONT *GREAT GRANDFATHER OF [https://www.geni.com/people/State-President-Hans-Grobler/6000000014070911972 STATE PRESIDENT HANS GROBLER]
2 CONT
2 CONT *2ND GREAT GRANDFATHER OF [https://www.geni.com/people/State-President-Paul-Kruger/6000000002215586290 STATE PRESIDENT PAUL KRUGER]
2 CONT
2 CONT *3RD GREAT GRANDFATHER OF [https://www.geni.com/people/President-Marthinus-Theunis-Steyn/6000000005391318240 STATE PRESIDENT M.T. STEYN]
2 CONT
2 CONT *3RD GREAT GRANDFATHER OF [https://www.geni.com/people/Cornelius-Wessels/6000000027092011860 SIR CORNELIUS HERMANUS WESSELS]
2 CONT
2 CONT *3RD GREAT GRANDFATHER OF [https://www.geni.com/people/Sarel-Eloff/6000000014327600109 KMDT-GENL. SAREL JOHANNES ELOFF]
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------
2 CONT
2 CONT Hermanus d'Oude was the father of President Hermanus Steyn (Hermanus d'Jonge) of the Swellendamse Republiek. He was also the 2nd Great Grandfather of President Paul Kruger, as well as the 3rd Great Grandfather of President M.T. St
2 CONC eyn. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Married Petronella Kemp 1731 in Cape Town. She died after the birth of their third child in 1735
2 CONT
2 CONT 1733 Briefly owned a small property at Zoutrivier
2 CONT
2 CONT Married Martha Potgieter 26 April 1739. She was the daughter of Hans Jurgen Potgieter who died in 1737 and who was the owner of Bruintjiesrivier and 't Voorhuys. Martha and Hermanus had 13 children together.
2 CONT
2 CONT Was a farmer in the Drakenstein district near Paarl for a while; then they moved to the Swellendam district
2 CONT
2 CONT Rented two farms: 't Voorhuis and Bruintjes. Bruintjes was at the Breede river - he made brandy there and he cultivated grain from 1743.
2 CONT
2 CONT ­1743.02.03 word eienaar van die leenplaas ``de Bruintjies Rivier over de Berg'', later Bruintjiesrivier. Die naam is ontleen aan een van hul ou perde met die naam 'Bruintjie' - source http://members.aol.com/kmeintjes/Genealogy/FW
2 CONC deKlerk.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT 1746: became a member of the heemraad of Swellendam. He became a prominent member of society there and was repeatedly elected as member in the course of the next forty years.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1760: bought the farm Combuys at the Cango river.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1762/3: bought the farm 't Voorhuys at the Breede river - made brandy there too.
2 CONT
2 CONT Later on he was known as Hermanus d'Oude to distinguish him from his son, Hermanus d'Jonge. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Key figure in the rebellion in Swellendam in 1795 who declared the independent Republic of Swellendam at the time.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hermanus d'Oude and Martha left the following farms in the Swellendam disctrict to their sons in the testament dated c. 1790:
2 CONT
2 CONT - Bruintjiesfontein on the Klip river with blacksmith's shop
2 CONT
2 CONT - Bruintjiesrivier on the Breede river with vessels and two brandy kettles (farmed here from 1743 with grain)
2 CONT
2 CONT - 't Voorhuis on the Breede river with vessels and brandy kettle etc (first rented it, then he became the owner in 1762)
2 CONT
2 CONT Hermanus died in 1795 
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1999, the Voorhuis farm is still owned by the Steyn family after nine generations. His son Petrus Paulus became the sole owner. The old farm house was destroyed by fire in abt 1914. Douw Steyn (1845-1926) did some repairs to th
2 CONC e ruins and used it as an ironsmith workshop. The wine cellar remained until the nineteen thirties when it was destroyed.   
2 CONT
2 CONT SOURCE: Die families van Ou Swellendam Deel 1 Steyn
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://www.graves-at-eggsa.org/main.php?g2_itemId=886734 Grave]
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT On 3 Feb 1743 Hermanus became the owner of the loan farm "De Bruintjies Rivier over de Berg". The name is derived from one of their old horses with the name of Bruintjies. (See article in Huisgenoot - "Die Man Van Bruintjesrivier"
2 CONC ). Hermanus was the father of President Hermanus Steyn of the Swellendamse Republiek. He was also the 2nd Great Grand Father of President Paul Kruger, as well as the Great Granduncle of President M T Steyn. 
2 CONT
