1 OCCU Farmer at Grootvadersbosch, dist. Swellendam, 'heemraad' and 'ritmeester'
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Profession: Farmer/Boer Grootvadersbosch
2 CONT
2 CONT Also served as heemraad, ritmeester (cavalry captain), burger (citizen) van Swellendam
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: Die families van Ou Swellendam Deel 1: Steyn
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT From 1765-1770 Jacobus Steyn had a farmhand on loan: Johann Eckart Barumessel. Braumessel worked on Grootvadersbosch and also gave music lessons to the children of the landdrost of Swellendam, Friedrich Mentz. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1791 Joachim Christoph Anton Schultze was schoolmaster in service of Jacobus Steyn at Grootvadersbosch in the district of Swellendam.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source of information in this section: Personalia of the Germans at the Cape, 1652=1806 by Dr J Hoge
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Other places mentioned in relation to his descendents are: Bantjiesrivier (Bruintjiesrivier?), Potjieskraal, Kliprivier and Swellendam Drostdy. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Jacobus had 13 kids
