1 NOTE {geni:about_me} PLEASE NOTE: Her surname  was '''never Potgieter  after marriage''' .
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Parentage issues:''' 
2 CONT Although Cornelia Botha's baptism register records her father as Jan Cornelisz, '''this might be incorrec!t'''.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Her biological father could have been any of 3 men''':
2 CONT  Jan Cornelisz; Ferdinandus  Appel; or Frederick Botha 1653-1717 but we do not know ( '''no definite  proof''' ) and her biological mother was Maria Kickers who was '''having a longstanding affair with Frederick Botha and Ferdinan
2 CONC dus  Appel while still married to Jan Cornelisz.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Her mother testified  that all her children were the children of F Both :  however DNA tests have now proven that statement not to be true. Thereby nullifying her statement. 
2 CONT
2 CONT "Unfortunately the paternity of Maria's three daughters during her marriage with Jan will never be known. For her four sons however, we can use the non-recombining part of the Ychromosome region to test if her sons descend from th
2 CONC e same patriline [1,2]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Of course, this will only be true if adulterous relationships in later generations did not result in a mismatch of haplotypes.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Fortunately, the Afrikaner population has an extremely low non-paternity rate of 0.8% [11] which means that direct male descendants will have a high probability of sharing the same Y-chromosome haplotype, even 10 generations late
2 CONC r (92% chance = (1-0.008)10). @
2 CONT
2 CONT Maria Kickers and Jan Cornelisz divorced in 1700.
2 CONT
2 CONT Please do not alter this posting.
2 CONT Please also refer to "The First Fifty Years" project compiled by Delia Robertson which documents the events of Frederick Botha, Maria Kickers and Ferdinandus Appel.
2 CONT No one not even Maria  Kickers knows  who her real father was.
2 CONT
2 CONT  https://www.e-family.co.za/ffy/g5/p5112.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT ===============
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Please note a woman did not assume  the surname of her husband  before 1806 at The Cape of Good Hope==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''See SA naming conventions"'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Legal married names must be recorded in the Last Name field.
2 CONT Before the 1800 government change in SA, married females from the continent (France, Holland, Germany) are unlikely to have used their husband’s surnames, so this field may be left open if they died before 1800.However, British re
2 CONC cords most often show a woman's married name after 1600 (and as early as 1200). Mike Stangel has asked us to represent the documentation possibilities accurately. So do not delete any SA married names after 1800 in order to replac
2 CONC e them with Maiden Names (And do not delete British Married names after 1600, unless you know for a fact that the woman did not assume her husband’s surname). Just set your Viewing Preferences in order not to view the Married Name
2 CONC / Last Name field / Surname, if you don't wish to see them
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT She remained  Botha  after marriage!
2 CONT
