1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Gregorius Jonson Huk=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Son of Jon Halkjellson and Princess Margrethe Haraldsdatter Gille 
2 CONT
2 CONT *Lendmann Gregorius Jonson of Blind Heims Ætta in Sunnmøre. Gregorius was the son of Lendmann Jon Hallkellson, who was married to Margreta, Dotter to Harald Gille. Andres arrived in great vein with Skule Bårdson, co-brother of Ing
2 CONC e Bårdson, after his brother Philippus Bagler Royal fall from 1217, and Skule was eared after him. Foster brother Arnbjørn Jonson was a member of King Håkon Håkonson, and was one of the foremost and most trusted loaves and his arm
2 CONC ies. However, Andres took the most tenest of Arnbjørn, and was badly wounded in the battle against the slit tongues of Tunsberg in February 1218, and was soon to linger. Before he did, he sent a letter of membership with a riddle 
2 CONC to Skule Earl. The zone of Andres and Gudrun entered Gregorius Andreson the elder. He was an heir to the Stårheimsgodset, after Nicholas Arneson, and was a wrapping and governor under King Håkon Håkonson (1217-1263).
2 CONT
2 CONT =Married=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married to '''Margreta''', Dotter of King  Harald Gille
2 CONT
2 CONT =Biography=
2 CONT
2 CONT Gregorius was of the Blindheim family from Sunnmøre, and was a supporter of Skule Bårdsson.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT His parents were Jon Hallkellson and Margreta Haraldsdatter, daughter of Harald Gille.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the father of Gudrun Gregoriusdatter who married Andres Simonson after he returned from Denmark in 1208.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Gregorius drowned in a capsizing south of Bergen in 1228.
2 CONT
2 CONT
