2 CONT '''This Thorfinn is the same as https://www.geni.com/people/Thorfnn-The-Black-Sigurdsson-Orkenoyene/6000000059316432961.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==brief biography==
2 CONT Thorfinn (1009?–-c1064?), called Thorfinn the Mighty, was Earl of Orkney. Son of Earl Sigurd Hlodvirsson by his marriage to the daughter of Malcolm II of Scotland. He married Ingibiorg Finnsdottir, daughter of Finn Arnesson, Jarl 
2 CONC of Halland.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Heimskringla of Icelandic historian Snorri Sturluson, and the anonymous compiler of the Orkneyinga Saga, write that Thorfinn was the most powerful of all the earls of Orkney. He is said to have been earl for seventy-five years
2 CONC  and ruler of nine earldoms in Scotland, of the Hebrides, and of part of Ireland. A sizable part of the account in the Orkneyinga Saga concerns his wars with a "King of Scots" named Karl Hundason whose identity is very uncertain.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==links==
2 CONT * https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thorfinn_Sigurdsson
2 CONT * https://www.familysearch.org/tree/person/details/KFPX-KY8
2 CONT ==content to clean up==
2 CONT Thorfinn was certainly out of the picture by 1066, perhaps even before 1057. When and under what circumstances he died is unknown, suggesting illness rather than anything more dramatic.
2 CONT
