2 CONT
2 CONT Possibly a twin, as he and his brother were joint rulers and always mentioned together.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paul_and_Erlend_Thorfinnsson
2 CONT
2 CONT __________
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://www.geni.com/people/Erland-Thorfinsson-Jarl-of-Orkney-and-Caithness/6000000003646023907?through=6000000001052011900 ERLEND] Thorfinnsson (-in prison Trondheim [Nidaros] 1098, bur Trondheim).  Orkneyinga Saga names “Paul an
2 CONC d…Erlend” as the two sons of Jarl [http://www.geni.com/people/Thorfinn-Sigurdsson/6000000001052002306 THORFINN II]  and his wife [http://www.geni.com/people/Ingibj%C3%B6rg-Finnsd%C3%B3ttir/6000000001052011900 Ingibjörg] who surviv
2 CONC ed childhood[902].  He succeeded his father in [1065] as Joint Jarl of Orkney, jointly with his brother.  Morkinskinna records that Harald III King of Norway sailed to Orkney en route for his invasion of England in 1066 and “recru
2 CONC ited the aid of Jarl Thorfinn´s sons Páll and Erlendr”[903].  Orkneyinga Saga records that Magnus "Barelegs" King of Norway “seized the Earls, Paul and Erlend” on his arrival in Orkney, “sent them east to Norway, and made his own 
2 CONC son Sigurd overlord of the islands with regents to govern the earldom”, adding in a later passage that Erlend “had died and been buried at Trondheim”[904].  He was deposed and imprisoned in 1098 by [http://www.geni.com/people/Magn
2 CONC us-III-Olavsson-%C2%ABBarefoot%C2%BB-Berrf%C3%B8tt/5381202464070053447  Magnus "Barelegs]" King of Norway, and "died of sickness at Nidaros and is buried there" according to Snorre[905].  [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SCOTTISH%
2 CONC 20NOBILITY.htm#_Toc268450047 (Cawley's Medlands)]
2 CONT
2 CONT m [http://www.geni.com/people/Thora-Sumarlidsdatter-Sida/6000000006589075249?through=6000000003646023907 THORA], daughter of [http://www.geni.com/people/Sumarlid-Ospaksson-Sida/6000000003646023917?through=6000000006589075249 SOMER
2 CONC LED]  Uspaksson & his wife ---.  Orkneyinga Saga records that “Earl Erlend Thorfinnson” married “Thora, the daughter of Sumarlidi Ospaksson”, adding that “the mother of this [http://www.geni.com/people/Ospak-Thordisson-Sida/600000
2 CONC 0015745571381?through=6000000003646023917 Ospak] was [http://www.geni.com/people/Thordis-Hallsdottir-Sida/6000000015746208028?through=6000000015745571381 Thordis], daughter of Hall of Sida”[906].  She married secondly [http://www.
2 CONC geni.com/people/Sigurd/6000000017405673361 Sigurd of Paplay].  Orkneyinga Saga records that “his mother was married…to a man called Sigurd” when her son Magnus returned to Orkney, adding that she and her second husband had a son “
2 CONC [http://www.geni.com/people/Hakon-Karl/6000000017405867140?through=6000000017405673361  Hakon Karl]…[and] a farm at Paplay”[907]. [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SCOTTISH%20NOBILITY.htm#_Toc268450047 (Cawley's Medlands)] 
2 CONT
2 CONT Erlend & his wife had four children:  [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SCOTTISH%20NOBILITY.htm#_Toc268450047 (Cawley's Medlands)]
2 CONT
2 CONT a)         [http://www.geni.com/people/Erling-of-Orkneys/6000000003820968908 ERLING] (-[Ulster [May] 1103]).  Orkneyinga Saga names “Erling and Magnus” as the two sons of “Earl Erlend Thorfinnson” and his wife “Thora, the daughter
2 CONC  of Sumarlidi Ospaksson”[908].  Jarl of Orkney.  Orkneyinga Saga states that “according to some people, Erling, the son of Earl Erlend, was killed in the battle of the Menai Straits, but Snorri Sturluson says that he met his death
2 CONC  with King Magnus in Ulster”[909].  [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SCOTTISH%20NOBILITY.htm#_Toc268450047 (Cawley's Medlands)]
2 CONT
2 CONT b)         [http://www.geni.com/people/St-Magnus-Erlendsson/6000000008248157090 St MAGNUS] Erlendsson (-murdered Egilsay 16 Apr [1117], bur Christchurch at Birsay, transferred to Kirkwall Cathedral).  Orkneyinga Saga names “Erling
2 CONC  and Magnus” as the two sons of “Earl Erlend Thorfinnson” and his wife “Thora, the daughter of Sumarlidi Ospaksson”[910].  He was installed as Jarl of ½ Orkney in Spring 1108 by Eistein I Magnusson Joint King of Norway.  Orkneying
2 CONC a Saga records that “Earl Magnus” was killed on the orders of his cousin Hakon “two days after St Tiburtius´ Mass…1091”, after ruling Orkney jointly for seven years, and was buried on “Mainland…at Christ Church”[911].  He was put 
2 CONC to death by his cousin Hakon Paulsson Joint Jarl of Orkney, with whom he had quarrelled.  Canonised.  
2 CONT
2 CONT m ---.  Orkneyinga Saga records that “St Magnus Earl of Orkney” married “a girl from the noblest family there in Scotland” but that they lived together for ten years without consummating the marriage[912].  [http://fmg.ac/Projects
2 CONC /MedLands/SCOTTISH%20NOBILITY.htm#_Toc268450047 (Cawley's Medlands)]
2 CONT
2 CONT c)         [http://www.geni.com/people/Gunhild-Erlendottir/6000000001169154976 GUNHILD].  Orkneyinga Saga names “[http://www.geni.com/people/Gunhild-Erlendottir/6000000001169154976  Gunnhild] and [http://www.geni.com/people/Cecili
2 CONC a-Erlendsdatter/6000000008177258360 Cecilia]” as the two daughters of “Earl Erlend Thorfinnson” and his wife “Thora, the daughter of Sumarlidi Ospaksson”[913].  Orkneyinga Saga records that [http://www.geni.com/people/Magnus-III-O
2 CONC lavsson-%C2%ABBarefoot%C2%BB-Berrf%C3%B8tt/5381202464070053447 Magnus "Barelegs"] King of Norway “gave Earl Erlend´s daughter Gunnhild in marriage to [http://www.geni.com/people/Kol-Kali-Lalisson/6000000001169130795?through=600000
2 CONC 0001169154976  Kol], son of [http://www.geni.com/people/Kali-S%C3%A6bj%C3%B8rnson/6000000003820968938?through=6000000001169130795  Kali Sæbjarnarson], in compensation for the death of his father”, adding that her dowry was “some p
2 CONC roperty in Orkney including a farm at Paplay” and that the couple “settled down on his estate at Agder”[914].  
2 CONT
2 CONT m (Spring 1099) [http://www.geni.com/people/Kol-Kali-Lalisson/6000000001169130795?through=6000000001169154976  KOL] Kalisson, son of [http://www.geni.com/people/Kali-S%C3%A6bj%C3%B8rnson/6000000003820968938?through=600000000116913
2 CONC 0795  KALI] of Agdir in Norway & his wife ---.  Lenderman in Agder.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Kol & his wife had two children:  [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SCOTTISH%20NOBILITY.htm#_Toc268450047 (Cawley's Medlands)]
2 CONT
2 CONT i)          [http://www.geni.com/people/Kali-Agder/6000000003820968970?through=6000000001169130795  KALI] [Rognvald] ([1100]-murdered Force, Calder, Caithness 20 Aug 1158, bur St Magnus Cathedral).  
2 CONT
2 CONT m ---.  The name of Kali-Rognvald´s wife is not known.  Kali-Rognvald & his wife had one child:  
2 CONT
2 CONT (a)       [http://www.geni.com/people/Ingirid-R%C3%B6gnvaldsd%C3%B3ttir/6000000003820968980 INGIGERD]
2 CONT
2 CONT m (Sutherland Spring 1156) [http://www.geni.com/people/Eric-Slagbrellir/6000000003820968990?through=6000000003820968980 ERIK] Slagbrellir, son of [http://www.geni.com/people/Edmund-de-VINGULMARK-de-SU%C3%88DE/6000000000571756282?t
