2 CONT = Ingibjörg, daughter of Hacon, earl of Orkney, and sister of Harold=
2 CONT
2 CONT Ingibjörg, daughter of Hacon, earl of Orkney, and sister of Harold, earl of Orkney, as well as Margaret, wife of Madadh, earl of Atholl. Orkney Saga explicitly states that Ingibjorg was married to King Olav, and it is certainly no
2 CONC t assumed that a lady of such well-known births and connections should humiliate herself to become a concubine even of a king. Ingibjörg, however, who was born after the death of King Magnus and the establishment of her father in 
2 CONC the Orkney Islands, ie about 1105-1110, may not have been married until about 1125, while the marriage of King Olav with Afreca of Galloway no doubt took place shortly after the accession by OLAF to the throne. (Chronicle of Man a
2 CONC nd Sudreys, Munch)
2 CONT Bar
