1 NOTE {geni:about_me} = NN Karlsdotter (Stjärnbjälke)=
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT * Ingrid Karlsdotter was the 3rd daughter of Karl Dansson (Stjärnbjälke) and Ingeborg Magnusdotter of the illegitimate branch of the Folkunga dynasty. 
2 CONT * Karl Dansson exchanges, with the approval of his wife Ingeborg and her brothers, 9 öresland in Medellenna and Söderlenna to the knight Nils Abjörnsson for a piece of land in Solberga in Teda parish and 2 öresland in Bondakyrklin
2 CONC ge. May 20, 1331. (or. perg., RA 0101)
2 CONT * Information about a letter in which Per Karlsson, Dan Karlsson, Ragvald Nilsson, Gregers Karlsson, Ingrid Karlsdotter and their mother Ingeborg Magnusdotter exchanged inheritance after their father Carl Dansson. One lot fell to 
2 CONC wife Ingrid and wife Ingegerd, "anan Gregers, tridie Daan and 4:de herr Peder". 1358. (Genealogica 41, fol. 173r, RA)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ='''Newly Discovered / Verified: A Third Daughter of Karl Dansson Stiernbielke and Ingeborg Magnusdotter oä Folkunge was married to Ragvald Erengislesson Puke'''=
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Historical Biography & Proof Summary'''
2 CONT
2 CONT This profile represents the third daughter of Karl Dansson (Stjärnbjälke) and Ingeborg Magnusdotter. In older, outdated genealogies (like Elgenstierna/Adelsvapen), her identity was completely missing or erroneously combined with h
2 CONC er sister Ingegärd (Fargalt). Modern medieval source analysis has restored her to her proper place in the tree.
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''The Historical Proof: SDHK-nr: 7288 (1358):''' This "smoking gun" document records a separate land and estate exchange between the widowed Ingeborg Magnusdotter and her son-in-law (måg) Ragvald Erengislesson Puke.
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''SDHK-nr: 7289''' proves that Ingeborg’s other daughters (Ingrid and Ingegärd) were married to Bengt Larsson and Ragvald Nilsson Fargalt, Ragvald Puke must have been married to a third daughter from this exact household to leg
2 CONC ally hold the title of måg.
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Descendants:''' Through this marriage, she is the mother of the squire Peter Ragvaldsson (Bonde) and the grandmother of the famous Swedish Riksråd, Ragvald Petersson Puke.
2 CONT =Genealogical Correction Note:=
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Older trees claim Ragvald Puke was married to Anna Markvardsdotter Görtz. This is completely false. Primary parchment records show that Anna Görtz was actually the wife of his grandson (who was also named Ragvald Puke). This pr
2 CONC ofile firmly connects Ragvald Erengislesson Puke to his true wife from the Stjärnbjälke family.''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT =Married= 
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married  '''Ragvald Erengislesson Puke''' - [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=Ragvald+Erengislesson+Puke&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=1&postid=sdhk_7288&tab=post '''SDHK-nr: 7288,'''] Date: 1358 without da
2 CONC te: Information about a letter in which NN Karlsdotter (Stjärnbjälke) mother Mrs.Ingeborg Magnusdotter oä Folkunge makes an exchange with her son-in-law Ragvald Erengislesson Puke.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Children of Ragvald (Erengislesson) Puke &  NN Karlsdotter (Stjärnbjälke),''' per [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=Ragvald+Erengislesson+Puke&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=1&postid=sdhk_7288&tab=post '''S
2 CONC DHK-nr: 7288,'''] Date: 1358 without date: Information about a letter in which Mrs. Ingeborg Magnusdotter makes an exchange with her son-in-law Ragvald Erengislesson Puke.
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Peter Ragvaldsson Puke,''' He married Catharina Håkansdotter (Stjärnbåt) daughter of Håkan Fadersson (Stjärnbåt) and Ingegerd Nilsdotter (Bielke).
2 CONT *  '''Elin Ragvaldsdotter Puke,''' daughter of Ragvald Erengislesson Puke (Bonde) and NN Karlsdotter (Stjärnbjälke). Gjord Karlsson / Fot County sheriff in Ydre härad, Småland 1397-1411. married (1st) already in 1379 to Elin Ragva
2 CONC ldsdotter Puke. Married (2nd) at the earliest 1400 and at the latest 1406 to Elin Torstensdotter (oxpanna). (Died (was deceased) 1406.) Married (3rd) in 1408 to Elin Jönsdotter. Died at the earliest 1411.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=Ragvald+Erengislesson+Puke&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=1&postid=sdhk_7288&tab=post SDHK-nr: 7288]
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Date: 1358 without date'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Information about a letter in which Mrs. Ingeborg Magnusdotter makes an exchange with her son-in-law Ragvald Erengislesson Puke.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Sources; Late medieval regest/notice: Genealogica 41, fol. 32r; identical in Genealogica 62, both RA'''
2 CONT
2 CONT http://sok.riksarkivet.se/?ValdSortering=DatumStigande&PageSize=20&Sokord=Ragvald&EndastDigitaliserat=False&AvanceradSok=False&page=90&FacettLimits=mcrcWA%3a0&FacettState=undefined%3ac%7c&postid=sdhk_7288&tab=post#tab
2 CONT
2 CONT Ragvald Erengislesson Puke was a 14th-century Swedish esquire (väpnare) belonging to the prominent noble Bonde family. He lived during a turbulent political era in medieval Scandinavia, appearing in historical records between 1345
2 CONC  and 1381, and passed away before March 1393 (likely between 1381 and 1384). He is notable for adopting the surname Puke from his maternal lineage, creating a distinct branch within the noble Bonde clan
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://sok.riksarkivet.se/sdhk/?EndastDigitaliserat=false&SDHK=7289&Innehall=++&TrycktUtgava=true&TrycktRegest=true&Brevtext=true&Extratext=true&Sigill=true&Original=true&MedeltidaAvskrifter=true&MedeltidaRegest=true&Eftermede
2 CONC ltidaAvskrifter=true&EftermedeltidaRegest=true&AvanceradSok=False&page=1&postid=sdhk_7289&tab=post#tab SDHK number: 7289]
2 CONT
2 CONT The Swedish Diplomatarium's main index of medieval letters
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Dating: 1358 without day''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT Information about a letter in which Per Karlsson, Dan Karlsson, Ragvald Nilsson, Gregers Karlsson, Ingrid Karlsdotter and their mother Ingeborg Magnusdotter divided the inheritance after their father Carl Dansson. One lot fell to 
2 CONC wife Ingrid and wife Ingegerd, "another Gregers, third Daan and fourth Mr. Peder".
2 CONT
2 CONT * Sources: Post-medieval regest/notice:  Genealogica 41, fol. 173r, RA
2 CONT
2 CONT Carii Daanson 1341. g(x) : Mrs. Ingeborgh Magnusadotter Carll Månson's sister 1358 widow. (three times gin-stitched shield)”Raguall Nilson [:]Carll Danson calls him(l) magh 1354 and Daan Karlson 1358. DS 5838 b  see pdf of print L
2 CONC iterature and commentary see DS no. 5838 b
2 CONT
