1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Peter Ragvaldsson Puke=
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Son of Ragvald Erengislesson Puke and NN Karlsdotter (Stjärnbjälke). Genealogical Correction Note: Older trees claim Ragvald Puke was married to Anna Markvardsdotter Görtz. This is completely false. Primary parchment records 
2 CONC show that Anna Görtz was actually the wife of his grandson (who was also named Ragvald Puke). This profile firmly connects Ragvald Erengislesson Puke to his true wife from the Stjärnbjälke family.'''
2 CONT * Peter Ragvaldsson pays the debt of his father, Ragvald Eringislasson, to Nydala monastery by ceding to the monastery his ancestral estates "Holmakra and Sigwadzthorp" in Hylletofta parish as well as a chalice, which belonged to 
2 CONC his father. Hjelmseryd's church on 9 March 1393. (or. perg. RA 0101)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=Ragvald+Erengislesson&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=1&postid=sdhk_11796&tab=post SDHK-nr: 11796]
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Dating: 1380 December 27, Place of issue; Bohus'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Ragvald Erengislesson and Peter Ragvaldsson''' announce in an open letter that they pledge to the honest man Abraham Brodersson their entire property Fastarp in the parish of Tvååker in the fiefdom of Varberg with all appurtena
2 CONC nces, including land dwellers and mills, which since ancient times have been under this estate, for 20 merks in right loan. The property can be redeemed by the issuers and their heirs for 20 merks. The issuers seal.
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Sources:''' Original: Orig. on perg. (20.3 x 9.2 cm, fold 1.2 cm; 10 lines), Uppsala University Library Post-medieval transcripts: E 170 no. 19, UUB
2 CONT
2 CONT
