1 NAME Heidenrich VI. 'der Jüngere' /von Plettenberg zu Lenhausen/ Herr zu Lenhausen
2 GIVN Heidenrich VI. 'der Jüngere'
2 NSFX Herr zu Lenhausen
2 _MARNM von Plettenberg zu Lenhausen
1 NAME Heidenrich VI. von Plettenberg zu Lenhausen
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1434
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1481
1 OCCU urk. 1439-1481, 1483 tot, 1457 Herr zu 3/4 Lenhausen, 1474 zu Finnentrop, 1477 zu Oedingen
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} General Notes:
2 CONT
2 CONT FW Schulte: '''The two sons Georg and Heinrich divided up the Lenhausen estate in 1483 as part of an inheritance division.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Events:
2 CONT
2 CONT • Notarized, 1438-1481.
2 CONT
2 CONT • Notarized, 1440-1485.
2 CONT
2 CONT • Notarized, 17 Jul 1469. '''Heydenrich, Herman, Gunterman and Hinrich''', sons of the '''late Hinrich van''' '''Plettenberch,''' declare a dispute about the 5 marks from the tithe to Vailbricht, which were prescribed to their '''
2 CONC grandfather Hinrich van Plettenberch,''' and about the dispute with the Ewich monastery that they had been satisfied by the knight Johan van Haitzvelt and his brother Junker Johan. They deliver their documents to the monastery. Si
2 CONC egel Hermans van Plettenbracht and Goderts Refflinchusen, Gografen zu Attendorn Witnesses: Hinrich Schaner, waiter zu Arnesborch, Evert van den Broke, Engelbert van Plettenberch, Wilhem Vaget. In the sancti Allexii confessoris Not
2 CONC es: Urschr., Pgt., 2 seals attached: 1) Herm. v. Plettenberg; 2) Godert Refflinchusen (like 1463 Febr. 24)
2 CONT
2 CONT -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Plettenberg-Lenhausen line''':
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Heidenreich von Plettenberg, the second son of the aforementioned Heidenreich von Plettenberg zu Bamenohl''' (* around 1450, † 1485), was '''born on the Waldenburg''' and was a '''co-heir to Finnentrop'''. '''In 1457 he acquire
2 CONC d Lenhausen Castle from Heinrich von Lenhausen''', who had remained childless. He married '''Adelheid von Wrede and in 1483 divided his property between his two sons.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT German Wikipedia
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
