2 CONT 1663 = Johannes Lohmann, priest and conventual of the Grafschaft monastery, Hermann Lohmann the younger to Lohof, Thonis Lohmann to Reiste,''' Elsen Baustes to Beisinghausen''', Gertrud Möller'sche zu Fretter, all biological broth
2 CONC ers and sisters, complain for themselves and''' Clara her sister daughter against Ebert Schulte zu Landenbeck''' for insulting. He should be on Sunday, October 4th, 1662, in Baustes house in Beisinghausen in the presence of others
2 CONC  have said that '''his son's wife''' came from the devil; she doesn't want him anything to eat. .... He should withdraw and pay a fine to the tax authorities.(Original paper certificate at the Lohof)
2 CONT
2 CONT '''His son's wife was Clara Lohmann''', who gave. around 1630, + Landenbeck 06/10/1677. Man remember that this utterance has fallen to the witch frenzy at the moment and it is easy to become one Persecution through the (witch) cou
2 CONC rts could come. That's why they complain. Siblings of '''Clara Lohmann'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes Individual note 04.10.1662 = '''The Lohmann siblings from Reiste are suing for themselves and their sister's daughter Clara against Ebert Schulte from Landenbeck''', who is said to have said on October 4th, 1662 during a bre
2 CONC ak at Beisinghausen: His son's wife had come from the devil; she doesn't want to give him anything to "eat". (Original paper certificate at the Lohof). The lawsuit was filed on January
2 CONT
2 CONT 20th, 1663 = at the "Judge vnd Scheffen deß secular court Eßloh vndt Reiste" (original document at the Lohof). The outcome of the trial is unknown.
2 CONT
2 CONT 04.10.1662 = The Lohmann siblings from Reiste are suing for themselves and their sister's daughter Clara against Ebert Schulte from Landenbeck, who is said to have said on October 4th, 1662 during a break at Beisinghausen: His son
2 CONC 's wife had come from the devil; she doesn't want to give him anything to "eat". (Original paper certificate at the Lohof). The lawsuit was filed on January
2 CONT
2 CONT 04.01.1682 = Else Lohmann, widow Baust* (see to 5.) acknowledges the receipt of her child part from Lohof. (Original paper certificate at the Lohof) 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT 07/03/1638 =''' Ebert Schulte zu Landenbeck''' commits himself to good things as liege lord to the Struwen Büemke the interest from both the 5 Rtlr., As well as of the 5 Rtlr. To pay Maria Stoer'sche memorial money, if Struwen sho
2 CONC uld stay behind. He pledged the Wiesenkamp behind the Büemke chapel adjoins Cordes Kamp. Witnesses: Pastor Caspar Berghoff, Hermann Lohmann, Thonies Scheiwe, both lay judges and provisional officers. Signature: Eberdt Schulte to l
2 CONC amb corner. (From a booklet with copies of old documents in the parish archive of Reiste, pages 15-16)
2 CONT
