2 CONC isti der Heiligen der Letzten Tage (Mormonen Kirche). - Collection - 40001 - https://www.myheritage.de/research/collection-40001/familysearch-stammbaum?itemId=463185701&action=showRecord - '''Clara Der Hennemöller (geb. Baust)''' 
2 CONC Geschlecht: weiblich Geburt: 27. Dez. 1649 - Beisinghausen, Nordrhein-Westfalen, GermanyHeirat: 26. Jun. 1674 - Meschede, Kurfürstentum Köln, Niederheinisch-Westfälischer Reichskreis, GermanyTod: ca. 1680. Ehemann: Julius Der Henn
2 CONC emöller. Kinder: Peter Möller, Pn Möller, Hilgerus-Hillegard Jodocus Muller-Möller
2 CONT
2 CONT '''MyHeritage Family Trees'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Clara Möller (born Baust), 1649 - 1680''' Clara Möller (born Baust) was born on month day 1649, at birth place, to '''Hermann Schelmann gt.Baust and Elsen Schellmann(born Lohmann).''' Clara married '''Julius der Hennemöller.'''
2 CONC  Julius was born in 1645, in Meschede, Hochsauerlandkreis, Nordrhein-Westfalen, Germany. They had 3 children: Hillegard Jodocus (Hilgerus) Möller(Müller) and 2 other children. Clara passed away in 1680, at age 30
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT July 8th, 1667 = Röttger Stirnberg and Catharina Balthes zu Reiste, married couple, declare that they will bequeath their Balthes dwelling with living and dead inventory to the honorable and virtuous Elisabeth Fredebolinges for ma
2 CONC ny years of faithful service. They ask Hermann and Toniesen Lomann, father and son, Everhardt Schulte zu Landenbeck, the judge zu Eslohe and Reiste Jacob Scheffer to sign and seal the letter of purchase. Signatures: Jacobus Scheff
2 CONC er, Caspar (Stirnberg gt.) Baltz, for me and my housewives, Hermann Lomann, magistrate, Ebert Schulte (from Landenbeck), I confess Tonies Lohmann to me and Catrina my married housewife that this is true. (Original certificate at t
2 CONC he Lohof)
2 CONT
2 CONT -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT 26.08.1658 = The brothers Eberhard, Jost and Caspar Frisse von Reiste confess that they '''Hermann Lohmann, electoral court clerk in Eslohe''', their parents' home to traveled with all countries, etc., for a sum of money which the
2 CONC  Buyers have to pay their parents and forefathers, creditors, on themselves. You ask to seal the letter to the electoral judge in Eslohe. Signatures: Jacob Schefer (from Grevenstein), electoral judge at Eslohe, Ebert Schulte zu La
2 CONC ndenbeck, Hermann Lohmann, court assistant. (Original parchment certificate from Kanter-Frisse zu Reiste) NB 1659, Thonies Lohmann, the son of Hermann Lohmann, married Frissen-Hof zu Traveled.
2 CONT
2 CONT -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT 04.10.1662 = The Lohmann siblings from Reiste are suing for themselves and their sister's daughter Clara against Ebert Schulte from Landenbeck, who is said to have said on October 4th, 1662 during a break at Beisinghausen: His son
2 CONC 's wife had come from the devil; she doesn't want to give him anything to "eat". (Original paper certificate at the Lohof). The lawsuit was filed on January 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://translate.googleusercontent.com/translate_c?depth=3&hl=en&prev=search&rurl=translate.google.com&sl=de&sp=nmt4&u=https:%2F%2Fgw.geneanet.org%2Fgoed%3Flang%3Dde%26pz%3Dandreas%2Bhagen%2Bandreas%26nz%3Dgodde%26p%3Djodocus%2Bj
2 CONC ost%26n%3Dlohmann&usg=ALkJrhiHR7wjivWBu4mIYyABFbbdBckPiw 
2 CONT
2 CONT 07/03/1638 = Ebert Schulte zu Landenbeck commits himself to good things as liege lord to the Struwen Büemke the interest from both the 5 Rtlr., As well as of the 5 Rtlr. To pay Maria Stoer'sche memorial money, if Struwen should st
2 CONC ay behind. He pledged the Wiesenkamp behind the Büemke chapel adjoins Cordes Kamp. Witnesses: Pastor Caspar Berghoff, Hermann Lohmann, Thonies Scheiwe, both lay judges and provisional officers. Signature: Eberdt Schulte to lamb co
2 CONC rner. (From a booklet with copies of old documents in the parish archive of Reiste, pages 15-16)
2 CONT
2 CONT https://translate.googleusercontent.com/translate_c?depth=3&hl=en&prev=search&rurl=translate.google.com&sl=de&sp=nmt4&u=https:%2F%2Fgw.geneanet.org%2Fgoed%3Flang%3Dde%26pz%3Dandreas%2Bhagen%2Bandreas%26nz%3Dgodde%26p%3Djodocus%2Bj
2 CONC ost%26n%3Dlohmann&usg=ALkJrhiHR7wjivWBu4mIYyABFbbdBckPiw 
2 CONT
2 CONT 23.10.1469 = Diederich Bleffken and Catharina sell his housewife a piece of land on the Reister Berge - tüschen den Loheholtern - 8 to 9 bushels in size, to Hannes to dem Lohe and Aleke his housewife. You ask Werner Seytveldt to s
2 CONC eal the letter. Witnesses: Diderich Schulte zu Landenbeck, Hans Schulte zu Reiste and Hans Schmendemul, Schulte zu Fredeboling. (Copy of the document in the Reiste parish archive. The original document is no longer available)
2 CONT
2 CONT July 8th, 1667 = Röttger Stirnberg and Catharina Balthes zu Reiste, married couple, declare that they will bequeath their Balthes dwelling with living and dead inventory to the honorable and virtuous Elisabeth Fredebolinges for ma
2 CONC ny years of faithful service. They ask Hermann and Toniesen Lomann, father and son, Everhardt Schulte zu Landenbeck, the judge zu Eslohe and Reiste Jacob Scheffer to sign and seal the letter of purchase. Signatures: Jacobus Scheff
2 CONC er, Caspar (Stirnberg gt.) Baltz, for me and my housewives, Hermann Lomann, magistrate, Ebert Schulte (from Landenbeck), I confess Tonies Lohmann to me and Catrina my married housewife that this is true. (Original certificate at t
2 CONC he Lohof)
2 CONT
2 CONT 01/20/1663 = at the "Herr Richter vnd Scheffen of the secular court Eßloh vndt Reiste" (original document at the Lohof). The outcome of the trial is unknown.
2 CONT
2 CONT 04.01.1682 = Else Lohmann, widow of Baust (see to 5.) acknowledges the receipt of her child part from the Lohof. (Original paper certificate at the Lohof)
2 CONT
2 CONT 02/10/1684 = Diederich Schelman (a relative of Hermann Schelmann gt. Baust, to ad 5.) makes his will. In it he bequeathed some amounts to Johannes "Boist zu Bösinghausen" (document in the Reiste parish archive)
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT 04.04.1689 = Johannes Baust zu Beisinghausen signs a certificate in which Johann Wefer and Ennecke announce to his housewife that they have sold Diederich Cordes gt. Frisse zu Reiste and Margarethe his housewife a piece of land at
2 CONC  the house shop. (Original certificate from Kenter-Frisse zu Reiste)k
2 CONT
