2 CONT BIOGRAPHY Freiherr Johann Sigismund von Heiden, 1656-1730. Having started his career as an officer in the Prussian army, he became adjutant-general to the Count of Nassau as well as serving under the Elector of Brandenburg from 16
2 CONC 91 till 1716. He obtained the rank of general of the cavalry and became governor of the city of Wesel.
