1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * '''Baptism:'''https://www.eggsa.org/sarecords/index.php/church-registers/cape-town-ngk-1665-to-1695/56-cape-town-baptisms-1686
2 CONT Cape Town Baptisms 1686 -Written by transcribed by Richard Ball and Corney Keller. Posted in Cape Town Baptisms 1665-1695.
2 CONT (page 30 continued)
2 CONT '''Note:''' as far as I can see above - this is rather the '''baptism of Theunis  (with dna as an Appel''') 
2 CONT Den 15 dito (April)
2 CONT '''Theunis
2 CONT Jan Cornelis van Outbeierlant and  Maria Kicker[t]s'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''PATERNITY ISSUES:'''
2 CONT * Frederich Both was his Step-father''' not''' his biological dna father  
2 CONT * '''Jan Cornlisz was NOT his  biological father' as stated on the baptism''.  
2 CONT *  Ferdinandus '''Appel was his biological dna father'''!  
2 CONT
2 CONT * His '''biological dna shows his father was Ferdinandus Appel''' - according to University of Pretoria's dna testing. [http://repository.up.ac.za/bitstream/handle/2263/32007/Greeff_Appel(2013).pdf?sequence=1 study  by  the Univer
2 CONC sity of Pretoria] 
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Kindly see dna test result's summary:''' WB
2 CONT A University of Pretoria genetics study (Jaco M. Greeff & J. Christoff Erasmus) used''' Y-chromosome STR testing''' on living male-line descendants and found that Maria Kickers’ first son (Theunis) was most probably fathered by ''
2 CONC 'Ferdinandus Appel, while her remaining three sons were likely fathered by Frederik (Friedrich) Botha—not by her husband, Jan Cornelitz.''' 
2 CONT UPSpace Repository
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Method: 17-marker Y-STR haplotyping with the AmpFlSTR® Yfiler™ kit; samples included random Botha males, patrilineal descendants of each of Maria’s four sons, and Appel male-line descendants. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The Theunis-line haplotype matched an Appel male-line haplotype, supporting Appel’s paternity for the first son; the other three sons shared a second haplotype consistent with a single father (presumably Botha). 
2 CONT '''UPSpace Repository
2 CONT
2 CONT Implication: because '''Theunis''' left many male descendants, the authors estimate that roughly half of living “Botha” men (≈38,000 people) actually '''carry the Appel Y-chromosome'''—a striking non-paternity event early in the l
2 CONC ineage. (That figure is an inference from the sample and census data, not a head-count of every Botha.)
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT '''
2 CONT {{https://www.geni.com/media/proxy?media_id=6000000221120485985&size=large}}
2 CONT
2 CONT {{https://www.geni.com/media/proxy?media_id=6000000221121053824&size=large}}
2 CONT [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000123663725823 ''''Appel Botha Cornelitz : the abc of a three hundred year old divorce case'.''' Jaco M. Greeff & J. Christoff Erasmus Department of Genetics, University of Pretoria
2 CONC , Pretoria 0002, South Africa.]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT * Although Friedrich Both is shown here '''as his adoptive father he is only his ''de facto'' father.''' Geni's functionality to differentiate between biological and adoptive/foster is utilised here to show his relationship to his
2 CONC  biolocical and de facto parents
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Theunis Botha''', b bef 15 April 1686. Called Botha after his mother, [http://www.geni.com/people/Maria-Kickers/4705796237050024653?through=6000000005788458301 Maria Kickers]' , 1700 divorce from [http://www.geni.com/people/J
2 CONC an-Cornelisz/4141861275630023780?through=4705796237050024653 Jan Cornelisz] '''(who is shown as his father on the birth certificate'''). 
2 CONT
2 CONT At which time  she said  - her 7 children were [http://www.geni.com/people/Friedrich-Botha-SV-PROG/5356428241620125193?through=4705796237050024653 Frederich Botha]'s.
2 CONT
2 CONT However, a recent DNA   [http://repository.up.ac.za/bitstream/handle/2263/32007/Greeff_Appel(2013).pdf?sequence=1 study  by  the University of Pretoria]  '''reveal him to have been the biological son of [http://www.geni.com/people
2 CONC /Ferdinandus-Appel-b2/6000000001580940776?through=6000000005788458301 Ferdinandus Appel].''''''
2 CONT
2 CONT * In1735 Will - Botha, Theunis & Maria Catharin van Eeden - 1735, Heemraad and Captain of the burger commando. Theunis Bota, from the Cape of Good Hope (Cape Archives, MOOC 7/1/7, 8 ;dated 16th July 1735, filed 26 July 1746)
2 CONT
2 CONT *1739, Maandag 31 Augustus: They depart from captain Botha's homestead with one party.(Resolutions of the Council of Policy of the Cape ofof men and wagons to Jan Celliers where tents were erected. Good Hope, http://www.tanap.net/
2 CONC content/activities/resolutions_CapeOfGoodHope/, Cape Archives C. 112, pp. 3-33, Saturdag den 31 October 1739)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT -----------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT * http://www.beeld.com/bylae/2013-08-16-die-appel-wat-onder-die-botha-boom-geval-het
2 CONT
2 CONT * Onder andere:
2 CONT ‘'''Onbeqwaamd’ in die bed Die meeste mense is onbewus van die Botha-familie se kleurryke ontstaan. In die eerste 17 jaar van die Cornelitz-huwelik skenk Maria geboorte aan sewe kinders en van almal buiten een is die doop-inskrywi
2 CONC ng bewaar. 
2 CONT
2 CONT * In al ses die inskrywings word '''Jan Cornelitz as pa''' van die kinders aangegee.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Tuis was alles egter nie pluis nie.''' '''In Mei '''1689 getuig twee vroue voor die hof''' Maria het hulle vertel Frederik Botha''' is eintlik haar '''tweede kind''' se pa.
2 CONT
2 CONT Frederik het saam met Maria se man om ’n deel geboer en die saak was waarskynlik ’n poging om Maria in toom te probeer hou. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Die vroue het ook gesê '''Maria het hulle vertel haar eerste kind, Theunis, is eintlik Ferdinandus Appel s’n. 
2 CONT '''
2 CONT Ten tyde van die vermeende owerspel was Ferdinandus Appel ’n ongetroude man van 20. Maar in 1700 spat die vonke rêrig toe Jan om ’n egskeiding vra.
2 CONT
2 CONT  '''Voor die hof het Jan Cornelitz beweer Frederik Botha is die vader van ál Maria se kinders''' en dat hy swak in sy eie huis behandel is. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Maria het nie die beweerde vaderskap van haar kinders ontken nie, maar gesê Jan was “onbeqwaamd” en hy het haar selfs aangemoedig'''. (sic)
2 CONT
