1 OCCU Farmer at Doornkraal, dist. Riversdale
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} A Historic Overview of Langstraat, Riversdale - thanks to prof Pieter Gerbrand Steyn who is the current owner of Langstraat (2016).
2 CONT
2 CONT The farm Doornkraal was proclaimed a loan farm in 1746, the same year as Zeekoegat. The original owner of the farm Doornkraal on which Riversdale was established, was Hermanus Egbertus Steyn, born in 1773. He was the brother of Do
2 CONC uw Gerbrand Steyn of the farm Cloetenburg in the Stellenbosch district, where Somerset West was later established.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hermanus Egbertus Steyn’s daughter Susanna Maria married his brother Douw Gerbrand’s son Hermanus Jacobus in 1815. In this way Hermanus Jacobus aquired the portion of the farm Doornkraal that was sold to the “Godsdienstige Gestich
2 CONC t” in 1838 to establish Riversdale. The thatched cottage located at Langstraat 8 was one of the original homesteads of Doornkraal built between 1746 and 1790.
2 CONT
2 CONT The homestead was located next to the current Royal Hotel in what later became Langstraat. It was probably built by Hermanus Jacobus circa 1815 after his marriage to Hermanus Egbertus’ daughter. It was rebuilt in 1849 by Barry and
2 CONC  Nephew as offices, a jail, and later the Standard Bank. Unfortunately it was destroyed by fire as recently as 1959. The homestead served as the first NG church in Riversdale after Hermanus Jacobus Steyn sold a portion of the farm
2 CONC  Doornkraal to the Godsdientige Gesticht in 1838. Riversdale was named after Civil Commisioner Sir Harry Rivers and proclaimed a town on 30 August 1838 with Langstraat as the focal point. It is important to note that the official 
2 CONC name of the town is indeed Riversdale, not Riversdal.
2 CONT
2 CONT The first “Lots” stretched all the way from the current Van Riebeeck Street to the Vette river on the eastern boundary. The “Lots” were bisected by a long road running parallel to the the Vette river, stretching all the way to whe
2 CONC re the golf course is today. Hence the name “Langstraat”, which was the access road to Riversdale from the south-east in the vicinity of the current golf course. The remains of the old “wa-brug” built in the 1800’s are still evide
2 CONC nt where the Vette and Goukou rivers meet.
2 CONT
2 CONT The house known as Avondrust at Langstraat 9 with its Edwardianised façade forms part of the original Lot 4 (1839). Lot 4, which originally included the Doornkraal thatched cottage at Langstraat 8 (until 1880), remained the proper
2 CONC ty of the Doornkraal Steyns from 1838 when Riversdale was established, until 1950 when [https://www.geni.com/people/Susanna-Maria-Steyn-b1c8d12e4f8g1/6000000020856122234 Susanna Maria van der Westhuizen (nee Steyn)] sold it to Han
2 CONC nes (Vark) van Wyk. During the 1920’s and 30’s her mother [https://www.geni.com/people/Anna-Margaretha-Steyn/6000000010857033760 Anna Margaretha (Annie) Steyn (nee Cronje)] operated a boarding house on the premises. One of her boa
2 CONC rders was the [https://www.geni.com/people/Ben-Marais/6000000019867780409 reverend Ben Marais] (later Professor) who together with [https://www.geni.com/people/Christiaan-Frederick-Naud%C3%A9-h4/6000000011411486931 Dr Beyers Naude
2 CONC ] opposed the NG church’s support of apartheid. It is ironic that Annie Steyn’s cousin [https://www.geni.com/people/Geoffrey-Cronj%C3%A9/6000000005104809284 Professor Geoffrey Cronje] became [https://www.geni.com/people/Prime-Mini
2 CONC ster-Hendrik-Verwoerd/6000000011527410721 Dr H F Verwoerd]’s mentor, two decades later.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: http://www.dedoornkraal.com/media.html and http://www.dedoornkraal.com/history-of-dedoornkraal/
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Digital copy of baptismal record https://familysearch.org/pal:/MM9.3.1/TH-267-12577-9516-24?cc=1392488&wc=10831322 image 34
2 CONT
