1 OCCU Soldier then farmer, vir Jan Cornelisz geboer, Farmer, vee boer/ soldaat, Vrijburger, Vryburger, Cabo
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Friedrich Botha / Friedrich Both ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Born:''' 4 March 1653, Wangenheim, near Gotha, Thuringia, Duchy of Saxe-Coburg-Gotha, Germany (50.57°N, 10.41°E)  
2 CONT '''Died:''' Unknown  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Parents:''' Michael Both and Susanna Saulus  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Occupation:''' VOC soldier; bywoner at Jan Cornelisz, later  farmer in Stellenbosch, Burgher Stellenbosch 1685 
2 CONT
2 CONT === Biography ===
2 CONT * Friedrich Botha arrived at the Cape as a VOC soldier in 1678. 
2 CONT * In 1683, five years after his arrival, he gained the right to practice as a farmer, his original profession, and worked for several farmers as a “subfarmer”, or as he put it, his "business" was then "landbouer bij den een en den
2 CONC  ander geweest te sijn" (farmer to one and then another?).
2 CONT * From 1686, he worked for [https://www.geni.com/people/Jan-Cornelisz/4141861275630023780 Jan Cornelisz van Oudbeijerland]  at the Stellenbosch farm (later named Libertas). Here Botha farmed for a quarter of the profits (‘oom voor
2 CONC  een vierde part met hem te zaaijen en te bouwen’) in the earliest example of the French "Métairie" system (tenant farming) being applied in South Africa.
2 CONT * In 1689 he acquired the 64-morgen farm of his own,''Zandberg'', later called ''Scholtzenhof'', originally 64 acres in area. ''Zandberg'' was transferred to his name in 1694. The farmhouse with thatched roof is located on the rig
2 CONC ht side of the road between Stellenbosch and Somerset West – a beautiful location indicated on the map of the area (See loaded images). Today a vineyard known as '[http://www.kenforresterwines.com Ken Forrester Vineyards]' can be 
2 CONC found there. The old homestead was originally a T-shaped building and the front walls are still about a meter thick, probably built by Friedrich Botha himself. The house has beautiful yellow wood ceilings a loft of fire clay a foo
2 CONC t thick above them. The house was later was enlarged to an H-shape and more recently restored by the architect, G. Osler. (See a sketch in the loaded images)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT === Children ===
2 CONT Friedrich Botha lived with [https://www.geni.com/people/Maria-Kickers/4705796237050024653 Maria Kickers] while she was married to Jan Cornelisz van Oud-Beijerland.  
2 CONT
2 CONT * In 1689 Belijtie Fredericks wife of the freeburger Harmen Jansen from Noorthorn (ie. the wife of Harmen Jansz Potgieter) stated under oath that she, the attestator, during the pregnancy of Maria Kickers (now four years in the pa
2 CONC st) from the mouth of the aforesaid Maria Kickers had heard, that the child with which she was pregnant, did not belong to her husband Jan Cornelis but to Frederik Boot, using in essence these words: that she did not belong to all
2 CONC  men, but kept herself to one, and that Frederik Boot was the father of the child with which she was now pregnant and also the father of her first child - 'ende dat van hare eerste kints vader was geweest [.]anen Ferdinandus Appel
2 CONC '.
2 CONT * In similar fashion was declared by Beatrix Gijsberts (wife of Hendrik Cornelisz), that at this same time the 11 August 1685 (it was a Sunday to the attestator's best knowledge) likewise from the aforesaid Maria Kickers to have h
2 CONC eard, that Frederick Boot had known her, and that she from that time on had become pregnant.
2 CONT >>''On today the 13 May 1689 Sworn to before me the undersigned Sibrandus Mancadan secretary to Stellenbosch at the request of Belijtie Fredericks wife of the freeburger Harmen Jansen from Noorthorn dwelling at Stellenbosch, the h
2 CONC onourable Hendrik Cornelis and the honourable Catrijn Cloeten in the presence of the undernamed witnesses admitting and declaring and attesting true and true to be, that she, the attestator, during the pregnancy of Maria Kickers (
2 CONC now four years in the past) from the mouth of the aforesaid Maria Kickers had heard, that the child with which she was pregnant, did not belong to her husband Jan Cornelis but to Frederik Boot, using in essence these words: that s
2 CONC he did not belong to all men, but kept herself to one, and that Frederik Boot was the father of the child with which she was now pregnant, and also the father of her first child was that of Ferdinandus Appel. In similar fashion wa
2 CONC s declared by Beatrix Gijsberts declaring that at this same time the 11 August 1685 (it was a Sunday to the attestator's best knowledge) likewise from the aforesaid Maria Kickers to have heard, that Frederick Boot had known her, a
2 CONC nd that she from that time on had become pregnant''.[Notarial Deeds: Declaration, 12.8.1699]
2 CONT
2 CONT *  In 1699 there was a dispute between Maria and 'Bombam' over a property that had to be worked on by him, that he had not done. She apparently said "Jeij sult doen wat eck hebben wil, ieij zulkt voor mijn door een vuur gaan, en j
2 CONC eij zult mijn de voeten kussen als ek het heben wil" (You will do what I want, you will walk through a fire for me, and you will kiss my feet if I want it." Court testimony records Maria scolding him: "Jeij zult nagt en dach voor 
2 CONC mijn loopen als eck het hebben wil, want ick hou jou minder als een knegt, ja minder als een Hottentot, ja minder als een hont." (You would run for me night and day, if I wanted you to, because I consider you less than a servant, 
2 CONC yes less than a Hottentot, yes less than a dog.") Someone else told the audience that she'd said "dat hij [Oud-Beijerland] onbequaam was om een man voor haar te wesen, en dat haare kinderen di sijne niet en waaren, en dat zij hem 
2 CONC minder agte als een slaaf, of als een hont"  (he [Oud-Beijerland] was unqualified to be a husband for her, and that her children were not his, and that she regarded him  as less than a slave or a dog)      (Biewenga, p. 268). Cour
2 CONC t records show Maria swearing under oath that all children born during her marriage to Jan Cornelisz were fathered by Friedrich Botha due to Jan Cornelisz’s incapacity.  ([CJ 3, 22 Jan 1700]) Maria said her children were conceived
2 CONC  by Botha with her husband’s encouragement (‘haren man haar daar toe selfs aanleijding soude hebben gegeeven’) because he was impotent (‘onbequaamd’).  [However, recent DNA studies by the University of Pretoria prove that while Ma
2 CONC ria was married to Jan Cornelisz, she also had a relationship with Ferdinandus Appel, and Theunis Appel is actually  fathered by him.]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Children declared to be Botha's:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT b1 [https://www.geni.com/people/Theunis-Botha/6000000005788458301 Theunis Botha]  
2 CONT Baptized: 15 Apr 1686  
2 CONT Married: 15 Dec 1710 to [https://www.geni.com/people/Maria-Magdalena-Snyman/6000000000000000001 Maria Magdalena Snyman] (biological father: Ferdinandus Appel)
2 CONT
2 CONT b2 [https://www.geni.com/people/Willem-Botha/6000000005788458302 Willem Botha]  
2 CONT Baptized: 2 Nov 1687  
2 CONT Married: 14 Jul 1709 to [https://www.geni.com/people/Catharina-Pyl/6000000000000000002 Catharina Pyl]
2 CONT
2 CONT b3 [https://www.geni.com/people/Catharina-Botha/6000000005788458303 Catharina Botha]  
2 CONT Baptized: 7 May 1690  
2 CONT Married: 31 Aug 1717 to [https://www.geni.com/people/Hendrik-Frederik-Klopper/6000000000000000003 Hendrik Frederik Klopper]
2 CONT
2 CONT b4 [https://www.geni.com/people/Jacobus-Botha/6000000005788458304 Jacobus Botha]  
2 CONT Baptized: 24 Aug 1692  
2 CONT Married: 22 Oct 1713 to [https://www.geni.com/people/Elsie-Snyman/6000000000000000004 Elsie Snyman]
2 CONT
2 CONT b5 [https://www.geni.com/people/Johannes-Botha/6000000005788458305 Johannes Botha]  
2 CONT Baptized: 1 May 1695  
2 CONT Married: 18 May 1721 to [https://www.geni.com/people/Anna-van-der-Merwe/6000000000000000005 Anna van der Merwe]  
2 CONT Remarried: 15 Mar 1739 to [https://www.geni.com/people/Helena-du-Toit/placeholder Helena du Toit] (widow of Arend Olivier)
2 CONT
2 CONT b6 [https://www.geni.com/people/Maria-Botha/6000000005788458306 Maria Botha]  
2 CONT Baptized: 1 May 1695  
2 CONT Married: 13 Mar 1712 to [https://www.geni.com/people/Coenraad-Scheepers/6000000000000000006 Coenraad Scheepers]  
2 CONT Married: 1 Jan 1730 to [https://www.geni.com/people/Pieter-Gerrit-Bezuidenhout/6000000000000000007 Pieter Gerrit Bezuidenhout]  
2 CONT Married: 3 Dec 1741 to [https://www.geni.com/people/Johan-Jacob-Breytenbach/6000000000000000008 Johan Jacob Breytenbach]
2 CONT
2 CONT b7 [https://www.geni.com/people/Cornelia-Botha/6000000005788458307 Cornelia Botha]  
2 CONT Baptized: 6 Jan 1697  
2 CONT Married: 31 Mar 1720 to [https://www.geni.com/people/Hans-Jurgen-Potgieter/6000000000000000009 Hans Jurgen Potgieter]
2 CONT
2 CONT b8 [https://www.geni.com/people/Anna-Botha/6000000005788458308 Anna Botha]  
2 CONT Baptized: 19 Mar 1702  
2 CONT Married: [https://www.geni.com/people/Christian-Schmidt/placeholder Christian Schmidt]  
2 CONT Remarried: 18 May 1735 to [https://www.geni.com/people/Johannes-Friedrich-Muller/placeholder Johannes Friedrich Muller]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT *Friedrich made his will in 1699, stating that he had no mother or father still alive, nor any other person who had a rightful claim to his estate after his death, and that he left all he had to Maria Kickers, also resident in Ste
2 CONC llenbosch. [http://www.ballfamilyrecords.co.uk/lombard/I415.html Richard Ball]
2 CONT * Jan Cornelisz accused her of beating him up  (‘met slaan en stooten’) as one of the grounds for his divorce. There is also an affidavit from neighbours stating that she shouted at him and hit him, presumably in preparation for t
2 CONC he divorce, but no proof. Maria Kickers and Jan Cornelisz (married 11 July 1683) were divorced 22 Jan 1700 [http://www.ballfamilyrecords.co.uk Ball Family Records]), but she was not given leave to marry again after her divorce fro
2 CONC m Jan Cornelisz .
2 CONT * The muster roll of 1701 (dated 31st Jan 1702) lists Freidrich living in Stellenbosch with 8 children, and Maria also listed in Stellenbosch but living apart from them.
2 CONT * In Nov 1706, Botha and Maria Kickers were convicted of adultery, possession of livestock, and assault on Claas Das. On that occasion She persisted in the confession she had made and maintained that with promises and vows Botha a
2 CONC nd she had sworn their troth in private, as if they had entered into marriage with each other, and that they had lived with each other as man and wife for some years, and having carnal relations together had procreated eight child
2 CONC ren in this union, with her husband's tacit approval.. According to Schoeman, p. 468 in 1706, Botha and Maria Kickers were found guilty of "adultery, detention and concealment of cattle, [and] violence to the person of Claas Das, 
2 CONC and banished 'separately' to Mauritius for ten years." They were also fined 100 Rds, but evidence suggests the sentence was never executed as both appear in Cape muster rolls shortly after 1706. ([http://www.ballfamilyrecords.co.u
2 CONC k Ball Family Records]).  
2 CONT * After 1706 they lived at "Moddergat" near Stellenbosch while she worked for Matthys Greef.  
2 CONT * After Jan Cornelisz died in 1713, Maria and Friedrich married on 21 June 1714 in Stellenbosch (Stellenbosch Registers, p. 9) ([http://www.ballfamilyrecords.co.uk Ball Family Records] ; [https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:
2 CONC 1:S3HT-6LX3-V8P?i=7&cc=1478678&lang=en South Africa, Dutch Reformed Church Registers (Cape Town Archives), 1660-1994, Cape of Good Hope] ).  
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT === Notes on Name and Origin ===
2 CONT * The surname Both(a) derives from the Frisian "Botho" (or "Bote"), meaning leader or commander; the "a" denotes “son of”.  
2 CONT * Some sources suggest the Gotha origin may have contributed to the Cape spelling "Botha".  
2 CONT * The surname spelling evolved: in 1692 he signed as "Both"; in 1699 as "Botha". In opgaafrolle (census/muster rolls), variations include Both, Boot, and Botha. [http://www.ballfamilyrecords.co.uk/lombard/I415.html Richard Ball] s
2 CONC ays "He signs his surname variously, In 1699 to his will he signed Friderick Botta, later apparently Botha. Generally, in the written Dutch records he is referred to as Fredrik Boot, and in the church registers up to around the 17
2 CONC 30s the name is spelt Bota, thereafter Botha.
2 CONT
2 CONT === Sources / References ===
