3 STAE Cape of Good Hope
3 CTRY South Africa
1 DEAT
2 DATE 6 JUN 1771
2 PLAC Cape Town, South Africa
2 ADDR
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Catrijna Cornelisz  (<7 May 1690 -)''' 
2 CONT d/o Frederich Both by association & Maria Kickers
2 CONT (baptised as d/o Jan Cornelisz)
2 CONT x 31 August 1714 Hendrik Frederik Klopper (c1675 -15 Jun 1739)
2 CONT *Margrita 2 Sep 1714
2 CONT *Maria Elisabeth  21 Jan 1720
2 CONT *Frederik 13 Sep 1722
2 CONT *Antie  27 Aug 1724
2 CONT *Johannes  24 Nov 1726
2 CONT *Hendrik <11 Jun 1730
2 CONT
2 CONT Unfortunately the paternity of Maria's three daughters during her marriage with Jan will never be known. For her four sons however, we can use the non-recombining part of the Ychromosome region to test if her sons descend from the
2 CONC  same patriline [1,2]. Of course, this will only be true if adulterous relationships in later generations did not result in a mismatch of haplotypes. Fortunately, the Afrikaner population has an extremely low non-paternity rate of
2 CONC  0.8% [11] which means that direct male descendants will have a high probability of sharing the same Y-chromosome haplotype, even 10 generations later (92% chance = (1-0.008)10).
2 CONT
2 CONT The null hypothesis  that F Both was father of all her children has been nullified with DNA testing  of Thuenis Botha. Maria Kickers  statement legally has been proven invalid.  She lied or did really not know.
2 CONT
2 CONT chrome-extension://efaidnbmnnnibpcajpcglclefindmkaj/https://media.geni.com/p13/c2/f5/d0/61/53444852b746b4ff/greeff_appel_2013__original.pdf?hash=66c3cd706336c70ae8f1130ffd55b3221bcc697dce65b20ee130aba61c38c6c0.1724741999  --- YDNA
2 CONC  TESTS BOTHA & Appel 
2 CONT
2 CONT Any valid original primary source or DNA tests  prove she was the natural/biological  daughter of F Both ?
2 CONT NO !
2 CONT She could have been the  natural daughter any of the 3 partners of Maria Kickers -- impossible  to prove  who.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT '''Baptism doc shows her father as Jan Cornelisz''' - https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-89ML-49TG-2?i=23
2 CONT
2 CONT {{https://www.geni.com/media/proxy?media_id=6000000208438299822&size=large}}
2 CONT
2 CONT ''South Africa, Cape Province, Cape Town, church records	Baptisms, memberships, marriages, 1665-1695''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''However - her mother puts on legal record that none of her children were biologically fathered by Jan:'''
2 CONT DNA proved some were not Botha's children  as Maria claimed in court -- so obviously  Maria did not know who were the natural fathers of her children. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Before the Council of Justice, in 1700, in the business of the divorce, she declared all her children from the existing marriage had been engendered not by her husband (due to his incapacity) but by Frederick Boot, and that her 
2 CONC husband himself encouraged this ('en dat haren man haar daartoe selfs aanleijding soude hebben gegeeven').''
2 CONT ''The muster roll of 1701 (dated 31st January 1702) lists Frederik living in Stellenbosch with eight children, and Maria listed on her own but also in Stellenbosch , apparently living apart from them.''https://www.ballfamilyrecord
2 CONC s.co.uk/lombard/I411.html
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Ménage à quatre : Between 11 June 1683 and 1700 Maria Kickers and Jan Cornelisz were legally married, but at the same time, from at least 1687 Frederich Both and Maria were lovers and  Maria had sexual relations with https://www
2 CONC .geni.com/people/Ferdinandus-Appel/6000000001580940776?through=4705796237050024653   as well , apparently with the agreement of Jan. During divorce proceedings in 1700 Maria conceded that eight of her children, that is Theunis Bot
2 CONC ha, Willem Bootha, Catrijna Both, Cornelia Botha, Anna Bota, Maria Botha and Johannes Botha were fathered by Frederich Both(a) with the apparent encouragement (aanleijding) of her spouse, Jan Cornelisz, at the time. All of these o
2 CONC ffspring subsequently used the surname Both(a)''.https://www.e-family.co.za/ffy/g5/p5169.htm#c5169.5
2 CONT
2 CONT But we do know today that via DNA rests Maria lied or did not know who were the  eral fathers of her 8 children. Theunis definitely  not Botha 's child and how many others?
2 CONT Who knows really whose children  they were.
2 CONT The Ydna  can prove the fathers of the sons but unfortunately  no tests to confirm  the fathers of her daughters .
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Marriage to Kloppers''' names her as Bota:  https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:VFTM-YVN
2 CONT {{https://www.geni.com/media/proxy?media_id=6000000208438640839&size=large}}
2 CONT ----
