2 CONT ===Baptism===
2 CONT '''Jacobus  Cornelisze''' was baptized on 24 August 1692 Nederduitsch Gereformeerde Kerk, (Cape Town), de Caep de Goede Hoop. The baptism was witnessed by '''Jan Cornelisze van Outbeirlant, Maria Kikkers''', Hans Hendrik Smith and
2 CONC  Aaltje Claasz.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.e-family.co.za/ffy/g7/p7664.htm - where links to the baptisms of his children are available
2 CONT
2 CONT '''----
2 CONT NOTE:''' 
2 CONT '''Adopted  and raised as son of Friederich  Both -- yDNA  testing  have confirmed him as biological  son of Friederich Both''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Marriage===
2 CONT Attach
2 CONT '''Jacobus Bota'''
2 CONT Male
2 CONT 22 Oct 1713
2 CONT Caab
2 CONT Single
2 CONT '''Elsje Snijman'''
2 CONT Jacobus married Elsij Snijman, daughter of Christoffel Snijman and Marguerite-Thérèse de Savoye, on 22 October 1713
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Jacobus Botha de oude farmer (1721) of Jan Harmens Gat heemraad of Swellendam will dated 30 June 1776 and filed 29 March 1782
2 CONT
2 CONT '''The parents of Jacobus Botha de oude:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Maria Kickers stated in 1706 that all her eight children had been fathered by Frederick Botha (CJ 4, 363).
2 CONT
2 CONT NB: In 1718 a note in the Resolutions of the Council of Policy stated that money was still owed to the Company by '''Jan Cornelisz. van oud Beijerland, whose widow, Maria Bombam had a daughter, married to Jan Barentsz Siger, and t
2 CONC hree sons still living, Theunis, Jacobus and Willem Bota. (C. 47, pp. 32-42, 13 Sept. 1718)
2 CONT '''
2 CONT on http://www.ballfamilyrecords.co.uk/lombard/I425.html
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT "In 1731 we find the grazing rights (of the farm "Jan Harmsgat" ) being granted to a famous hunter, Jacobus Botha. His hunting career was brought to an end a couple of years later, when he shot a lion, and the lioness (which he ha
2 CONC d not seen) attacked and mauled him, leaving him for dead. Botha recovered but was never able to hunt again, and in 1734 Governor de la Fontaine made a freehold grant to Botha, for services rendered, of the farm Jan Harmans Gat wh
2 CONC ich he was then occupying. The farm was described as 'vier uur te perd van die dorp Swellendam' . Jacobus Botha lived to the age of 90, dying in 1782, and his 12 sons gave him 190 grandchildren. The farm is situated along the slop
2 CONC es of the Langeberg, between the mountain and the Breede River. The modern road from Swellendam to Ashton runs along this beautiful valley."
2 CONT
2 CONT https://janharmsgat.com/about-us/
