2 CONT According to the First Fifity Years Project, the mother of https://www.geni.com/people/Jacobus-Botha/6000000105788216970, Maria Kickers, was married to Jan Cornelisz. However, "from at least 1687 Frederich Both and Maria were love
2 CONC rs, apparently with the agreement of Jan. During divorce proceedings in 1700 Maria conceded that eight of her children, that is Theunis Botha, Willem Bootha, Catrijna Both, Cornelia Botha, Anna Bota, Maria Botha and Johannes Botha
2 CONC  were fathered by Frederich Both(a) with the apparent encouragement (aanleijding) of her spouse, Jan Cornelisz, at the time. All of these offspring subsequently used the surname Both(a).''' However, in 1689 two women alleged that 
2 CONC Theunis, Maria's oldest child, was fathered by Ferdinandùs Appel.''' This is born out by modern DNA tests, which have shown that direct patrilineal descendants of Theunis tested positive for the same Y-DNA haplogroup as direct pat
2 CONC rilineal descendants of Appel." 
2 CONT
2 CONT Names in the record, in publications, for https://www.geni.com/people/Jacobus-Botha/6000000105788216970 between 2 September 1714 and 8 August 1717, was written in the record as Jacobùs Bota and, between 7 October 1714 and 5 Januar
2 CONC y 1716, as Jacobùs Boota.
2 CONT
2 CONT *****
2 CONT https://ancestors.familysearch.org/en/LK1N-QJY/jacobus-botha-1692-1779
2 CONT '''When Jacobus Botha was born on 24 August 1692, in Cape of Good Hope, South Africa, his father, Frederick Botha, was 39 and his mother, Maria Kickers, was 30. He married Elsje Snyman on 22 October 1713, in Stellenbosch, Cape of 
2 CONC Good Hope, South Africa. They were the parents of at least 7 sons and 3 daughters. He lived in Cape Province, South Africa in 1713 and Cape Town, Cape Province, South Africa in 1719. His occupation is listed as butcher in Cape Pro
2 CONC vince, South Africa. He died on 19 May 1779, in Land van Waveren, Cape of Good Hope, South Africa, at the age of 86.'''
