3 CITY Cape Town
3 CTRY South Africa
1 DEAT
2 DATE 8 SEP 1819
2 PLAC Graaff-Reinet, Eastern Cape, South Africa
2 ADDR
1 OCCU Burger
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Potgieter Philip, burger Swellendam † voor 1843 
2 CONT
2 CONT Volgens SAG is sy naam  Philippus Potgieter. Gedoop 11/12/1758 Drakenstein   Dries Potgieter
2 CONT
2 CONT ______________________________________________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Notas deur David Abraham Swanepoel'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Sparrman noem die persoon in sy reisjoernaal [1]:
2 CONT
2 CONT “After this they bent their course towards Agter Bruntjeshoogte and were met on the road by three farmers, viz. Jacob Potgieter, with his son Flip, and his son-in-law Frans Labeskanje, who were coming with three Hottentots, accord
2 CONC ing to agreement, to strengthen our party, and to enable us the better to block up and shoot the sea-cows.” (p 263).
2 CONT
2 CONT “They” is ‘n aantal Xhosas wat naby Sparmann se geselskap uitgekamp het.
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Bron:''
2 CONT
2 CONT 1 . Sparmann, Anders. 1785. Voyage to the Cape of Good Hope: Towards the Antarctic Polar Circle, and Round the World: But Chiefly Into the Country of the Hottentots and Caffres, from the Year 1772 to 1776, Volume 2
2 CONT
2 CONT Inligting verskaf as Oop Toegang onderhewig aan lisensie CC BY-NC-ND 4.0 - Creative Commons https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/legalcode
2 CONT
2 CONT Kwytskelding: geen verantwoordelikheid word aanvaar vir enige foutiewe of onakkurate inligting nie, hetsy aangehaal, herverpak of self geskryf. Terme soos Hottentotte en Caffres was destyds in gebruik.
2 CONT --------------------
