1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =='''Reidulf Thoressøn (14th century – c. 1404)'''==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Biography''':
2 CONT * '''1378''': Witnessed, together with Gard Alfssøn at Søndre Hasle, that the heirs of the wife of his brother (Reidar) had received their inheritance.
2 CONT * '''1396''': Participated in a property exchange where one of the heirs received land in Søndre Hasle.
2 CONT * '''1398''': Announced, together with other men, a land exchange at Eker between Bishop Eystein and Guttorm Rolfssøn.
2 CONT * '''1404''': Last mentioned in records when he announced a settlement reached with the consent of Bishop Eystein.
2 CONT
2 CONT 🛡️ '''Heraldry''':
2 CONT In the 1398 document, Reidulf used the seal of the Kane noble family: 4 stars in a cross-divided shield. The historian assumes that he used this coat of arms due to a close cognitive connection with the Kane family, suggesting his
2 CONC  wife was likely a Kane. This is further supported by his son receiving the name Thoralde, which was a distinct Kane name.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sources''':
2 CONT # Norsk tidsskrift for genealogi (1908), Vol. 1, No. 3, [https://www.nb.no/items/e10dd023f88a4b86e782b2a2173a9e52?page=4&searchText=Olaf%20Haldorssøn p. 163].
2 CONT # Archival references from the text: DN. I 449, DN. XV 34, DN. II 552, DN. II 579.
2 CONT ———————
2 CONT
2 CONT I 1398 kunngjør Reidulf jordbytte på Eker mellem biskop Eystein og dennes værbror Guttorm Olfssøn. '''Reidulf fører etten Kane's våpen''': 4 stjerner i et korsdelt skjold (etter sin hustru).
