1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Kristina BIRGERSDOTTER (Folkungaätten)=
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT *'''Daughter of  Birger Birger Jarl MAGNUSSON FOLKUNGE (~1200 - 1266) & Ingeborg ERIKSDOTTER (1214 - 1254)''' 
2 CONT * [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SWEDEN.htm#BirgerMagnussondied1266B '''KRISTINA Birgersdotter''' (-after 1285).  Married SIGGE Guttormsson, from Ljuna (-bur Alvastra Abbey).]
2 CONT * [http://samla.raa.se/xmlui/bitstream/handle/raa/1098/1935_237.pdf?sequence=1&isAllowed=y '''Death Record:''' 1273-02-05 Östergötland, Näsby i Åkerbo hd]
2 CONT * Kristina Birgersdotter is mentioned several times as married to the knight Sigge Guttormsson (two lilies with stems, rising from an open rose).
2 CONT
2 CONT =Married=
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married: [https://www.geni.com/photo/view/6000000009365755840?album_type=photos_of_me&photo_id=6000000116462334837 '''Sigge Guttormsson of Ljuna,'''] GUTTORMSSON (TVÅ LILJESTAVAR SNETT NEDSKJUTANDE FRÅN SÄNKT ROS). and mother-in
2 CONC -law to the lords Lidinvard Ödesson (Örnfot) and to the national council Ulf Holmgersson (Ama). 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children=
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Birger Siggesson (gumsehuvud),''' Oh my dear, my dear, I give my furded coat with a capuchon - for my son Birger, this armor as a whole, as I have had." The young son Birger gets his father's armor, because he seems to be ded
2 CONC icated to a worldly career as a knight. 
2 CONT * '''Helena Siggedotter;''' Their daughter Helena's daughter has to have been married first to the Danish knight Ingemar Nielsen, and Then to Ulf Holmgersson (Ama). A son is also known by Siggy Guttormssons Testament, written 11 J
2 CONC une 1283
2 CONT * '''Margaret Siggesdotter'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source''' Adelsvapen - https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Folkunga%C3%A4tten#TAB_13
2 CONT
2 CONT = The Swedish Diplomatarium's National Archives of Medieval Letters=
2 CONT
2 CONT ==SDHK No: [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=sigge+guttormsson&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=1&postid=sdhk_1238&tab=post#tab 1238]
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Dating: 1283 June 11'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Sigge Guttormsson to Ljuna prepares his will as follows: to the monks in Alvastra, where he chooses his grave, he donates his farm in Västra Ljuna (Hogstads parish) with movable property in accordance with a previous letter (12760
2 CONC 000 b, DS 608), to the church of Näsby's estate, comprising a tooth of any new cultivation, to Salmundus, the parish priest in the church, 1 land of money, to the church in Hogstad (Hogstad parish) 1/4 eighth in "Colsthorp" to cov
2 CONC er the expenses of someone Sister Priest there, to Mr. Runstanus, Sister Priest there, 2 Mark Pence, to the Lesser Brothers in Söderköping 1 Mark Silver, to the Preacher Brothers in Skänninge 1 Mark Silver, to the Preacher Brother
2 CONC s in Skara 1 Mark Silver, to the Brothers in Skara 1 Mark Silver, to the hospital in Skara 1/2 mark silver, to the brothers in Lödöse 1 mark silver, to two hospitals in Östergötland 1 mark silver, to the monastery in Askeby 1 mark
2 CONC  silver, to the monastery of Vreta 1 mark silver, t ill brothers in Nyköping 1 mark of silver, further 1 mark of silver as a kind of replacement, which he mentioned to his father in law, and finally to the hospital at Öland 1/2 ma
2 CONC rk silver. In order to pay the above, he pledges his red clothes and 1 eighth in West Ljuna between the two farms and forbids anyone besides the monks in Alvastra or his wife to redeem this eighth. Furthermore he donates to the ch
2 CONC urch in Linköping's farm in Hogstad with all belongings and buildings1 and releases all his troops. To the prostitute Nils in Högby, he donates his black tunic with surkot and hood, to his nephew N, his lined hoodie, to his son Bi
2 CONC rger as the "schooling" the value of his own armor, since it was sold by the testament dean Dean Jng (e / mouth /?). His other weapons are to be distributed to his wife, between his friends, Beno Byllasson, Hakvin Rød, Nils Krok, 
2 CONC Yandus, Torkil, Peter Långe and Toke, in addition to a horse, his sword and helmet, which he gives to Yandus. In order to get rid of his crusade promise he dedicates two silver beads and a silver cannon, which is found at the gold
2 CONC smith Tideman in Söderköping. In addition, he pays a lot of goods to solve a number of money requirements for individuals and institutions. Witnesses are his wife Kristina, the linking schnapps Svennung and Birger, magician Otto, 
2 CONC brother Knut from Söderköping and his priest Nils, who also sealed together with the issuer and the linköping chapter. - https://www.geni.com/photo/view?album_type=photos_of_me&id=6000000025565454677&photo_id=6000000138090200144&p
2 CONC osition=0
2 CONT
2 CONT ==SDHK No: [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=sigge+guttormsson&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=2&postid=sdhk_1286&tab=post#tab 1286]
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Dating: 1285 without day'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Kristina, Birger Earl's daughter (and widow of Mr. Sigge Guttormsson to Ljuna), establishes his testament as follows: To the monks of Alvastra, with whom she chose her graveyard with her husband, she donates the farm Ljuna (Hogsta
2 CONC ds socken, Göstrings (1 in its entirety with the exception of an oath and a plot, which with all its belongings is inevitably linked to its farm "walled"; this is, however, subject to all returns of the farm (Ljuna?) annually on 2
2 CONC 9/8 shall be paid in return for the whole convention, if possible in the form of a joint extradition, and celebrating her anniversary. Furthermore, she donates to Linköping's cathedral, the Normlösa farm, where on the bishop's beh
2 CONC alf an altar will be established Week two fairs will be held for the dead, one for the Virgin Mary and a death fair for her deceased husband (2. Finally, she also donates 1 mark of silver to each monastery In Sweden, with the exce
2 CONC ption of those in Gotland and Finland, for night quarters and 1/2 mark silver for each hospital in the Kingdom. Sigillants are the issuer, King M (agnus), his brother Duke B (eng) of Finland, Bishop B. (wrong for H.?) In Linköping
2 CONC  and the daughters of the issue Margaret and Helena. Witnesses were Abbot Nils in Alvastra and Kristina's confessor brother Knut from Söderköping. - https://www.geni.com/photo/view?album_type=photos_of_me&id=6000000009365755840&ph
2 CONC oto_id=6000000143167703111&position=0
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SWEDEN.htm#IngeIdied1111 Project MedLands, Sweden Kings]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Chapter 3.  KINGS of SWEDEN 1250-1412 (FOLKINGAÄTTEN)'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''BIRGER Magnusson, son of MAGNUS "Minnesköld" [Folkungaatten] & his second wife Ingrid [Ylva] '''([1200]-20/21 Oct 1266, bur Varnhem Abbey).  The Icelandic Annals record that "dominus Birgerus Magni filius" was made "comes in Sv
2 CONC ecia" in 1248[173].  Jarl at Bjälbo.  Regent of Sweden.  Founder of Stockholm.  “B…Dux Sueorum” donated property to Eskilstuna Kloster by charter dated 16 Jul 1266 which names “filiorum nostrorum…W…Regis Sueorum, Magni Ducis…Ericj
2 CONC  ac Benedictj Scolaris”[174].  The Icelandic Annals record the death in 1265 of "Birgerus dux Sveciæ"[175]. 
2 CONT '''married firstly ([1235]) INGEBORG of Sweden, daughter of ERIK Knutsson King of Sweden & his second wife Richeza of Denmark''' ([1212]-17 Jun 1254).  Her marriage is confirmed by a charter dated 4 Nov 1246 in which “Ericus…rex S
2 CONC wethie” names “domino Birgero genero nostro”[176].  The primary source which confirms her name has not yet been identified. 
2 CONT '''married secondly (1261) as her second husband, MECHTILD von Holstein, widow of ABEL King of Denmark, daughter of ADOLF IV Graf von Holstein und Stormarn & his wife Hedwig zur Lippe''' (1225-1288, bur Varnhem Abbey).  The Annale
2 CONC s Stadenses record the marriage "1237 VII Kal Mai" of "dux Abel" and "filiam comitis Adolfi de Scowenborch", naming her "Mechtildem" and recording her second marriage to "ducem Sueciæ" in a later passage[177].  The Icelandic Annal
2 CONC s record the marriage in 1261 of "Bergerus Sveciæ dux" and "Mathildam reginam Daniæ"[178]. 
2 CONT Mistress (1): ---.  The name of Birger's mistress is not known. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Birger Magnusson & his first wife INGEBORG of Sweden had eight children:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1.     '''    RIKISSA Birgersdotter''' (-before 13 Dec 1288).  The Cronica Principum Saxonie names "Rixam filiam regis Suecie" as wife of "Henricum seniorem [filium Nycolai domini de Werle]"[179].  The primary source which confi
2 CONC rms her first marriage has not yet been identified.  m firstly (Oslo 1251) HAAKON Haakonsson "den Unge/the Young" under King of Norway, son of HAAKON IV "den Gamle/the Old" King of Norway & his wife Margareta Skulesdotter (Bergen 
2 CONC 10 Nov 1232-Tønsberg 30 Apr or 5 May1257, bur Oslo, St Hallvards Church).  m secondly (1262) as his first wife, HEINRICH von Werle, son of NIKOLAUS I Herr von Werle zu Rostock [Mecklenburg] & his wife Jutta von Anhalt (-murdered n
2 CONC ear Saal, Rügen 8 Oct 1291).  Herr zu Werle zu Güstrow 1281. 
2 CONT * 2.        ''' VALDEMAR Birgersson''' ([1237]-Nyköping Castle 26 Dec 1302).  The Icelandic Annals record that "Valdemarus Birgiri filius" succeeded as king of Sweden in 1249[180].  He succeeded in 1250 as VALDEMAR King of Sweden.
2 CONC   “Waldemarus…rex Swechie” confirmed the donation of property to Gudhems Kloster by “reginam dominam Katerinam” by charter dated 17 Jan 1251 which names “patris nostri domini Byrgerj ducis”[181].  The Annales Lubicenses records th
2 CONC at "Waldemarus rex Sweorum" was deposed in 1275 by "Magno duce fratre suo"[182].  The Icelandic Annals record the reconcilation between "reges Valdemarus et Magnus" and the departure of Valdemar for Denmark soon after[183].  The I
2 CONC celandic Annals record the death in 1302 of "Valdemarus Birgeri filius Rex Sveonum"[184].  m firstly (1260, divorced after 1276) SOPHIE of Denmark, daughter of ERIK IV "Plovpenning" King of Denmark & his wife Jutta of Saxony (-128
2 CONC 6).  The Icelandic Annals record a visit to "Konúngahellam…festo martyris Albani" by "rex Valdemarus Sophiaque regina cum filio domicello Erico annos quinque nato" in 1276[185].  The Icelandic Annals note the presence of "Sophia r
2 CONC egina Valdimari regis, eorumque filio Erico domicello et filiabus Ingeburga quæ nupsit Gerhardo filio Gerhardi comitis Holsatiæ et Catharina virgine" at the reconcilation between "reges Valdemarus et Magnus"[186].  m secondly LUCA
2 CONC RDIS, daughter of ---.  1296.  The primary source which confirms her marriage has not yet been identified.   Mistress (1): JUTTA of Denmark, daughter of ERIK IV "Plovpenning" King of Denmark & his wife Jutta of Saxony ([1246]-[128
2 CONC 6/95]).  Abbess of St Agneta in Roskilde 1266.  She left the convent in 1271[187]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ''' King Valdemar had & his first wife had seven children:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>* a)        ''' ERIK Valdemarsson''' (-1261, bur Sigruna Abbey).  The primary source which confirms his parentage has not yet been identified.  
2 CONT >>>>* b)         '''INGEBORG Valdemarsdotter''' (-[1290]).  The Annales Lubicenses refer to the first wife of "Gherardi comitis Holtzatiæ" as "filia Woldemari Regis Sweciæ"[188].  “Waldemarus…Rex Sveorum” confirmed a grant to Hamb
2 CONC urg by “pater noster Dominus Byrgerus felicis memoriæ Dux Sveorum” by charter dated 12 Dec 1275 “in nuptiis filiæ nostræ…et comitis Gerardi…de Holsatia”[189].  The Icelandic Annals note the presence of "Sophia regina Valdimari reg
2 CONC is, eorumque filio Erico domicello et filiabus Ingeburga quæ nupsit Gerhardo filio Gerhardi comitis Holsatiæ et Catharina virgine" at the reconcilation between "reges Valdemarus et Magnus"[190].  m (12 Dec 1275) as his first wife,
2 CONC  GERHARD II Graf von Holstein in Plön, son of GERHARD I Graf von Holstein in Itzehoe & his first wife Elisabeth von Mecklenburg (1254-Plön 28 Oct 1312, bur Hamburg Cathedral).
2 CONT >>>>* c)         '''KATARINA Valdemarsdotter''' (-1283).  The Icelandic Annals record a visit to "Konúngahellam…festo martyris Albani" by "rex Valdemarus Sophiaque regina cum filio domicello Erico annos quinque nato" in 1276[191].
2 CONC
2 CONT >>>>* d)         '''ERIK Valdemarsson''' [Folkungaättens Valdemarsgren] ([1271/72]-1330).  The Icelandic Annals record a visit to "Konúngahellam…festo martyris Albani" by "rex Valdemarus Sophiaque regina cum filio domicello Erico 
2 CONC annos quinque nato" in 1276[192].  The Icelandic Annals record a visit to "Konúngahellam…festo martyris Albani" by "rex Valdemarus Sophiaque regina cum filio domicello Erico annos quinque nato" in 1276[193].  The Icelandic Annals 
2 CONC record that "domicellus Ericus filius Valdemari" was released from prison in 1302[194].  Norwegian High Councillor 1308.  Swedish High Councillor 1322.  m INGEBORG Knutsdotter, daughter of KNUT Jonsson [Aspenäsätten] & his wife Ka
2 CONC tharina Bengtsdotter [Folkungaättens lagmansgren].  1333.  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Erik & his wife had one child:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>>>>* i)         ''' VALDEMAR Eriksson'''  1345/69.  m firstly (before 1347) INGEGÄRD Karlsdotter [Färla], daughter of [KARL Orestason [Färla] & his wife Helena Magnusdotter [Folkungaättens oäkta gren]].  m secondly as her firs
2 CONC t husband, HELGA Anundsdotter [Balk av Strand], daughter of ANUND Röriksson [Balk av Strand] & his wife Cecilia Magnusdotter.  She married secondly (before 1379) Ya Königsmarck, Vogt of Stockholm Castle.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Valdemar & his wife had one child:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>>>>>>>(a)       ERIK Valdemarsson (-[1388/96]).  m ERMEGARD --- (-[1402/03].
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>* e)       '''  RIKISSA Valdemarsdotter''' (-[1 Sep 1288/19 Apr 1293]).  The Annales Polonorum record the marriage "1285 in octavis sancti Francisci" of "filiam regis Swecie nomine Rithcam" and "dux Primislius maioris Polonie"
2 CONC [195].  m (1285) as his second wife, PRZEMYSŁ Prince of Greater Poland, son of PRZEMYSŁ I Prince of Poznan, Kalisch and Gniezien [Piast] & his wife Elisabeth von Schlesien [Piast] (14 Oct 1257-murdered Rogoźno 8 Feb 1296, bur Pose
2 CONC n Cathedral).  He succeeded in 1295 as PRZEMYSŁ II King of Poland. 
2 CONT >>>>* f)          '''MARIANNA Valdemarsdotter''' The primary source which confirms her parentage and marriage has not yet been identified.   1299.  m (Nyköping 1285) as his second wife, RUDOLF von Diepholz, son of --- (-1303 or af
2 CONC ter).
2 CONT >>>>* g)         '''MARGARETA Valdemarsdotter'''  The primary source which confirms her parentage has not yet been identified.   Nun at Skänninge Convent 1288. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''King Valdemar had one possible illegitimate son by Mistress (1):'''
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>* h)         '''ERIK Valdemarsson''' ([1273]-).  Brenner doubts his existence, saying he is likely confused with King Valdemar's legitimate son Erik[196].] 
2 CONT
2 CONT * 3.         '''MAGNUS Ladulås Birgersson''' ([1240]-Visingsö 18 Dec 1290, bur Stockholm, Riddarholm Church).  The Annales Lubicenses names "Magno duce fratre suo [=Waldemarus rex Sweorum]" when recording that he deposed his broth
2 CONC er in 1275[197].  He succeeded in 1275 as MAGNUS I Ladulås King of Sweden.   
2 CONT * 4.         '''KRISTINA Birgersdotter (-after 1285).  The primary source which confirms her parentage and marriage has not yet been identified.   '''Married SIGGE Guttormsson, from Ljuna (-bur Alvastra Abbey)'''.1285 or after, bu
2 CONC r Alvastra Abbey [Östergötland]).  “M...Sweorum Gothorumque Rex et B. frater suus” confirmed the donation made to Linköping made by “soror nostra Domina Cristina” by charter dated 25 Jun 1282, sealed by “...prefate sororis nostre 
2 CONC Domine C. et mariti sui Domini S. ac filiarum suarum Dominarum M. et E.”[278].  The testament of “Cristina Byrgheri ducis Sweorum quondam filia”, dated 1285, chose burial “monachis in Alwastrum apud quos ex deliberacione diutina u
2 CONC na cum marito meo...domino Siggone” for which she donated “curiam...Lywnær [Ljuna, in Högstad, Östergötland]”, donated property to Linköping for masses including “omni septimana...una missa pro defunctis, pro anima...mariti nostri
2 CONC  Domini Siggonis, sicut in suo continetur testamento” [confirming that he was then deceased], sealed by “Domini M....regis Sweorum Gothorumque et...germani eius B. ducis Fynlandie...meum, nec non et predulcium mearum, Margarte et 
2 CONC Helene filiarum feci presentibus”[279].  [m firstly ---.  No proof of this possible earlier marriage has been found.  However, the absence of Kristina’s two daughters (named in her 1285 testament, presumably as adults so born late
2 CONC  [1250s/1260]) from her known husband’s 1283 testament (see below) suggests that he may not have been their father[280].  This suggestion appears corroborated by Kristina’s 25 Jun 1282 charter cited above which refers to “mariti s
2 CONC ui” and “filiarum suarum”.]  m [secondly] SIGGE Guttormson, son of --- (-[1283/1285], bur Alvastra Abbey).  He was named in the 25 Jun 1282 charter cited above.  Sigge’s testament, dated 1283, names the couple’s son Birger, who pr
2 CONC esumably died before his mother’s 1285 testament in which he is not mentioned, but not the two daughters which suggests their birth from an earlier otherwise unrecorded marriage of their mother, see above[281].  The daughter Margr
2 CONC ete married Leonard/Lidinvard/Lennart Ötheson, Iagman i Nárke, while Helene married firstly riddare Ingemar Nielsson (murdered in 1278, discussed in Erikskrönikan[282]) and secondly (Papal dispensation 13 Feb 1284) her third cousi
2 CONC n riddare Ulf Holmgerson till Rammshammar (who is named until 1290), their unnamed daughter marrying riddare Torkel Andersån, high counsellor of Sweden (who was named in 1311, 1318, and 1335)[283].  The testament of Helene’s grand
2 CONC daughter, “Ingiburgis Thorstensdoter” [Ingeborg Torstensdotter], dated 28 Mar 1346, bequeathed property to “consanguineo meo domino Birghero Magnusson...matri mee...domine Katerine Vlpsdoter...sorori mee domicelle Katerine...Laure
2 CONC ncio Ingibyornæson...”, witnessed by “dominum Birgherum Magnusson [executor] dominam Katerinam consortem suam, dominam Elenam Thorchilsdoter, domicellam Katerinam Birghersdoter, Holmgerum Thorchilssom, fratrem Johannem Allonis, do
2 CONC minum Thorgotum, dominum Swenungam, Jaconbum Sonæson cum uxore Hermannum Cristinam Eriksdoter, Cristinam Pætersdoter...”[284]. 
2 CONT * 5.         '''KATARINA''' The Cronica Principum Saxonie names "Katerinam, filiam regis Suecie" as wife of "Sifridum comitem"[198].  m (before 17 Oct 1259) SIEGFRIED Graf von Anhalt in Köthen und Dessau, son of HEINRICH I "der Fe
2 CONC tte" Graf von Anhalt und Aschersleben & his wife Irmgard von Thüringen (-after 25 Mar 1298, bur Coswig).
2 CONT * 6.         '''ERIK Birgersson''' (-17 Dec 1275).  “B…Dux Sueorum” donated property to Eskilstuna Kloster by charter dated 16 Jul 1266 which names “filiorum nostrorum…W…Regis Sueorum, Magni Ducis…Ericj ac Benedictj Scolaris”[199]
2 CONC .  Duke in southern Sweden 1275. 
2 CONT * 7.      '''   INGEBORG '''(-30 Jun 1302, bur Mölln).  The Cronica Principum Saxonie refers to the wife of "Iohannem [filium Alberti dux]" as "filiam regis Suecie"[200].  The Annales Lubicenses record the death in 1302 of "Ingebu
2 CONC rgis, mater Alberti, Iohannis et Erici ducum Saxoniæ, filia Regis Sweonum"[201].  m ([1270]) JOHANN I Herzog von Sachsen, son of ALBRECHT I Herzog zu Sachsen, Engern und Westfalen [Askanier] & his third wife Helene von Braunschwei
2 CONC g (-30 Jul 1286).
2 CONT * 8.         '''BENGT Birgersson''' ([1254]-25 May 1291).  “B…Dux Sueorum” donated property to Eskilstuna Kloster by charter dated 16 Jul 1266 which names “filiorum nostrorum…W…Regis Sueorum, Magni Ducis…Ericj ac Benedictj Scolari
2 CONC s”[202].  Duke in Finland 1284.  Bishop of Linköping 1286. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Birger Magnusson had one illegitimate son by Mistress (1):'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * 9.        '''  GREGERS Birgersson or Frilloson''' [Folkingaättens oäkta gren] (-1276, bur Uppsala).  At Ängsjö.  The Icelandic Annals record the death in 1276 of "Gregorius filius notus Birgeri comitis"[203].  He was ancestor of
2 CONC  the Folkingaättens Oäkta Gren family. 
2 CONT
