1 NOTE He was called Lawmender.  He who replaced the various provincial laws with 
2 CONT a common national code. The son and successor of Håkon IV, he continued 
2 CONT the governmental reforms begun by his father, establishing a hereditary 
2 CONT nobility and making the king's council a permanent institution. His 
2 CONT national law code, issued in 1274, for the first time made the punishment 
2 CONT for crime a public rather than a private responsibility. In 1277 he 
2 CONT concluded a concordat with the church and issued a special municipal code, 
2 CONT which was based on the existing institutions of Bergen. He was succeeded 
2 CONT by his son, Eric the Priesthater.
1 NOTE Källa:http://harmkraka.se/slaktforskning/fm/index.htm
1 NOTE He was king from 1263 to 1280.
