2 CONT
2 CONT ==Astrid Njalsdotter==
2 CONT
2 CONT * The Hervarar saga (13th century) describes Stenkil as the son of Ragnvald the Old and Astrid Njalsdotter, the daughter of Njal Finnsson from Hålogaland in Norway and a cognatic descendant of Harald Fairhair. Later historians hav
2 CONC e identified the father of Stenkil Ragnvald Ulfsson who was the earl of Staraja Ladoga and the grandson of the legendary Viking Skoglar Toste. But this presumed family-connection is not supported by any other sources and must ther
2 CONC efore be regarded as very uncertain.[6] The Icelandic sagas mention a wife and two sons to Ragnvald Ulfsson but none are identical with Stenkil and his mother Astrid. The contemporary chronicler Adam of Bremen says Stenkil was the
2 CONC  nephew (nepos) or stepson (privignus) of the former King Emund the Old,[7] while the Hervarar saga asserts that he was related to the previous dynasty by marriage to Emund's daughter.
2 CONT *  Married secondly as her second husband EMUND Olofsson, son of OLOF, son of ERIK "Segersäll/the Victorious" King of Sweden & his wife Sigrid "Storråda/the Haughty" ASTRID Njalsdotter, widow of RAGNVALD Ulfsson Jarl of Västergötl
2 CONC and, daughter of NJAL
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Project MedLands, Sweden Kings==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''KINGS of SWEDEN 1060-[1111] (FAMILY of STENKIL)'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Skoglar" TOSTE, son of ---.  In Svithjod.  Snorre records that Harald "Grenske" was welcomed in Svithjod by "Toste…often in battle…therefore called Skoglar-Toste" and lived five years with him[68]. 
2 CONT m ---.  
2 CONT
2 CONT The name of Toste's wife is not known. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Toste & his wife had two children: 
2 CONT * 1.         '''ULF'''.  According to Snorre[69], he was the brother of Sigrid "Storråda/the Haughty".  m ---.  The name of Ulf's wife is not known.  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''ULF & his wife had one child:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * a)        ''' RAGNVALD Ulfsson,''' Snorre names "Earl Ragnvald, Ulf's son" when recording his [first] marriage[70].  Jarl in Västergötland.  Snorre records that Ragnvald accompanied Ingegerd to Russia and was installed as Earl o
2 CONC f Ladoga[71].  '''married  firstly INGEBORG Trygvesdatter, daughter of TRYGVE Olavsson of Norway & his wife Åstrid Eiriksdatter.''' Snorre records the marriage of Ingebjorg, Trygve's daughter, King Olaf's sister and Earl Ragnvald,
2 CONC  Ulf's son"[72].   '''married  secondly [as her first husband,] ASTRID Njalsdotter, daughter of NJAL & his wife.'''  The primary source which confirms her parentage and two marriages has not yet been identified.  [She married seco
2 CONC ndly as his second wife, Emund Slemme den Gamle/the Old King of Sweden.  Her supposed second marriage to Ragnvald may be nothing more than a guess based on Adam of Bremen recording that nepos eius [=rex Sueonum Emund] Stinkel succ
2 CONC eeded on the death of Emund[73].]  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Jarl Ragnvald & his first wife had two children:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>* i)          '''ULF''' Snorre names "Earl Ulf and Earl Eilif" as the sons of Ragnvald & his wife[74]. 
2 CONT >>>>* ii)         '''EILIF''  names "Earl Ulf and Earl Eilif" as the sons of Ragnvald & his wife[75]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Jarl Ragnvald & his second wife had one child:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>* iii)       ''' STENKIL Ragnvaldson''' (-1066).  The primary source which confirms his parentage has not yet been identified.  He succeeded [his stepfather] in 1060 as STENKIL King of Sweden.   
2 CONT
2 CONT * 2.         '''SIGRID "Storråda/the Haughty'''.  Snorre names Sigrid as daughter of "Skoglar" Toste and refers to her '''marriage to "the Swedish king, Eirik the Victorious'''  Saxo Grammaticus names "Syritha" as mother of "Erici
2 CONC  filius Olavus"[77].  The Fagrskinna names Sigrid, mother of King Olof, as daughter of Skoglar-Tosta[78].  Morkinskinna names "Sigridr en stórráda" as mother of “the lady Ástrídr…sister of two kings, Knútr the Great and Óláfr the 
2 CONC Swede” who married “Jarl Úlfr sprakaleggr”[79].  '''married firstly ([before 985]) ERIK "Segersäll/the Victorious" King of Sweden, son of [EMUND Erikson King of Sweden]''' (-Uppsala [994/95]). '''married secondly ([1000]) as his s
2 CONC econd wife, SVEND I "Tveskæg/Forkbeard" King of Denmark, son of HARALD I "Blåtand/Bluetooth" King of Denmark & his first wife Gunhild''' ([960]-Gainsborough 3 Feb 1014, bur in England, later removed to Roskilde).   
2 CONT
