2 CONC C3%B8ks/6000000003094359287?through=6000000005049052310 ERIK I] "Blodøks/Blood-axe" King of Norway & his wife [http://www.geni.com/people/Gunhild-Ossursdotter/6000000005049052310 Queen Gunhild]  Gormsdatter.  
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>d)         [http://www.geni.com/people/H%C3%A5vard-Season-Prosperous-Thorfinsson/6000000002855667029  HAVARD] Torfinnsson "Season-prosperous" (-murdered, bur Stennis, Hrossey). 
2 CONT >>>m as her second husband, [http://www.geni.com/people/Ragnhild-The-Wicked-Eiriksdotter/6000000003645825602?through=6000000002855667029 RAGNHILD Eiriksdatter], widow of ARNFINN Torfinnsson Jarl of Orkney, daughter of ERIK I "Blod
2 CONC øks/Blood-axe" King of Norway & his wife Gunhild Gormsdatter.  
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>e)         [http://www.geni.com/people/Ljot/6000000003645977990   LJOT] Torfinnsson (-killed in battle).  
2 CONT >>>m as her third husband, [http://www.geni.com/people/Ragnhild-The-Wicked-Eiriksdotter/6000000003645825602 RAGNHILD] 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>f)          [http://www.geni.com/people/Hlodver-Thorfinnsson/6000000001045422816  HLODVIR Torfinnsson] ([945/50]-[988], bur Hofn, Caithness).  Orkneyinga Saga names (in order) “Arnfinn…Havard the Fecund…Hlodvir…Ljot…Skuli” as t
2 CONC he five sons of Thorfinn[844].  Snorre names "the Earls Hlodver, Arnfid, Ljot and Skule, the sons of Thorfin Hausakljufer" as rulers in Orkney when [http://www.geni.com/people/Gunhild-Ossursdotter/6000000005049052310 Queen Gunhild
2 CONC ]  and her sons returned to Orkney[845].  In a later saga, Snorre names (in order) "Arnfin, Havard, Hlodver, Liot and Skule" as sons of Thorfin "Hausakljufer"[846].  Orkneyinga Saga records that “after Ljot´s death, Hlodvir took c
2 CONC harge of the earldom”, presumably indicating Ljot´s brother but this is not explicitly stated in the text, recording that “he died in his bed” and was buried “in a burial mound at Ham in Caithness”[847]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>m [http://www.geni.com/people/Audna-of-Orkney/6000000000160947334?through=6000000001045422816  EITHNE], daughter of KIARVAL King of Ireland & his wife ---.  Orkneyinga Saga records that “Hlodvir” married “Eithne, the daughter 
2 CONC of King Kjarval of Ireland”, adding in a later passage that “Sigurd´s mother was a sorceress”[848].  Hlodve´s supposed father-in-law has not been identified among known Irish kings.  
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>Hlodve & his wife had [three] children:  [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SCOTTISH%20NOBILITY.htm#_Toc268450047 (Cawley's Medlands)]
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>i)          [http://www.geni.com/people/Sigurd-II-Hlodvesson/6000000001041474621?through=6000000001045422816  SIGURD] "Digri/the Stout", son of [HLODVIR Torfinnsson Jarl of Orkney & his wife Eithne of Ireland] ([965/70]-killed
2 CONC  in battle Clontarf 23 Apr 1014).  Orkneyinga Saga names “Sigurd the Stout” as the son of Hlodvir and his wife, adding that he “took over the earldom” after his father died[856].  Snorre names "Sigurd the Thick" as the son of Hlod
2 CONC ver[857].  His birth date is estimated from the fact that his older sons were already sufficiently mature in 1014 to be placed in charge of Orkney by their father when he left for war in Ireland.  He succeeded his father in [988] 
2 CONC as Jarl of Orkney and Caithness.  He defeated Findlaech Mormaer of Moray before 995 at the second battle of Skidmoor in Caithness, consolidating his power on the Scottish mainland.  Orkneyinga Saga records Sigurd´s battle against 
2 CONC “a Scottish earl called Finnleik”[858].  Orkneyinga Saga records that “[http://www.geni.com/people/Olav-Tryggvason/6000000003867333182 Olaf Tryggvason]” pressured Sigurd to accept baptism and returned to Norway with Sigurd´s son a
2 CONC s a hostage[859].  Orkneyinga Saga records that Sigurd went to Ireland “five years after the Battle of Svoldur” to support “King [http://www.geni.com/people/Sitric-I-King-of-Dublin/6000000002043182790?through=6000000003645985234 S
2 CONC igtrygg Silk-Beard]” against “[http://www.geni.com/people/Brian-B%C3%B3ruma-mac-Cenn%C3%A9tig/6000000002043263223  King Brian] of Ireland”, and left “his elder sons in charge of the earldom”, but was killed in the battle in which 
2 CONC King Brian was killed[860].  Snorre records that "Sigurd the Thick" went to Ireland and fell "in Brian's battle"[861].  [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SCOTTISH%20NOBILITY.htm#_Toc268450047 (Cawley's Medlands)]
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>m firstly ---.  The name of Sigurd´s first wife is not known.  Sigurd & his [first wife] had four children:  
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>>1.         [http://www.geni.com/people/Sumarlidi-Sigurdsson-988-1015-Jarl-of-Orkney/6000000003645672837 SOMERLED] (-[1015/20]).  
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>>2.         [http://www.geni.com/people/Brusi-Orkneyjarl/6000000001041560317   BRUSI] (-[1030/35]).  .  m ---.  The name of Brusi´s wife is not known.  Brusi & his wife had one child:  
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>>>a)         [http://www.geni.com/people/Ragnvald-Orkneyjarl/6000000002512272392  RAGNVALD] Brusason ([1010/15]-Dec 1046, bur Papa Westray).  
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>>3.         [http://www.geni.com/people/Einar-Jarl-of-Orkney/6000000004333578987  EINA] "Rangmund/Wrymouth" (-murdered Sandwick [1023/25]). 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>>4.         [http://www.geni.com/people/Hlodve-Hund-Orkney/6000000003645712452   HUNDI] [Hlodvir] ([990]-[996/1000]).  
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>'''m ([1005 or after]) --- of Scotland, [http://www.geni.com/people/Olith-possibly-Donada-MacKenneth/6000000004093135189 daughter of MALCOLM II] King of Scotland & his wife ---.  Orkneyinga Saga records that “Earl Sigurd” marr
2 CONC ied “the daughter of Malcolm King of Scots” (whose succession is recorded in 1005)[862].  Snorre records the marriage of "Sigurd the Thick" and "a daughter of the Scottish king Malcolm"[863].  It appears unlikely that Sigurd´s wif
2 CONC e could have been King Malcolm´s daughter Donada (as shown in many secondary sources, including the Complete Peerage[864]) if it is correct that Donada´s recorded husband Findlaech was killed in 1020 and that their son was born in
2 CONC  [1005][865]. [Note – It is perfectly possible that Sigurd took Donada from Findlaech, long before Findlaech died – Sharon]''' [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SCOTTISH%20NOBILITY.htm#_Toc268450047 (Cawley's Medlands)] 
2 CONT >>>>Sigurd & his second wife had one child:    
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>>5.         [http://www.geni.com/people/Thorfinn-Sigurdsson/6000000001052002306   THORFINN] "the Black" ([1009]-[1060/65], bur Birsay, Christchurch).  Orkneyinga Saga names “Earl Thorfinn” as the son of Sigurd and his wife “th
2 CONC e daughter of Malcolm King of Scots”, adding that his father sent him to Scotland “to be fostered by the King, the boy´s maternal grandfather” when he left for Ireland, and that he was five years old when his father was killed[886
2 CONC ].  Snorre names Thorfin as son of "Sigurd the Thick" & his wife, recording that he was five years old when his father was killed[887].  He succeeded [1030] as sole Jarl of Orkney.  [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SCOTTISH%20NOBI
2 CONC LITY.htm#_Toc268450047 (Cawley's Medlands)]
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>ii)         [http://www.geni.com/people/Svenlaug/6000000003097958681 SVANLAUG or Nereid].  
