2 CONT '''Máel Coluim mac Donnchada''' (Modern Gaelic: Maol Chaluim mac Dhonnchaidh), Anglicised Malcolm III, in later centuries nicknamed Canmore, (c.1031[6] - 13 November 1093), King of Scots. 
2 CONT
2 CONT * Parents: Donnchad mac Crínáin & Suthen
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouses and children:
2 CONT * Ingebjorg Finnsdóttir
2 CONT ** 1. Duncan II of Scotland, suceeded his father as King of Scotland
2 CONT ** 2. Donald
2 CONT * Margaret 'Ætheling' of England
2 CONT ** 1. Edward, killed 1093.
2 CONT ** 2. Edmund of Scotland
2 CONT ** 3. Ethelred, abbot of Dunkeld
2 CONT ** 4. King Edgar of Scotland
2 CONT ** 5. King Alexander I of Scotland
2 CONT ** 6. King David I of Scotland
2 CONT ** 7. Eadgyth of Scotland, also called Matilda, married King Henry I of England
2 CONT ** 8. Mary of Scotland, married Eustace III of Boulogne
2 CONT
