1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Hákon faukr and his family is mentioned in Heimskringla (Hkr) by Snorri Sturluson, Vol 3, chapter 19, page 156 (trans. by Finlay / Faulkes) "There was a powerful landowner called Óláfr in the Dale, a wealthy man. H
2 CONC e lived at Aumorð in Dalr mikli. He had two children. His son was called Hákon faukr (Drifter?), and his daughter Borghildr."
2 CONT
2 CONT Hákon fukr is later mentioned as a hansome but stupid man, who is killed by the men of King Haraldr Gilli (Hkr 3, FF, p. 175). The killing of Hákon faukr mentioned in similar terms by Morkinskinna (Ed. Andersson / Gade, p. 364). N
2 CONC o children of Hákon faukr are mentioned.
