2 CONT After half a century of reign, Olaf I was killed.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Olaf was too young to assume the throne on his fathers death in 1095.  His regent, Domnall Mac Teige was oppressive and was deposed.  Magnus III controlled the Isles via his son, Sigurd III.  Olaf resided in the court of Henry I o
2 CONC f England, learning about Norman administration.  Olaf finally regained Man abt 1111.  He ruled in peace for 40 years, unheard of in this time.  This was because of his powerful fleet that protected the waters.  He established the
2 CONC  Cictercian monastery of Man at Rushen in 1134.  In 1140, his daughter Ragnhild married Somerled, lord of Argyll. At the end of his life, he sent his son, Godred to Norway to pay homage to King Eystein III.  During this time, he w
2 CONC as killed by his nephew, Harald's son Ragnald in an attempt to ursurp the throne.
2 CONT
2 CONT (source - "the mammoth book of British kings and queens" by Mike Ashley.  pp 425-428)
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Olaf was also known as Oláfr II Bitling Godfredsson.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was born before 1095. He was King of Man between 1103 and 1153.
2 CONT
2 CONT See "My Lines"
2 CONT
