1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Ärkebiskop Eskil''' gjorde kyrkan till en del av Europa
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eskil_of_Lund?wprov=sfla1
2 CONT
2 CONT Archbishop Eskil made the church to a part of the rest of Europe Eskil is considered to be one of the great archbishops of Lund. He led the archdiocese of Lund from 1138 until 1177, with some interruptions. Eskil was probably born
2 CONC  about 1100. He belonged to a family which was allied with the Danish royal family. As Archbishop, he was an important ecclesiastical person who founded many monasteries. In the early 1150s Eskil visited the famous Bernard of Clai
2 CONC rvaux and when Eskil 1177  put down his bishop rod, it was to Clairvaux he traveled and spent his last years. Eskil also had his final resting place in the monastery at Clairvaux. Archbishop Eskil's importance was that he helped t
2 CONC he church in the Nordic countries into becaming an integral part of the international church community.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://lundsdomkyrka.se/2014/06/12/arkebiskop-eskil/
2 CONT
2 CONT Nephew of Asger. Was bishop of Roskilde 1134-1137. Consecrated and opened the cathedral in Lund 1145.  After his episcopal ministry he retired at the monastery of Clairvaux.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://sv.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lista_%C3%B6ver_%C3%A4rkebiskopar_och_biskopar_i_Lunds_stift
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT da.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ærkebiskop_Eskil
