1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Gjord Karlsson / Fot=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Son of Karl Gjordsson (Fot) and Helena Ragvaldsdotter
2 CONT * District Chief of Ydre. 
2 CONT * Gjord Karlsson / Fot  was county sheriff in Ydre härad, Småland 1397-1411.
2 CONT * Häradshövdingar: Gjurd Fot 1397−1411 (Rääf 1:62, SD 1437) − Jöns Knutsson (båt) (?1415−)1421−32 (Rääf 1:90, 1:93, 1:100) − Harald Jonsson (fisk)1443−47 (Rääf 1:109, 1:113) − Erengisle Gjurdsson (Fot) 1450−58 (C 4 f 39v,GöHoA 21/
2 CONC 1)1− Sven Nilsson (Grabyätten) 1460−65 (Rääf 1:120, Rääf 3 s 383f) − Nils (Jönsson) Slatte 1496(GiSt s 63) − Jöns Nilsson (Slatte) 1526−41 −Tord Olofsson skrivare 1545 − Christer Persson (Halvhjort av Flishult)1550−51 − Henrik Per
2 CONC sson 1552−57 − Olof Gustavsson (stjärnbjälke) 1559−senast 1568 (ALD 1 s 279).
2 CONT *  A document from 1450 states that Erengisle Nilsson was the county governor of Ydre, which has been interpreted in the literature as Erengisle Nilsson (Hammerstaätten), but the document is only known in a transcript. This is mos
2 CONC t likely a misreading for Erengisle Gjurdsson, son of the predecessor Gjurd Fot and father-in-law of the successor Sven Nilsson (Grabyätten).
2 CONT * In 1383(?) Karl Andersson sells his lots in B and Tångarp to Gjurd Fot (Rääf 1:50). In 1402 Ramborg Magnusdotter (split shield), Peter Bonde's widow, is said to have sold B and Tångarp to Asby prästbord (Widegren 1 p 378).
2 CONT * In 1382, Hemming, dean of Asby, granted to Gjurd Fot and his wife Elin Ragvaldsdotter (split shield with half-fan eagle) a farm K worth half a third (2½) attung. After Elin's death, the farm was to return to the church. The gran
2 CONC t was made with the consent of Erengisle Sunesson (boat), Bo Bosson (Natt och Dag), Ulf Jonsson (Aspenäsätten) and all parishioners (Rääf 1:47). In 1383, Gjurd Fot and Elin Ragvaldsdotter confirmed that they would only hold K duri
2 CONC ng Elin's lifetime, after which it would return to Asby church (Rääf 1:49).
2 CONT * (Graby) The county governor Gjurd Fot lived in Graby in 1391 (Gen 41 f 200), and he collected estates here in 1392−97. It was the manor house of Mikael Magnusson (rafter over leaf) in 1433 (Rääf 1:103) and in 1446−58 for Gjurd F
2 CONC ot's son Erengisle (Rääf 1:112, GöHoA 21/1). In 1482−1506 it was the manor house of Erengisle's son-in-law, the county governor Sven Nilsson (Grabyätten) (Rääf 1:134, 1:142) and in 1512−55 for his daughter Elin (Rääf 1:143, 1:163,
2 CONC  1:168, 1:173). His son Sven Nilsson (Slatte), who died before 1549, is said to have registered here (Gen 41 f 213). His daughter Helga lived here with her husband Tönne Olofsson in the 1560s (AH p 171, GiSt p 62).
2 CONT * In 1403 it is attested that Elin Ragvaldsdotter gave her husband Gjurd Fot a stream at F and two farms in Oppreda (SD 382 after Rääf 1:72)
2 CONT
2 CONT =Married=  
2 CONT
2 CONT *  Married: '''(1st)  Helena Elin Ragvaldsdotter Puke (Bonde)''' already in 1379. In 1383, Elin Ragvaldsdotter (split shield with half fan eagle) with the consent of her husband Gjurd Fot donates Bredgården in A, to the priest's t
2 CONC able in Asby, for the holding of masses (Rääf 1:48).
2 CONT * Married: '''(2) Elin Torstensdotter (oxpanna) ,''' before 1406-07-25. Married 1st 1397-02-05 according to a morning deed to Bengt Arvidsson [Divided shield with three stars] who was alive 1399-02-15, but was † 1400-02-09. Marrie
2 CONC d 2nd about 1403 to the district chief of Ydre district Gjurd Karlsson Foot [Crossbeam with two stars] in his 2nd marriage, † about 1411. In his 1st marriage before 1379 to Helena Ragvaldsdotter [Divided shield with half a fan eag
2 CONC le] in her 2nd marriage. In his 3rd marriage 1408-01-16 according to a morning deed to Elin Jönsdotter , daughter of Jöns Björnsson . Katarina Torstensdotter . before 1406-07-25. Married 1st 1397-02-05 according to a morning deed 
2 CONC to Bengt Arvidsson [Divided shield with three stars] who was alive 1399-02-15, but was † 1400-02-09. Married 2nd about 1403 to the district chief of Ydre district Gjurd Karlsson Foot [Crossbeam with two stars] in his 2nd marriage,
2 CONC  † about 1411. In his 1st marriage before 1379 to Helena Ragvaldsdotter [Divided shield with half a fan eagle] in her 2nd marriage.
2 CONT * Married: '''(3rd) Elin Jönsdotter''' in 1408 . Died not earlier than 1411". Gjurd Fot Häradshövding in Ydre härad, Småland 1397-1411. Married 1st already in 1379 to Elin Ragvaldsdotter. Married 2nd not earlier than 1400 and late
2 CONC st in 1406 to Elin Torstensdotter (oxpanna). (Died (was deceased). In his 3rd marriage 1408-01-16 according to a morning deed to Elin Jönsdotter , daughter of Jöns Björnsson . Katarina Torstensdotter . Married before 1397 to Danie
2 CONC l Nilsson Fargalt , born 1366, † 1402.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Oxenstierna_af_Eka_och_Lind%C3%B6_nr_1 Oxen Trails of Eka and Lindö No. 1, by Adelsvapen Geneologies]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''TAB 3'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Torsten Gjurdsson , † before 1399-02-15. Married before 1370 to Bengta Eriksdotter Sparre . She gave land on 10 February 1404 to the choir of Our Lady in Strängnäs Cathedral.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Children:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Bengta Torstensdotter .''' Was engaged on 10 May 1385 to Ingemund Ingevaldsson [Two Angle Brackets] , to Svepnäs in Näs sn/C.
2 CONT * '''Elin Torstensdotter ,''' † before 1406-07-25. '''Married 1st 1397-02-05 according to a morning deed to Bengt Arvidsson [Divided shield with three stars]''' who was alive 1399-02-15, but was † 1400-02-09. '''Married 2nd about 
2 CONC 1403 to the district chief of Ydre district Gjurd Karlsson Foot [Crossbeam with two stars] in his 2nd marriage, † about 1411.''' In his 1st marriage before 1379 to Helena Ragvaldsdotter [Divided shield with half a fan eagle] in he
2 CONC r 2nd marriage. In his 3rd marriage 1408-01-16 according to a morning deed to Elin Jönsdotter , daughter of Jöns Björnsson .
2 CONT * '''Katarina Torstensdotter .''' Married before 1397 to Daniel Nilsson Fargalt , born 1366, † 1402.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=%22gjord+fot%22&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=2&postid=sdhk_11553&tab=post#tab SDHK-nr: 11553]
2 CONT
2 CONT The Swedish Diplomatarium's main catalog of medieval letters
2 CONT
2 CONT * Dating: 1379 December 13, Issuer: Gjurd Fot and Helena Ragvaldsdotter
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Gjord Fot and Elin Ragvaldsdotter''' give, in order to atone for their sins, to Nydala Kloster upon entering there all their property lots in Nässjö (in Nässjö parish), with all appurtenances, including land dwellers and land d
2 CONC wellers. Nydala monastery must bear half of the avraden from the main farm. The other half, as well as everything from the supplements, will go to Gjord and Elin during their lifetime. The executors dispose of these properties and
2 CONC  their heirs and leave them to the monastery as perpetual property. Gjord and Elin, under the punishment of God and the Church, forbid their surviving heirs, relatives and friends to oppose this open letter and their good will. Th
2 CONC e mentioned properties have not accrued to Elin as the fathers or the mothers, but as her rightful inheritance and by exchange. The issuers ask their priest Peter i Sund and Henrik Svinakula to seal the letter together with them.
2 CONT
2 CONT Original: or. perg. RA 0101 bilder
2 CONT Eftermedeltida avskrifter: Peringskiöld: E 90 reg.; Örnhielm: VIII s. 738
2 CONT Eftermedeltida regest/notis: Notis bland Jonas Bures egenhändiga excerpter ur ”Asken Kylebreff, Bruner och Läijonansichte Footer” i riksarkivet, Genealogica 79, fol. 47, RA: ”Giurder Foter, Hans Hustru Elena RagwaldzDott, Item Hed
2 CONC rich Swinakulla förer ett seinehufwudh medh store tänder”.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=Elin+Ragvaldsdotter&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=12&postid=sdhk_11595&tab=post SDHK no: 11595]
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Dating: 1380 without day'''
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1380, Giurder Foot and his wife Elin a Ragwaldsdotter gave to Sunds church their estate in Vittskögle in Hässleby parish in Häsleby sochn, as well as three m ark of land Probably Ödhult in Ingatorps parish; see OAU. all appurte
2 CONC nances, to witness with seal here r Hemming in Asby Parish, prowast and Mr. Holmsten in Torpa parish.
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Source''' Post-medieval regest/notice:  Note in hs B 22, pag. 87, Linköping City Library, Stiftsbiblioteket (by Bishop AO Rhyzelius in a "Linköping Stifts-Krönika", conceptual notes, which R. kept from around 1722 until his d
2 CONC eath in 1761.); Mentioned by LF Rääf in a letter to LC Wiede, dat 1854 29/4, Br. 53, no. 215, LStB,Printed
2 CONT DS 10087  see pdf of print Printed regest J. Laurenius, De Ydria, I, Diss., Ups. 1736, p. 43 north L. F. Rääf, Collections and notes to a description of Ydre härad i Östergöthland 3 (1861), p. 379, no. 44 ½.) Literature and commen
2 CONC taryRegarding Gjord (Karlsson) Foot, see J. E. Almquist, Lagsagor och domsagor i Sverige I (1954), pp. 278–279.About the dean Hemming in Asby see DMS, Småland 4:6, p. 24, 35 and 46. Regarding the localities in Outer District, see 
2 CONC DMS, Småland 4:6, p. 28 f. (Asby), p. 113 f. (Sund) and p. 147 f. (Torpa). About Vittsjögle see J. Silfving, From northern Småland medeltid (1952), p. 348.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=%22gjord+fot%22&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=4&postid=sdhk_12359&tab=post#tab SDHK-nr: 12359]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''The Swedish Diplomatarium's main catalog of medieval letters'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Date: 1383 February 19, Place of issue: Vadstena'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Gjord Fot and his wife Ælina Ragvaldsdotter''' certify that they hold the estate “Kungzbiærgha” of “Asby” church only during Elin’s lifetime.
2 CONT
2 CONT * Sources: Late medieval copies: (1691 by D. Hadorph) VaLA (Linköpings domkapitels arkiv E IV:1).; B. E. H-d IV (Wiede) Photocopy: DK Printed Rääf: Ydre I no. 49 p. 191 Literature and commentary, See A. Sandberg, Linköpings stifts
2 CONC  kyrkoarkivalier t.o.m. 1800 (1948), p. 591 ff
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=Foot&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=35&postid=sdhk_14130&tab=post SDHK no.: 14130]
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Dating:  1392 December 20, Place of issue: Sund Church''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT Magnus Ömundsson exchanges land in "Grafby" in Sund parish with Gjurd Karlsson Foot for land in "Bordhsiö and Swensthorppe" in Askeryd parish.
2 CONT
2 CONT * Sources: Original:  Or. perg. Dragon Collection RA 0107.04, Post-medieval copies:  (16th century) X 257 d 1, p. 170, UUB, SEAL three Printed, Rääf, Ydre 1, no. 61 p. 203 f.. Literature and commentary, A copy of Rääf is in the co
2 CONC llection; cf. notes by AO Rhyzelius, B 22, pp. 87 and 88, LStB, dated 1393 regarding parish priests Ake and Petrus Plebanus.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=%22gjord+fot%22&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=6&postid=sdhk_39287&tab=post#tab SDHK-nr: 39287]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''The Swedish Diplomatarium's main catalog of medieval letters'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''1400 without day'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Gjord Fot and his wife Elin Rangvaldsdotter sell their estate in "Asenom" in Remmene parish in Kullings härad, a farm in "Fylynö", a mill stream and a farm in "Quaernabiaerghom" in Grolanda parish''' to Johan Simonsson Arvid Jo
2 CONC nsson, Halsten Ingevaldsson, Bengt "Twidzson" seal.
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Sources''' Original: perg. UUB, Literature and commentary, '''Elin Rangvaldsdotter died before 1403 Sept.''' (SD 382) 13830219 and 14110503. Arvid Jonsson, Halsten Ingevaldsson, Bengt "Twidzson" beseglar.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=Elin+Ragvaldsdotter&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=10&postid=sdhk_16167&tab=post SDHK no: 16167]
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Dating: 1403 September, Place of issue: Sund's church''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Peter, priest in Sund, and Holmsten, priest in Asby , certify that Elin Ragvaldsdotter gave her husband Gjurd Fot two farms in Oppreda and a stream at Forsnäs in Sunds sn in Ydre and that the spouses agreed that whoever survive
2 CONC d the other would own the estate all chattels.'''
2 CONT The issuers seal.
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Source:'''Original:  perg., Drake collection. RA 0107.04
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=%22gjord+fot%22&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=8&postid=sdhk_18585&tab=post#tab SDHK-nr: 18585]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''The Swedish Diplomatarium's main catalog of medieval letters'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Date: 1415 August 3, Place of issue: Vadstena'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Karl Magnusson, magistrate in Tiohärad, sells to his nephew Nils Guse on certain conditions everything that his son Magnus Karlsson inherited from '''Gjord Fot's wife Elin Ragvaldsdotter.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Sources''' Original: Or. perg. Bergshammarsamlingen RA 0107.02
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT In my post above, I avoided addressing the question of which weapon Elin Ragvaldsdotter carried - for good reason - as it is very easy to jump to conclusions based on the similarity of weapons. F. island a weapon may have been att
2 CONC ributed to a person who does not belong to the family at all.
2 CONT
2 CONT I still have to address the question, as it is in principle of decisive importance for determining family affiliation.
2 CONT
2 CONT The problem is that so far I have not found any primary source where it is explicitly stated that Elin sealed the document - and that the seal is preserved and unequivocally identified! If anyone has access to such a source, I wou
2 CONC ld be grateful for that information!
2 CONT
2 CONT Raneke gives her shield as 'cleft, l. emerging cleft demi-eagle' [p. 732]. She is listed as known in 1399, which can be interpreted as the year referring to the basis for determining her coat of arms - which in this case probably 
2 CONC refers to the undated document SDHK 15155 - issued by Elin R. attached (addition to?) SDHK 15154 in 1399.
2 CONT
2 CONT The main message in SDHK 15155 is that Elin R. disposes of crop goods after her first husband, Bengt Magnusson and his children. This means that all of them were dead, but that at least one child survived their father, which is wh
2 CONC y Elin inherited all their property as a back inheritance and had free disposal rights over it.
2 CONT
2 CONT There are five seal bags on the letter, of which at least two contain visible seals (see image below). Seal no. 2 must have been the seal attributed to Elin R. of Raneke, as it can probably be interpreted as a cleft half eagle – a
2 CONC  weapon also attributed to a Mattias Bryniolfsson (k. 1385) [Raneke, p. 924], who sold land in Ydre to Bo Jonsson (Grip) and also held property in Asby sn. (Bryniolfsson's coat of arms is described by Rääf [part 1, no. 52] as: "..
2 CONC .an indistinct erect right-facing lizard or some other animal.")
2 CONT
2 CONT Interesting are the coat of arms sketches above seals 3 - 5. They obviously belong to:
2 CONT
2 CONT * 3) '''Nils Magnusson (Röde )''' k. 1374 – 1427. [J Raneke, p. 31]
2 CONT
2 CONT * 4) '''Sten Haraldsson (Stubbe)''' k. 1376 – 1417. [J Raneke, p. 72]
2 CONT
2 CONT * 5) '''Sten Lalasson''' k. 1390 – 1420. [J Raneke p. 427].
2 CONT
2 CONT Nils Magnusson's sister, Christina, was married to Sten Lalasson who had a daughter, Elin, who was married to Filip Bonde - Elin Ragvaldsdotter's uncle I postulated - brother of Ragvald Erengislesson!
2 CONT
2 CONT The Sigillants obviously belonged to the same geosocial cluster as the Bonde/Puke family and ensured Elin Ragvaldsdotter's (Puke?) rights.
2 CONT
2 CONT As Gjurd Karlsson is not mentioned in the letter (SDHK 15155), it seems (?) seal 1) belongs to Elin R rather than seal 2) as she is the issuer - but I am not completely sure. Could it be that seal 2) instead belongs to Mattias Bry
2 CONC niolfsson? You can perhaps sense a couple of hanging feathers in the seal with an angle that is close to Mattia's coat of arms - or?!
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =Sources=
2 CONT
