1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Erengisle Gjordsson / Fot=
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Son of Gjord Karlsson / Fot and Elin Ragvaldsdotter'''
2 CONT *  In a document evidence from 1450, Erengisle Nilsson is stated to be the district governor of Ydre, which in the literature has been interpreted as Erengisle Nilsson (Hammerstaätten), but the document is only known in a copy. Th
2 CONC is is most likely a misreading for Erengisle Gjurdsson, son of the predecessor Gjurd Fot and father-in-law of the successor Sven Nilsson (Grabyätten).
2 CONT * Page. 233 "About Gjurd Fot's son, Erengisle Gjurdsson i Graby, there is only a few pieces of information. Palmskiöld announces that he was the son of Elin Ragvaldsdotter, 'Explanation': Ernegisle Gjurdsson was, based on the hypo
2 CONC thesis, most likely named after his mother's postulated grandfather, Erengisle Petersson (Farmer).
2 CONT * Häradshövdingar: Gjurd Fot 1397−1411 (Rääf 1:62, SD 1437) − Jöns Knutsson (båt) (?1415−)1421−32 (Rääf 1:90, 1:93, 1:100) − Harald Jonsson (fisk) 1443−47 (Rääf 1:109, 1:113) − Erengisle Gjurdsson (Fot) 1450−58 (C 4 f 39v, GöHoA 2
2 CONC 1/1)1 − Sven Nilsson (Grabyätten) 1460−65 (Rääf 1:120, Rääf 3 s 383f) − Nils (Jönsson) Slatte1496 (GiSt s 63) − Jöns Nilsson (Slatte) 1526−41 −Tord Olofsson skrivare 1545 − Christer Persson (Halvhjort av Flishult) 1550−51 − Henrik
2 CONC  Persson 1552−57 − Olof Gustavsson (stjärnbjälke) 1559−senast 1568 (ALD 1 s 279).
2 CONT * '''The county governor Gjurd Fot lived in Graby in 1391 (Gen 41 f 200), and he collected estates here in 1392−97. It was the manor house of Mikael Magnusson (rafter over leaf) in 1433 (1:103) and in 1446−58 for Gjurd Fot's son E
2 CONC rengisle (Rääf 1:112, GöHoA 21/1). In 1482−1506 it was the manor house of Erengisle's son-in-law, the county governor Sven Nilsson (Grabyätten) (Rääf 1:134, 1:142) and in 1512−55 for his daughter Elin (Rääf 1:143, 1:163, 1:168,1:1
2 CONC 73). His son Sven Nilsson (Slatte), who died before 1549, is said to have registered here (Gen 41 f 213). His daughter Helga lived here with her husband Tönne Olofsson in the 1560s (AH p 171, GiSt p 62).'''
2 CONT
