2 CONC s also the progenitor of the Lenhausen-Stockum tribe. ''' Both''' son Heidenreich''' (* around 1402, † around 1474) was a '''squire and heir of the Finnentrop castle complex''', today Altfinnentrop. Around 1433 he married the '''h
2 CONC eiress Angela von Heyen (Heygen) and thus came into joint ownership of the Bamenohl house''' . In 1447 he was able to expand his holdings at Bamenohl. Bamenohl later came into the possession of the Plettenberg-Heeren line (see abo
2 CONC ve)
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Engel von Heygen''', born around 1410 (religion: rK ), died after 1466 , urk. 1438-1466, 1478 dead, '''heiress of Bamenohl and the patronage right of the church of Elspe.'''
