1 NAME Johann Jodokus /Schnier said Honerhans said Hühnerhans/
2 GIVN Johann Jodokus
2 SURN Schnier said Honerhans said Hühnerhans
2 NICK Johann Jodokus Schnier said Honerhans
2 NICK and in 1725 a Johann Schneider
2 NICK said Hühnerhans.
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 21 MAR 1671
1 DEAT
2 DATE 18 APR 1743
2 PLAC Löllinghausen 
2 ADDR
3 STAE Nordrhein-Westfalen
3 CTRY Deutschland
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 1. '''Johann Jodokus SCHNIER said Honerhansen''' 1671-1743
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. In 1669 '''Josten [short for Jodocus] Schneider, known as Honerhans''', was invested with the Hühnerhans-Hof in 1669.
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. In 1700 a '''Jobsten [diminutive of Jodocus] Schnieders, said Honerhans, and in 1725 a Johann Schneider, said Hühnerhans. The name Schneider then disappeared among the tenants of the Hühnerhans-Hof'''
2 CONT
2 CONT 4.  It was their eldest son '''Johann Schnier, said Coers''', born around 1655, who '''inherited the Coershof''' on the death of his father in 1678. Unfortunately, he died two years later. '''He left no children from his marriage 
2 CONC to Maria Catharina Lohmann, said Frisse'''. The Coershof then passed to his '''brother Christian''', who was born around 1656 and died in 1713. From '''his''' marriage to '''Maria Elisabeth Steilmann''', he left many descendants i
2 CONC n the Meschede region, who are still followed to the present day. The descendants of Conrad Schnier also maintained a female line in the Meschede region, where they continued to devote themselves to agriculture
2 CONT until well into the 20th century.
2 CONT
2 CONT        i. '''Maria Catharina LOHMANN'''
2 CONT
2 CONT          Birth: 2. August 1662, Reiste, Hochsauerlandkreis, Nordrhein-Westfalen, Deutschland 	
2 CONT          Death: 7. July 1700, Niedereimer, Hochsauerlandkreis, Nordrhein-Westfalen, Deutschland 	
2 CONT
2 CONT          Parents: Anton LOHMANN and Catharina SCHULTE ZU UENTROP, GEN. FRISSE
2 CONT
2 CONT 5. The name Schemhof then disappeared. We then must jump to 1689 to see a Jobst [diminutive of Jodocus] Schneider, said Honerhansen, invested in Schemhof. In the meantime, the Meschede chapter of the Hühnerhans-Hof, the Hühnerhans
2 CONC  farm in Immenhausen, which is not mentioned in the tax registers of the 16th century, is mentioned as being under the control of the Hühnerhans-Hof
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
