1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Susanna Kittle Phillips BIRTH	4 Jun 1738 Wawarsing, Ulster County, New York, USA DEATH	unknown Randolph County, West Virginia, USA BURIAL	Unknown
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/136239559/susanna-phillips
2 CONT
2 CONT Controversy: She was supposedly married to Thomas Phillips. Genealogy written in the mid 1970s by Calbert Phillips  alleged that Thomas was born in Wiltshire, England, and was married to Susannah Kittle. However, that information 
2 CONC has never been fully verified. (see http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=6426414) Other genealogists claim that she couldn't have been married to Thomas Phillips*.  Also, she is supposedly the sister of Abraham Ke
2 CONC ttle, Sr. (Revolutionary soldier) but some genealogists claim she was a cousin, not a sister**. (?)
2 CONT
2 CONT The birth date listed is actually her baptismal date. Her name is spelled Zusanna on her baptismal record. Susanna was baptized at the Old Dutch Church of Kingston, Ulster County, New York.
2 CONT
2 CONT Susanna "Zusanna" Kittle Kortrecht AKA Cutright, Kortright, Cortregt,  formerly Westbroeck AKA widow of Antony Westbrook (middle name found on other trees- Susanna Nancy Kittle)
2 CONT
2 CONT Wife of 1. Anthony Westbroeck — married August 5, 1757 (until his death, about November 30, 1762) b. 19 May 1738 -1 Child
2 CONT
2 CONT Wife of 2. John Kortrecht (later Cutright) — married November 30, 1762 b. 18 Jun 1734 -5 Children
2 CONT
2 CONT On November 30, 1762 in New York Johannes Cortregt married Susanna Kittle. On his marriage record his name is listed as Johannis Cortregt. Her name is listed as Susanna Kittel, widow of Antony Westbrook. Both resided at Machackeme
2 CONC ck, Port Jervis, Orange County, New York.
2 CONT
2 CONT Johannes died sometime between 1780 and 1782.
2 CONT
2 CONT *Incorrect info- married Thomas Phillips? Her last child by John Kortrecht was born 1 Nov 1870, so she couldn't have been married to Thomas Phillips. All records indicate that her last child was born in NY, so the family possibly 
2 CONC stayed there. 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=136239559
2 CONT
2 CONT Died about 1790, in the rural area between Elkins and Beverly, Randolph County, West Virginia (then Virginia)
2 CONT
2 CONT Siblings: Catharine Kittle, Jeremiah Kittle, Zuveryn Kittel, Elizabeth Kittle, Jerennas Kettel, Jan Kittel, Abraham Kittle Sr. (KETTLE on his gravestone), Catharina Kittel, Lea Kittel, Marcus Kittle, Maria Kittle, Samuel Kittle an
2 CONC d Johanna Kittel
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: Surname Kettle- some records spell it Kittle and the name varies between generations. Apparently, different family members preferred one spelling over another (?) Her brother Abraham used KETTLE.
2 CONT
2 CONT source- http://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Kittle-58
2 CONT
2 CONT Additional info: Susanna "Zusanna" (named after Richard's sister)Wawarsing NY b 4 Jun 1738
2 CONT
2 CONT m#1 5 Aug 1757 Anthony Westbroeck Jr. b 19 May 1738 1 Child
2 CONT
2 CONT m#2 30 Nov 1762 John Kortrecht b 18 Jun 1734 5 Children
2 CONT
2 CONT *Her last child by John Kortrecht was born 1 Nov 1870, so she couldn't have been married to Thomas Phillips. All indications that I have seen indicate that her last child was born in NY, so the family possibly stayed there.
2 CONT
2 CONT **Susannah Nancy Kittle was possibly a cousin to Abraham Kittle Sr. but not his sister.
2 CONT
2 CONT If anyone wishes her children's names, please contact me.
2 CONT
2 CONT Susannah Kittle resided in:
2 CONT
2 CONT Wawarsing, Ulster County, New York
2 CONT
2 CONT Mahackamack (Machackemeck), Port Jervis, Orange County, New York (Deerpark, Minisink Valley)
2 CONT
2 CONT Sussex, Sussex County, New Jersey
2 CONT
2 CONT Between Elkins and Beverly, Randolph County, West Virginia
2 CONT
2 CONT http://boards.ancestrylibrary.com/thread.aspx? mv=flat&m=464&p=localities.northam.usa.states.westvirginia.counties.randolph
2 CONT
2 CONT FORMATION OF SUSSEX TOWNSHIP:
2 CONT
2 CONT Wantage precinct formed on May 30, 1754, from Newton Township, became incorporated as a Township on February 21, 1798. Boundary exchanged were made with Frankfort Township in 1826 and 1834. Portions of Wantage were taken to form D
2 CONC eckertown on October 14, 1891. Deckertown was renamed Sussex Borough in 1902. 
2 CONT
