3 CTRY South Africa
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Lijsbeth Arabus (possibly 'Sabba') - a 'royal' Madagascar slave (argued below, by [https://mansellupham.wordpress.com/2020/03/21/the-dregs-of-the-storm-koddo-and-sabba-two-captured-ethiopian-slave-girls-brought-by-
2 CONC the-french-ship-la-marechale-to-the-cape-of-good-hope-and-the-ships-two-abortive-voyages-to/ Upham] to have been Abyssinisan; & explained succinctly by [https://www.e-family.co.za/ffy/g6/p6297.htm Delia Robertson in ffy] ), b c164
2 CONC 5 in Abyssinia and captured on Madagascar OR near Golfe d'Aden, on the Horn of Africa; < August 1665 Cape Town)
2 CONT
2 CONT Baptized before August 1665 Cape Town. gifted by Admiral  Admiral Gilles de La Roche-Saint-André, to Maria de la Queillerie in 1656 at the Cape;  transaction later revoked  by the Visiting VOC Commissioner Ryckloff van Goens,becau
2 CONC se of the VOC's policy against 'gifting',  & Lijsbeth & sister Cornelia became property of VOC. 
2 CONT
2 CONT # Lijsbeth Sanders  (bapt  2 Mar 1659 - c1743) [POSSIBLE child? by Gerrit Sandersz]
2 CONT # Pieter Willemsz Tamboer van de Caep  (bapt 18 Jul 1660 -1729)
2 CONT # Armosyn de Groote van de Caep (17 Sep 1679 ->13 May 1713)
2 CONT http://www.e-family.co.za/ffy/g6/p6297.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Updated by Mansell Upham; his recent account suggests that she was of Arab origin and was captured in "Abyssinia" -- therefore likely not born in Madagascar. '''see  [https://mansellupham.wordpress.com/2020/03/21/the-dregs-of-t
2 CONC he-storm-koddo-and-sabba-two-captured-ethiopian-slave-girls-brought-by-the-french-ship-la-marechale-to-the-cape-of-good-hope-and-the-ships-two-abortive-voyages-to/  The Dregs of the Storm: KODDO and SABBA – two captured Ethiopian 
2 CONC slave girls brought by the French ship La Maréchale to the Cape of Good Hope] 
2 CONT ''This article salvages an almost forgotten episode of early 17th century French colonial activity in Africa – the two voyages of the ship La Maréchale de la Meilleraye to Madagascar. During its 1st voyage (1656-1657), the ship of
2 CONC floads at the Cape of Good Hope rescued survivors of the Dutch galiot De Tulp (destroyed in a hurricane while on a trading expedition to Madagascar).  The ship also offloads KODDO and SABBA – two Arab slave girls from Abyssinia [E
2 CONC thiopia] – being of the very 1st imported slaves at the Cape who leave a hitherto overlooked legacy – a substantial and documentable progeny amongst South Africa’s so-called ‘White’ and ‘Coloured’ colonially induced communities.''
2 CONC ...
2 CONT
2 CONT '''''Koddo (born 1645) and Sabba (born 1647):  Slave girls from Abyssinia'''
2 CONT Before departing from Table Bay (April 1657), Admiral Gilles de-la-Roche-St André (1621-1668) presents Maria de la Queillerie, wife to Jan van Riebeeck, with two slave girls  – Koddo and Sabba –  in gratitude for Dutch assistance.
2 CONC   Later renamed Cornelia and Lijsbeth, they are two Arab girls from Abyssinia [Ethiopia, Eritrea, Somalia and/or Yemen], aged 12 and 10 years respectively.[30]  They are listed as Cornelia Arabus and Lijsbeth Arabus following thei
2 CONC r settlement at the Cape.[31]  Blommaert states (incorrectly?) that the girls are bartered on Madagascar.[32]  Since both the St Georges and La Maréchale had sailed along the Abyssinian coast and captured a Moorish prize and trade
2 CONC d on Suqutra, the Arab girls would have been obtained during this time.  ''  [https://mansellupham.wordpress.com/2020/03/21/the-dregs-of-the-storm-koddo-and-sabba-two-captured-ethiopian-slave-girls-brought-by-the-french-ship-la-ma
2 CONC rechale-to-the-cape-of-good-hope-and-the-ships-two-abortive-voyages-to/  The Dregs of the Storm: KODDO and SABBA – two captured Ethiopian slave girls brought by the French ship La Maréchale to the Cape of Good Hope -Posted on Marc
2 CONC h 21, 2020 by mansellupham] 
2 CONT
2 CONT Possible mtDNA Haplogroup  L3b3  by triangulated descendents
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.e-family.co.za/ffy/g6/p6297.htm http://www.e-family.co.za/ffy/RemarkableWriting/UL03MadeOrMarred.pdf
