1 NOTE {geni:about_me} NG Kerk, Swellendam, Cape Colony - Marriage Register of 1817
2 CONT
2 CONT Andries Petrus de Jager and Cornelia Gertruida Brits were married at the NG Kerk, Swellendam on  7 September 1817 by presiding minister, Ds J. Spyker. https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3Q9M-CSK6-79XC-Z?i=707&cat=959223
2 CONT
2 CONT Andries exited the Cape Colony from the Gamtoosriver district Uitenhage c.1837. Many of his De Jager relatives trekked along with him.. It appears that they were in Pieter Lafras Uys' party. Later, in the absence of Carel Landman,
2 CONC  who was on Commando he was in charge of the Boers at the Mlaziriver encampment in Natal. Most of the families there were from Somerset or Uitenhage.
