2 CONT * Kortryk, 1699 eienaar van "Klipvallei" in Wagenmakersvallei (Wellington).
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Des Prez in Boucher
2 CONT North-west of Ath is Courtrai in Flanders, a town on the Lys associated with the Des Prez family which reached the Cape on the Schelde in 1688.  Courtrai was held by the French between 1668 and 1678. ..The Des Prez party consisted
2 CONC  of [https://www.geni.com/people/Hercules-SV-PROG/6000000003877602171?through=6000000003422087235  Hercule des Prez], born about the year 1645, his wife [https://www.geni.com/people/Cecilia-SM-PROG/6000000003059183663?through=6000
2 CONC 000003422087235 Cecile (Cecilia) Datis], some five years his junior, and six children: [https://www.geni.com/people/Hercule-b2/6000000003262531813  Hercule], [https://www.geni.com/people/Isabeau-b1-SM/6000000003059183642?through=6
2 CONC 000000003262531813  Elisabeth], [https://www.geni.com/people/Jacquemine-b5-SM/6000000007241708084?through=6000000001952585327  Jacquemine (Jacomina)], [https://www.geni.com/people/Marie-Jeanne-Therond-b4-SM/6000000006402475377  Ma
2 CONC rie-Jeanne], [https://www.geni.com/people/Philippe-b6/6000000003422087235  '''Philippe'''] and [https://www.geni.com/people/Francois-Jean-b4/6000000001288213831?through=6000000003877602171  Francois-Jean]. The place of origin of t
2 CONC he Des Prez family is uncertain, but Athis southwest of Mons may provide a clue to the earliest beginnings of the Datis family. Later generations would certainly not have remained confined to the village from which they presumably
2 CONC  took their name and it is interesting to find in the church registers of Oostburg in the United Provinces a reference in 1748 to the marriage there of a Marie-Catherine Dathee (sic) from the Saint-Quentin generality of Picardy.
2 CONT
2 CONT It is, however, certain that the Des Prez family was living in the Courtrai district when the town was a French possession. The daughter [https://www.geni.com/people/Isabeau-b1-SM/6000000003059183642?through=6000000003262531813  E
2 CONC lisabeth] was baptized in the Sint-Maartens church there on August 31, 1670, with Charles Loridon and Ludovica (Louise) Pittens as godparents. In the same church on July 4, 1677 [https://www.geni.com/people/Francois-Jean-b4/600000
2 CONC 0001288213831?through=6000000003877602171#  Francois-Jean] was christened, taking the name of his godfather Francois Loridon. The godmother on that occasion was Jeanne, or Johanna van Neste, of a family well represented in the loc
2 CONC al church registers.  It is probable that, as with other French-speaking settlers from Flanders, the Des Prez party was at home in the Flemish language.
2 CONT
2 CONT The family must also have lived at some time in Bethune in the province of Artois, since it is known that [https://www.geni.com/people/Marie-Jeanne-Therond-b4-SM/6000000006402475377  Marie-Jeanne des Prez]  was born there. If the 
2 CONC date of her birth, 1675, is correct, this would indicate a temporary move there from Courtrai. ''' It is possible that [https://www.geni.com/people/Philippe-b6/6000000003422087235  Philippe des Prez] was also born in Bethune, as h
2 CONC e gave the name Artois to his farm in the Land van Waveren.  On the other hand, this could be taken to indicate that the Des Prez family had its origins in that province.''' It is also evident that [https://www.geni.com/people/Her
2 CONC cules-SV-PROG/6000000003877602171?through=6000000003422087235   Hercule des Prez] and his wife were once resident in Lille, where [https://www.geni.com/people/Jacquemine-b5-SM/6000000007241708084?through=6000000001952585327  Jacqu
2 CONC emine] was born. Graham Botha gives Courtrai as the birthplace of both [https://www.geni.com/people/Hercules-SV-PROG/6000000003877602171?through=6000000003422087235 Hercule des Prez] and his son of the same name, but no confirmati
2 CONC on of this has been discovered.
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.geni.com/people/Hercules-SV-PROG/6000000003877602171?through=6000000003422087235   Hercule des Prez] and his family were at Flushing in Zeeland by 1686, together with his wife’s brother [https://www.geni.com/people/Ni
2 CONC colas-D-Aties/6000000001634093237?through=6000000003059183663   Nicolas Datis]. On August 29 of that year the two men applied to the municipal authorities to join the Sint- Jans guild of tailors without payment of the usual charge
2 CONC s. The request points to the necessity of guild membership for obtaining remunerative employment as an artisan, as well as to the financial difficulties in which so many refugee families found themselves. It also provides evidence
2 CONC  of the trade followed by the Cape settler, an occupation in keeping with his background in the textile centres of the north-east. The Flushing authorities were prepared to accept the applicants as paying members and to admit them
2 CONC  to citizenship when they had taken the required oath.
2 CONT
2 CONT The refuge in Flushing enabled [https://www.geni.com/people/Hercules-SV-PROG/6000000003877602171?through=6000000003422087235  Hercule des Prez] and his wife to practise openly the Calvinist faith and on February 11, 1688, eight da
2 CONC ys before they sailed with their children on the Schelde, they were given an attestation of membership by the minister and elders of the Walloon church in Flushing. They had, in the words of the document, “fait ouverte profession 
2 CONC de la Religion Reformee, et vescu avec edification au milieu de nous, frequentant les sainctes assemblies et participant au Sacrement de la saincte Cene du Seigneur”. The attestation was signed by the pastor Andre Lombard and, in 
2 CONC the name of his colleagues, by the church elder Daniel de Groot.
2 CONT
2 CONT … The voyage to the Cape on the Schelde brought the Des Prez and Prevost families close. [https://www.geni.com/people/Isabeau-b1-SM/6000000003059183642?through=6000000003262531813  Elisabeth des Prez] stood godmother at the shipbo
2 CONC ard baptism of Jacob Prevost, with the ship’s captain as godfather; [https://www.geni.com/people/Philippe-b6/6000000003422087235 ''' Philippe des Prez'''] was later to marry Charles Prevost’s daughter Elisabeth.
2 CONT
2 CONT *Boucher.M (1981). French speakers at the Cape: The European Background. Pretoria, UNISA. CHAPTER NINE Cape settlers V: from Flanders to Alsace on the turbulent frontier pp269-271
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
