2 CONT
2 CONT VAN EEDEN JAN. - Oldenburg. * 1637, arr. 1662 as junior ship's corporal, later (1688) burgher at Stellenbosch. ~ (1) 1671 Lysbeth Jansz of Amsterdam; (2) 13.6.1688 Maria Russaar of Blois in France. 6 children. + 1704. (C 2, p. 135
2 CONC ; Test. O.C. 1: 36; Inv. O.C. 1: 80; G.R. nr. 105.)
2 CONT ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Jan and Lysbeth were divorced on the 13th June 1688 in Cape Town.
2 CONT
2 CONT *     Birth Date 1654
2 CONT *     Death Date 1742
2 CONT *     First Name Lijsbeth Sanders
2 CONT *     Last Name Herbst
2 CONT *     Suffix SM/PROG
2 CONT *     Maiden Name van de Caap
2 CONT *     Gender Female
2 CONT *     Birth Location Bremen, Deutschland
2 CONT *     Death Location Wellington, Cape Colony
2 CONT
2 CONT See also: http://www.e-family.co.za/ffy/g6/p6951.htm
2 CONT '''
2 CONT Biography - WB'''
2 CONT He and his wife, Lijsbet Jans, were apparently sent back to
2 CONT Europe in March 1677 because of problems caused by her
2 CONT habitual drunkenness (C.G.de Wet, below) and in the muster
2 CONT roll of 1677 they are noted to be ready to leave (VC 39, p.56,
2 CONT 'staet te vertrecken'). He does not appear in the muster rolls
2 CONT of 1678 or 1679 (there are none for 1680 and 1681) but is back
2 CONT in that of 1682, working in partnership with Mattijs Greef,
2 CONT another blacksmith.
2 CONT ('''source: C.G.de Wet, Die Vryliede en Vryswartes in die Kaapse
2 CONT Nedersetting 1657-1707, published 1981, page 174).'''
2 CONT ( The marriage ended in divorce in May 1684, on
2 CONT grounds of her adultery.
2 CONT source: C.G.de Wet, Die Vryliede en
2 CONT Vryswartes in die Kaapse Nedersetting 1657-1707,
2 CONT published 1981, page 175.)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''See:''' http://www.e-family.co.za/ffy/g6/p6951.htm
