2 CONT
2 CONT Legal married names must be recorded in the Last Name field.
2 CONT Before the 1800 government change in SA, married females from the continent (France, Holland, Germany) are unlikely to have used their husband’s surnames, so this field may be left open if they died before 1800.However, British re
2 CONC cords most often show a woman's married name after 1600 (and as early as 1200). Mike Stangel has asked us to represent the documentation possibilities accurately. So do not delete any SA married names after 1800 in order to replac
2 CONC e them with Maiden Names (And do not delete British Married names after 1600, unless you know for a fact that the woman did not assume her husband’s surname). Just set your Viewing Preferences in order not to view the Married Name
2 CONC / Last Name field / Surname, if you don't wish to see them.
2 CONT
