2 CONT Death notice 1760 filed under Roggeveldt
2 CONT See under media
2 CONT Died 1760 de Berenfonteyn , Roggeveldt  , Drakenstein, Cape of Good Hope 
2 CONT
2 CONT Drakenstein (Paarl) Baptism Record - See Sources
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3Q9M-C9BY-H975?i=716 Inventory 27 November 1760]
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT b5 - GISA  CD   SAF  CD v 9
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT A  burger van Drakenstein. He was a corporal in the dragonders (1730-1740) and later a farmer near Ceres (Cape)  where he produced vegetables, fruit, mutton, wool, grain, wine, brandy and nuts.
2 CONT
2 CONT He farmed on his own loan farms "Uitkomst" (in the present day Ceres district near Karoopoort in the Agter Bokkeveld) and "Beerenfontein" (in the Roggeveld above Kamsberg, the present day district of Sutherland south of town); bot
2 CONC h these towns were then part of the Drakenstein district.
2 CONT
2 CONT According to SA Genealogies''' he had a voorkind with Catharina Hoffman, presumably a slave and daughter of Johannes Hoffman (*Langenberg, Duitsland, 1698).'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Died: natural causes
2 CONT --------------------
