1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Here is the extract about the second baptized child of Douwe GERBENS of which we have records:
2 CONT
2 CONT Gerben DOUWES: (The surname according to Frisian custom at the time is derived from the first name of the father = patronym.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Leeuwarden, dopen, doopjaar 1663
2 CONT
2 CONT Dopeling: Gerben
2 CONT
2 CONT Gedoopt op 25 oktober 1663 in Leeuwarden
2 CONT
2 CONT Kind van Douwe Gerbens en niet genoemde moeder
2 CONT
2 CONT Gestandaardiseerde namen (voornaam en patroniem):
2 CONT
2 CONT Dopeling  : GERBEN of GERBRICHJE
2 CONT
2 CONT Vader   : DOUWE GERBENS
2 CONT
2 CONT Bron:
2 CONT
2 CONT Collectie Doop-, Trouw-, Begraaf- en Lidmaatboeken (DTBL)
2 CONT
2 CONT Herv. gem. Leeuwarden, doop 1654-1667
2 CONT
2 CONT Inventarisnr. : 931
2 CONT
2 CONT Op microfiche beschikbaar op studiezaal Tresoar
2 CONT
2 CONT Wijzigingsdatum: 19-12-2006
2 CONT
2 CONT I think it is highly probable that Gerben GERBENS also was a son of Douwe GERBENS. 
2 CONT
2 CONT However, if he was, why was he not mentioned in the 1687 will of his father?  Most feasible explanation would be that he died at a young age.
2 CONT
2 CONT A search in the electronic archives of Tresoar.nl has not shown any records about his death and/or burial have been found thus far.
2 CONT
2 CONT More research is needed... Very interesting would be to do a full genealogical research on the descendants of Age Douwes to see if one could find some living descendants. Their DNA could be genealogically compared with the DNA of 
2 CONC living descendants of Jacobus Steyn *c.1683 If they are significantly similar, then one would be able to conclude that Jacobus was the biological son of Douwe Gerbrand Steyn. If they are dissimilar, one would know that Jacobus was
2 CONC  the adopted son but not the biological son of Douwe. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Lodewyk Christiaan 'Chris' STEYN
