2 CONT Bredasdorp 1838
2 CONT Cape - (post 1994 Western Cape)
2 CONT //www.geni.com/images/transparent.gif
2 CONT The town of Bredasdorp was founded with the building of a Dutch Reformed Church in 1838 on the farm Langefontein. The town was named after Michiel van Breda, the first Mayor of Cape Town, who was also known as the father of South 
2 CONC Africa's merino sheep industry. Van Breda and Pieter Voltelyn van der Byl could not agree on a location for the church; as a result two churches were built, and two towns, Bredasdorp and Napier, were established.
2 CONT
