1 NOTE Disguised as violinist during flight from Merindol to Lausanne, Frankfurt-am-Main (10/1687) and then Netherlands.  Left for Cape 20/3/1688 aboard Berg China (4/8/1688).  Farmed in partnership with Jourdans.  Owned La Motte, Olipha
2 CONC ntshoek. Owned La Rhone, Drakenstein; Ezels Kloof and Rhebokskloof, Paarl; Morgenster, Cloetenburg, De Kromme Rivier, De Faisante- kraal.  Elder, Deacon, member of Stellenbosch church council. Name derived from Waldensian origins 
2 CONC in Piedmont Valley = heretic/brigand. Granted La motte 18/12/1713
