1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Jan Cornelisz, van Outbeijerland 'Jan Bombam' (c1646 -1713)'''
2 CONT x 22 May 1672 Catarina Harmensz (c1650,Rhenen -)
2 CONT *Trijntie Cornelisz (<12 May 1675-)
2 CONT *Cornelis Cornelisz (29 Nov 1676 -)
2 CONT *Anna Cornelisz (<29 Mar 1680 -)
2 CONT xx 11 July 1683 Maria Kickers (div.1700)
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ='''Birth'''
2 CONT Oud Beijerland, Hoeksche Waard, Zuid-Holland
2 CONT Oud Beijerland is een stadje in de Hoekse Waard, een van de Zuid Hollandse eilanden ten zuiden van Rotterdam. Oud Beijerland is de grootste plaats van het eiland en heeft als zodanig een centrumfunctie voor de regio. - http://www.
2 CONC jackbazen.nl/Nederland/
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ='''Huwelik met Catharina Harmansz SM/PROG'''
2 CONT NGK Kaapstad 
2 CONT >den 22 May [1672'''] Jan Cornelisz jongh-man''' geboortigh van out-beyerland, met''' Catharina Harmansz van Rhenen"
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ='''Huwelik met  Maria Kickers SM/PROG'''
2 CONT NGK Kaapstad : https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-89ML-49Y7-J
2 CONT >ao' '''1683''' eodem dito (den 11 Julii) Jan Cornelisz van Outbeierlant vryman, en Maria Kickers Jonge dochter. 	
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ='''Baptism''' 
2 CONT http://www.eggsa.org/sarecords/index.php/church-registers/cape-town...
2 CONT '''Note''': as far as I can see  - this is rather the baptism of '''the son Theunis''' - not his father! His real biological dna father, though dna testng, shows he is Fredrich Appel's son '''not''' Jan Cornelisz's son!
2 CONT Den 15 dito (April)
2 CONT Theunis
2 CONT Jan Cornelis van Outbeierlant en Maria Kicker[t]s
2 CONT (no witnesses) 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ='''Egskeiding: Maria Kickers''' SM/PROG
2 CONT Cabo de Goede Hoop
2 CONT >Vrijdag den 22' Januarij 1700
2 CONT >Jan Cornelisze van Oudbeijerland vrijburger aan Stellenbosch woonagtig, eijscher in cas van divorcie.>Contra>desselfs huijsvrouw Maria Kickers ged[aagd]e>...
2 CONT
2 CONT {{https://www.geni.com/media/proxy?media_id=6000000221120485985&size=large}}
2 CONT https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000123663725823
2 CONT
2 CONT '''>'''De gedaagdesse antwoordende, segt en bekendt all hare kinderen staande huwelijck, niet bij den eij[se]r haren man; (vermits desselvs onbequaamheijdt) maar bij een ander, te weeten den voorn[oemde] '''Frederick Boot, te hebb
2 CONC en geprocrëeer'''t ...'''
2 CONT '''
2 CONT ...
2 CONT
2 CONT >Den E.A. Rade van Justitie, partijen gehoort, soo meede de genoemde Frederick Boot die het voor[zegde] feijt rondelijck confesseerde, en gelet op der gedaagdessen eijge vrijwillige confessie, doend regt &a, separeert de banden va
2 CONC n hun eij[se]rs en gedaagdesses huwelijck, en gemeenschap van goederen, admitteert den eij[se]r met een andre te mogen trouwen, en cond[emneer]t de gedaagdesse in de costen.
2 CONT
2 CONT >Int Casteel de Goede Hoop datum ut s[upra]
2 CONT >mij present
2 CONT
2 CONT >Melchior Kemels
2 CONT >[rt] & secret[ari]s
2 CONT >1700.
2 CONT
2 CONT [Record of Divorce Proceedings, (folio) 77; CJ 3-22, Court of Justice; Court of Justice, Western Cape Archive Repository on http://www.e-family.co.za/ffy/p7773.htm]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://www.geni.com/people/Theunis-Botha/6000000005788458301?through=6000000001580940776 Theunis Botha], b bef 15 April 1686. Called Botha after his mother, [http://www.geni.com/people/Maria-Kickers/4705796237050024653?through=60
2 CONC 00000005788458301 Maria Kickers]' , 1700 divorce from [http://www.geni.com/people/Jan-Cornelisz/4141861275630023780?through=4705796237050024653 '''Jan Cornelisz'''] (who is '''shown as his father on the birth certificate'''). At w
2 CONC hich time  she said her 7 children were [http://www.geni.com/people/Friedrich-Botha-SV-PROG/5356428241620125193?through=4705796237050024653 Frederich Botha]'s. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''However, a recent DNA  [http://repository.up.ac.za/bitstream/handle/2263/32007/Greeff_Appel(2013).pdf?sequence=1 study  by  the University of Pretoria]  reveal him to have been the biological son of [http://www.geni.com/people/
2 CONC Ferdinandus-Appel-b2/6000000001580940776?through=6000000005788458301 Ferdinandus Appel].''''''
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.e-family.co.za/ffy/g5/p5169.htm
2 CONT This link shows '''Jan Cornelisz had a daughter with Maria Kikkers - Catryna baptized 1690, Cape Town - https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-89ML-49TG-2?i=23'''
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.myheritage.com/research/record-40001-981766681/jan-cornelisz-in-familysearch-family-tree FamilySearch Family Tree] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Oct 6 2020, 22:26:56 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Re the divorce and relations between Appel x Botha x Cornelitz and Kickers'''
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/Appel-Botha-Cornelitz-%3A-the... '''In 1683 Maria Kickers and Jan Cornelitz got married''' in Cape Town. Today, 330 years later, the living patrilineal descendants of Maria’s four sons, number
2 CONC  in excess of 76,000 people. Curiously, '''none of them carry the surname Cornelitz''' – in fact, they are all called Botha and include former President P. W. Botha, general Louis Botha and Minister Pik Botha. The reason for this 
2 CONC anomaly is also the reason why '''Jan got divorced from Maria in 1700'''. According to Maria’s testimonies she did indeed have a '''long term relationship with Frederik Botha''', '''but in her defence she claimed that her husband 
2 CONC '''was impotent''' and that he actually encouraged her. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Other witnesses, presumably prompted by Jan, gave testimonies that implied that Maria was in fact licentious.''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT We combined haplotyping with the AmpFlSTR® YfilerTM kit with deep-rooting genealogies to show that''' Maria’s first son was actually fathered by Ferdinandus Appel''' and that roughly half the living Bothas (38,000 people) actually
2 CONC  descend from ''''''Ferdinandus Appel''' while the remaining three sons all stem from the same father, presumably''' Frederik Botha''', and '''this implies that Maria’s husband did not father any of her sons.'''
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ='''Dood'''
2 CONT Stellenbosch
2 CONT
2 CONT >1/STB 12/17 (36) "kerkelijke gerechtigheden” (begrafnisgelde) aan die koster betaal 1713 Jan Cornelisz van Oudbeijerland f6
2 CONT
2 CONT op http://www.heemkring.org.za/Eerste%20Kerkhof.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT Aan d' E. Compe. nogh ten agteren zijn
2 CONT
2 CONT Cabo de Goede Hoop
2 CONT
2 CONT >Dingsdagh den 13e September 1718, voormiddags.
2 CONT
2 CONT >Den land-drost, Sr. Jacob Voet, ingevolge de ordres van den Wel Edele Heer Gouverneur en voorige besluijten van desen Raad ten dien subjecte genomen, zigh geinquireert hebbende naer soodanige menschen als tot nogh toe aan de leen
2 CONC ingh rol diverse penningen schuldigh en onder de districten van Stellenbosch en Drakensteijn sorteerende waren, ende dies bevindinge in geschrifte den hoogh gem. Edele Heer Gouverneur ter handen gesteld zijnde, heeft Zijn Edele 't
2 CONC  selve in Raade geproduceert, bestaande in desen inhoud:
2 CONT >Volgens extract uijt de leeningh rollen zouden d' ondergesche. uijt dien hoofde aan d' E. Compe. nogh ten agteren zijn de daar voor g'extraheerde sommen, namentlijk:
2 CONT
2 CONT >...
2 CONT
2 CONT >Jan Conelisz. van oud Beijerland, wiens wede., door de wandelingh '''Maria Bombam gent'''., in leeven en desselfs''' dogter getrouwt is met Jan Barentsz. Siger, als mede nogh drie sonen, Theunis, Jacobus en Willem Bota.... ƒ81:05
2 CONC :-'''
2 CONT
2 CONT [Resolutions of the Council of Policy of Cape of Good Hope Cape Town Archives Repository, South Africa Reference code: C. 47, pp. 32-42. on http://databases.tanap.net/cgh/]
2 CONT ----
