2 CONT
2 CONT If anyone has information about when Jacobus b4-c3 died please add it to the profile basics and perhaps add the source to these notes.  [See below - JS]
2 CONT
2 CONT Name	Jacobus Botha De Jonge
2 CONT Sex	Male
2 CONT Spouse's Name	Sophia Van Rooyen
2 CONT Spouse's Sex	Female
2 CONT Event Type	Marriage
2 CONT Event Date	26 Apr 1739
2 CONT Event Place	Paarl, Cape Province, South Africa
2 CONT
2 CONT Never called Hercules !
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3Q9M-CSKD-F3FZ?i=461&cc=1478678  Death notice 1784]
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3Q9M-C9BB-MDZK?i=81 Inventory 14 February 1784]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT There were 2 Jacobus Bothas - both baptised on the same day - 8/8/1717. The first, the son of Theunis Botha and Maria Magdalena Snyman, married Amerentia Potgieter. I have noted him as b1-c4. The second, the son of Jacobus Botha a
2 CONC nd Elsie Snyman, married Sophia van Rooyen. I have noted him as b4-c3. - June Barnes/Buchanan
2 CONT
2 CONT b1-c4 - Baptism - Drakenstein - https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3Q9M-CSV8-W944-4?cat=993681
2 CONT
2 CONT b4-c3 - Baptism, Stellenbosch - https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:S3HY-6LWK-MJ?i=66&cc=1478678
2 CONT
2 CONT -----------
2 CONT
2 CONT Inventaris van de boedel van '''Jacobus Boota de jonge''' overleeden den 14:n Februarij anno 1784.
2 CONT
2 CONT De opstal van een leenings plaatz gen: de Goede Moeds Fontyne geleegen in het Outenikwas Land
2 CONT
2 CONT [His inventory lists one Farmhouse on the loan farm called De Moeds Fontyne, situated in Outeniqualand. This was most likely an out post run by the one male and two female slave listed (not named) since the furniture consists of o
2 CONC ne bed, one table and a chair.}
2 CONT
2 CONT married 26 April 1739 at Drakenstein, to Sophia van Rooijen ...
2 CONT
2 CONT     De ondergeteekende als getuygen bij het naesien van boovengemelde boedel.
2 CONT
2 CONT     Jan Willem Barkhuijsen
2 CONT
2 CONT     Jirrie Louw
2 CONT
2 CONT - Inventories of the Orphan Chamber Cape Town Archives Repository, South Africa Reference no.: MOOC8/18.87 on http://databases.tanap.net/mooc/
