1 BAPM
2 DATE 24 MAR 1694
2 ADDR
3 STAE Caep de Goede Hoop
3 CTRY South Africa
1 DEAT
2 DATE BEF 8 MAY 1750
2 PLAC Swartland
2 ADDR
3 STAE Caap de Goede Hoop
3 CTRY South Africa
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} See http://www.ballfamilyrecords.co.uk/lombard/I028.html
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Anthonij Lombard 1  farmer 2  of Droogevalley in the Paardeberg 3  private in the burger infantry, Drakenstein (1719)  born circa 1693  died circa 1750 4
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes: The children are given as found in the Inventory and Deceased Estate Accounts of their mother, dated May 1755.
2 CONT
2 CONT In the above accounts are listed various properties. The farm Drogevalij in the Paardeberg would seem, from the furnishings, to have been their main home, but they also had a well furnished house in the Table Valley of Cape Town, 
2 CONC and five other farms: Voorspoed in Riebeek Casteel, Bruijntjes Rivier at Klipheuvel, Keurbooms Rivier in that area, Vette Rivier situated on that river and another called Vette Rivier not far from the first. They also owned a grav
2 CONC e plot or vault ('een grafsteede) in the church at Swartland.
2 CONT
2 CONT The inventory of the estate suggest they were very comfortably off, with two slaves in the Cape Town house and 32 slaves on the farms, a quantity of gold and silver objects, a total of 305 cattle, 2000 sheep and 36 horses.
2 CONT
2 CONT The house at the Cape and that at Drogevallij both consisted of a Voorhuis (main room) with a room on each side and a kitchen, but the farmhouse had also a Corn store, a workshop, a cellar, a stable and a yard.
2 CONT
2 CONT The farm Drooge Valliej was bought from the deceased estate of Maria van der Westhuisen for 5000 gulden, 23 Nov. 1734.
2 CONT
2 CONT for a note on his parentage see below# married 7 February 1717 at Drakenstein 5
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Three LOMBARD brother arrive with the Huegenotes in the Cape.  Antoin was the eldest.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
