3 NOTE Raymond, I've just seen this. Yes it would be interesting to research Maria's origins.
3 NOTE Aagh!  Why is there no editing function in this program?  Michael George was born at the end of the eighteenth century, not the seventeenth.  And 'ma' should be 'me', of course.
3 NOTE This accords precisely with what I have always understood about the original South African Doubell.  One thing intrigues ma, though.  Is it not a bit strange that his mother's name was 'Maria'?  'Mary' would be far more likely in 
4 CONC the case of a seventeenth-century Englishwoman.  Perhaps she wasn't English?  Perhaps, because the name, 'Maria' was common in the Eastern Cape, there was an error in the Death Certificate?  Or perhaps she was indeed given a more 
4 CONC 'Continental' version of the name by her parents.
