1 NOTE {geni:about_me} NO ACTUAL SOURCE WHEN AND WHERE HE DIED !
2 CONT
2 CONT 1776 Marriage in CAPE Town not Plettenberg bay established 1779 only !!
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3Q9M-CSFQ-SRLV?view=index&action=view Marriage Cape Town 1776]
2 CONT
2 CONT STROEBEL or STROBEL GEORG HEINRICH (S Strobel). – Hünern. Arr. 1764 as so., farmhand 1769-79, b. 1779. ~ 27.10.1776 Martha Botha. 13 children. (GMR 1764-68; CJ 1153a: 27; CJ 1155: 35; Rq. 1779: 22; G.R. nr. 934.)
2 CONT
2 CONT - Dr. J. Hoge, Personalia of the Germans at the Cape, 1652-1806, Archives Year Book for South African History (Cape Town: Government Printer, Union of South Africa, 1946)
2 CONT
2 CONT NB - There is no evidence whatsoever that he was ever married to a Pienaar lady. All the children were brought to church for their baptism by George Heinrich Stroebel and Martha Botha - finally confirmed by the baptism of the last
2 CONC  child Johannes Christoffel on 16 Oct 1803. NB - We've also been deceived by a careless transcription mistake in SAG... There was NO b3 Cornelia Magdalena born c. 1779. There is only one Cornelia Magdalena baptised in 1797. [Note 
2 CONC 1779 and 1797!!] Hence they had 14 children, NOT 15.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------------------------
2 CONT VOC record: https://www.nationaalarchief.nl/onderzoeken/index/nt00444/d4ff24ec-c864-11e6-9d8b-00505693001d?searchTerm=strobel
2 CONT
2 CONT Voornaam opvarende: George
2 CONT Patroniem opvarende: Hendrik
2 CONT Achternaam opvarende: Strobel
2 CONT Herkomst opvarende: Hinderen
2 CONT Datum indiensttreding: 1764-05-18
2 CONT Functie bij indiensttreding: Soldaat
2 CONT Uitleg over functie: Militair
2 CONT Uitgevaren met het schip: Amerongen
2 CONT Datum uit dienst: 1772-08-12
2 CONT Waar uit dienst: Kaap de Goede Hoop
2 CONT Reden uit dienst: Vrijburger
2 CONT
2 CONT The bay housed a barracks for the Dutch East India Company in 1776. The Governor of the Cape, Baron Joachim van Plettenberg, renamed the town Plettenberg Bay in 1779
