1 NOTE     * OCCUPATION: Konge i Norge 1066-1069
2 CONT     * BIRTH: ABT 1049, (oppvokst i Ranrike (Götaland) ?)
2 CONT     * DEATH: 28 Apr 1069, Trondheim (av reveormsott) 
1 NOTE SOURCE NOTES:
2 CONT       Occupation:  King in Norway
2 CONT       King 1066 - 1069.
1 NOTE Konge fra 1066 til 1069.
1 NOTE Hans sønn, Håkon Toresfostre, ble konge i 1093 sammen med sin fetter, Magnus III Olavsson Berrføtt, men døde allerede året etter.
2 CONT
2 CONT Joint king of Norway with his brother Olaf III Haraldsson, from 1066 until 1069. He was a son of Harald III Haraldsson.
2 CONT
2 CONT From Snorre Sturlasson: Saga of Harald Hardrade:
2 CONT
2 CONT "105. KING MAGNUS'S DEATH.
2 CONT
2 CONT King Magnus Haraldson ruled over Norway the first winter after King Harald's death (A.D. 1067), and afterwards two years (A.D. 1068-1069) along with his brother, King Olaf. Thus there were two kings of Norway at that time; and Mag
2 CONC nus had the northern and Olaf the eastern part of the country. King Magnus had a son called Hakon, who was fostered by Thorer of Steig in Gudbrandsdal, who was a brother of King Magnus by the mother's side; and Hakon was a most ag
2 CONC reeable man.
2 CONT
2 CONT After King Harald Sigurdson's death the Danish king Svein let it be known that the peace between the Northmen and the Danes was at an end, and insisted that the league between Harald and Svein was not for longer time than their li
2 CONC ves. There was a levy in both kingdoms. Harald's sons called out the whole people in Norway for procuring men and ships, and Svein set out from the south with the Danish army. Messengers then went between with proposals for a peac
2 CONC e; and the Northmen said they would either have the same league as was concluded between King Harald and Svein, or otherwise give battle instantly on the spot. Verses were made on this occasion, viz.: --
2 CONT
2 CONT "Ready for war or peace,
2 CONT King Olaf will not cease
2 CONT From foeman's hand
2 CONT To guard his land."
2 CONT
2 CONT So says also Stein Herdison in his song of Olaf: --
2 CONT
2 CONT "From Throndhjem town, where in repose
2 CONT The holy king defies his foes,
2 CONT Another Olaf will defend
2 CONT His kingdom from the greedy Svein.
2 CONT King Olaf had both power and right,
2 CONT And the Saint's favour in the fight.
2 CONT The Saint will ne'er his kin forsake,
2 CONT And let Svein Ulfson Norway take."
2 CONT
2 CONT In this manner friendship was concluded between the kings and peace between the countries. King Magnus fell ill and died of the ringworm disease, after being ill for some time. He died and was buried at Nidaros. He was an amiable 
2 CONC king and bewailed by the people."
2 CONT
2 CONT Acceded: King of Norway, 1066.
1 NOTE He ruled from 1067 to 1068. He died of the "ringworm" plague.
1 NOTE He ruled from 1067 to 1068. He died of the "ringworm" plague.
1 NOTE Magnus Haraldsson eller Magnus II (født 1048, død 1069) var konge av Norge 1066 til 1069, det meste av tiden var han samkonge med broren Olav Kyrre (Olav III Haraldsson Kyrre).
2 CONT
2 CONT Magnus II Haraldsson var sønn av kong Harald Hardråde, og skal ifølge sagaene ha vært med på hærferd mens han ennå var barn. Det antas[1], men virker likevel påfallende, at han var den Magnus som nevnes i en angelsaksisk krøni
2 CONC ke fra 1058; da han skal ha ledet en flåte fra Norge til Wales og hjulpet kongen der til å jage bort en engelsk jarl. Derimot er det rimelig sikkert at han fulgte faren mot Danmark i 1062, en ferd som endte med seier i Slaget ve
2 CONC d Niså i Halland.
2 CONT
2 CONT Magnus ble kronet til konge da faren i 1066 dro mot England. Dette innebar at Magnus var enekonge i Norge fra sommeren 1066 til våren 1067. Broren Olav, som hadde fulgt faren til England vendte hjem våren 1067 og de to delte rik
2 CONC sstyret i vennskap. Selv om de i prinsippet rådde likt over hele riket, tyder mye på at Magnus hadde ansvaret for Vest-Norge, Trøndelag, Opplandene og Nord-Norge, mens Olav rådde over Viken. Magnus ble tidligere ikke regnet med
2 CONC  til kongerekken; delvis fordi han døde ung og bare hadde kort tid som enekonge; og delvis fordi broren som regjerte i mer enn 25 år var den som i realiteten rakk å prege tiden og riket etter kong Haralds død.
2 CONT
2 CONT Magnus døde 20/21 år gammel. Dødsårsaken var i følge sagaen ringorm, men det er mer trolig at det var meldrøyeforgiftning (ergotisme)[2].
2 CONT
2 CONT Magnus' sønn Håkon var i en drøyt år samkonge med fetteren Magnus Berrføtt før han - som sin far - døde ung.
