2 CONT 4.         [https://www.geni.com/people/Gerberge-countess-of-Anjou/6000000004533604973?through=6000000009909505293 GERBERGE] d'Anjou (974 or before-after 1 Apr 1040).  The Chronicle of Adémar de Chabannes records the marriage of "
2 CONC comes…Engolismæ Willelmus" and "Girberga sorore comitis Fulconis"[106].  The Historia Pontificum et Comitum Engolismensis names "Giberta sorore comitis Guillermi Andegavensis" as wife of "Guillermus Comes Engolismensis"[107].  "Ga
2 CONC ufredus et uxor mea Petronilla" donated property "ecclesiam Sancti Pauli…in Sanctonensi territorio subter castrum…Botavilla" to Sauvigny on the advice of "Vuillelmi comitis Engolismensis et uxoris eius dominæ Girbergiæ patris…mei 
2 CONC et matris et domini Elduini fratris mei" by charter dated before 1028[108].  m (before 1000) GUILLAUME IV Comte d'Angoulême, son of ARNAULD "Mancer" Comte d'Angoulême & his first wife Raingarde --- ([978]-murdered 6 Apr 1028, bur 
2 CONC Angoulême Saint-Cybard).  He was poisoned by his daughter-in-law Alaisia.    
