2 CONT 1.         ADELAIS [Judith] ([1000]-7 Jul [after 1030]).  Guillaume de Jumièges records that Duke Richard and Judith had three daughters, of whom one named Adelise married "Renaud comte de Bourgogne"[170].  Orderic Vitalis records
2 CONC  her marriage and calls her amita of William I King of England[171].  "Otto comes qui nominatur Willelmus" issued a charter dated 2 Nov 1023 subscribed by "Raynardi comitis, Adheleydis uxoris eius"[172].  "Raynaldi comitis, Adhele
2 CONC ys uxoris eius" subscribed the charter dated 1030 by which "Robertus regis Roberti filius et regis Henrici filii eius germanus…Burgundie Dux" restored property to Cluny[173].  "Raginaldus comes comitis Guillelmi filius" donated pr
2 CONC operty to the abbey of Flavigny by charter dated 18 May 1037 subscribed by "Iudid comitisse uxoris eius, Guillelmi filii eius, Hugonis filii eius…"[174].  "Iudid comitisse" is assumed in traditional genealogies[175] to have been t
2 CONC he same person as Adelais.  However, it is also possible that she was Comte Renaud's second wife, Adelais having died earlier.   m (before 1 Sep 1016) [as his first wife,] RENAUD de Mâcon, son of OTHON I GUILLAUME Comte de Mâcon [
2 CONC Bourgogne-Comté] & his first wife Ermentrude de Roucy ([990]-3/4 Sep 1057, bur Besançon).  He succeeded his father in 1026 as RENAUD I Comte Palatin de Bourgogne. 
