2 CONT [edit] Other marriages / children
2 CONT
2 CONT Traditionally, Richard had a third wife named Astrid (Estritha), daughter of Sweyn Forkbeard, King of England, Denmark, and Norway, and Sigrid the Haughty. This is extremely unlikely, however, given the political situation.
2 CONT
2 CONT An illegitimate daughter of Richard I, sometimes called "Papia", is also at times given as a daughter of Richard II. Tancred de Hauteville's two wives Muriella and Fredensenda are likewise given as daughters of "Duke Richard of No
2 CONC rmandy", referring to either Richard I or Richard II.
2 CONT
2 CONT Richard II 'le Bon'
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of Richard I 'Sans-Peur and Gunnor de Crèpon
2 CONT
2 CONT Married Judith de Bretagne (996), by whom he had the following issue:
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Richard (c.997), duke of Normandy
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Robert (999), duke of Normandy
2 CONT
2 CONT     * William, monk at Fécamp, died 1025
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Adélaide, married Renaud I, Count of Burgundy
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Eleanor (or perhaps Ainor or Judith), married Count Baldwin IV of Flanders
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Matilda, d.1033
2 CONT
2 CONT Secondly he married Poppa, by whom he had the following issue:
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Mauger, Archbishop of Rouen
2 CONT
2 CONT     * William , count of Arques
