1 NOTE
2 CONT Robert contributed to the restoration of Henry King of France to his throne, and received from the gratitude of that monarch, the Vexin, as an additional to his patrimonial domains. In the 8th year of his reign, curiosity or devot
2 CONC ion induced him to undertake a pilgrimage to the Holy Land, where the fatigues of he journey and the heat of the climate so impaired his consitution he died on his way home.
2 CONT
2 CONT Some sources call him Robert I the Magnificent!
