2 CONT
2 CONT Duke of Normandy (1026-27, or 1027), son of Richard II the Good. He was succeeding in quelling the revolt of his brother, Robert, when he died opportunely, perhaps of poison, making way for his brother's succession as Robert I.
2 CONT
2 CONT d. , Feb. 3, 1027
2 CONT
