1 NOTE Saxon kings. When Edward "the Confessor" died in 1066, William of
1 NOTE For hundreds of years before 1066, England had been ruled by Anglo-
1 NOTE Normandy saw his chance for a successful invasion of England. He
1 NOTE Entered into hostilities with Emporer Otho II and aquired from that monarchValenciennes and the Isles of Zealand. He subseqently further increased histerritories by another rich accession, that of the citadel of Ghent.
