1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rozala_of_Italy ''(27 languages)''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Rozala of Italy''' (also known as '''Rozala of Lombardy''', '''Rozala of Ivrea''' or '''Susanna of Ivrea'''; c. 950–960 –1003) was countess consort of Flanders by marriage to Arnulf II of Flanders, and queen of the Franks by ma
2 CONC rriage to Robert II of France. She was regent of Flanders in 987-988 during the minority of her son Baldwin IV of Flanders. .. ... .... ....
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------
2 CONT
2 CONT   Daughter of Berengar II and Willa.
2 CONT -http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/NORTHERN%20ITALY%20900-1100.htm#RozalaM1ArnoulIIFlandresM2RobertIIFrance
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT 6.    ''' ROZALA''' [Suzanne] '''d´Ivrea '''([950/960]-13 Dec 1003 or 7 Feb 1004, bur Gent, church of the Abbey de Saint-Pierre du Mont-Blandin). Regino records that two of the daughters (unnamed) of ex-King Berengario were brough
2 CONC t up in the imperial palace by the empress after being brought to Germany[571]. One of these two daughters was presumably Rozala, bearing in mind that the emperor arranged her marriage. The Genealogica Comitum Flandriæ Bertiniana 
2 CONC names "filiam Berengeri regis Langobardorum, Ruzelam quæ et Susanna" as wife of Comte Arnoul[572]. The Annales Elnonenses Minores record the marriage [undated between 950 and 968] of "Arnulfus iunior" and "filiam Beregeri regis Su
2 CONC sannam"[573]. Her marriage was presumably arranged by Emperor Otto to increase his influence in Flanders at a time when Lothaire IV King of the West Franks was asserting his own control over the county. According to Nicholas, Coun
2 CONC t Arnoul II married Rozala d´Ivrea when he reached the age of majority in 976[574], but the source on which this is based has not been located. "Baldwinus marchysus cum matre sua Susanna" donated "villam Aflingehem…jacentem in pag
2 CONC o Tornacinse" to Saint-Pierre de Gand, after the death of "Arnulfi marchysi", by charter dated 1 Apr 988, signed by "…Waldberto advocato, Theoderico comite, Arnulfo comite, Artoldo comite, Baldwino comite, item Arnulfo comite…"[57
2 CONC 5]. The Vita Sancti Bertulfi names "Rozala filia…Berengarii Regis Italiæ", specifying that "post mortem Arnulfi [Balduini filius] principis, Roberto Regi Francorum nupsit et Susanna dicta"[576]. Kerrebrouck, presumably basing his 
2 CONC supposition on this passage from the Vita Sancti Bertulfi, says that she adopted the name Suzanne on her second marriage[577], but the sources quoted above show that she was referred to by this name earlier. Hugues "Capet" King of
2 CONC  France arranged her second marriage to his son and heir, apparently as a reward for Flemish help when he seized power in 987[578]. She was given Montreuil-sur-Mer by the county of Flanders as her dowry on her second marriage. Ric
2 CONC her records that King Robert repudiated his wife "Susannam…genere Italicam eo quod anus esset" but refused to allow her to retake her castle at Montreuil, whereupon she constructed another nearby[579]. She returned to Flanders aft
2 CONC er she was repudiated by her second husband, and became one of the principal advisers of her son Count Baldwin IV. France retained Montreuil-sur-Mer. "Susanna regina cum filio suo Baldwino" donated "alodem suum…Atingehem…et in Tes
2 CONC tereph" to Saint-Pierre de Gand, for the soul of "filie sue Mathildis", by charter dated 26 Jun 995[580]. "Susanna regina…cum filio suo Baldwino" donated "alodem suum…in pago Flandrensi…in Holtawa…in Fresnere…in Clemeskirca…in Jat
2 CONC beka…in Sclefteta…" to Saint-Pierre de Gand by charter dated 1 Jun 1003[581]. The Annales Elnonenses Minores records the death in 1003 of "Susanna regina"[582]. The Memorial of "regina Susanna" records her death "VII Feb"[583]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' firstly ( [968][584] ) ARNOUL II “le Jeune” Count of Flanders, son of BAUDOUIN III joint Count of Flanders & his wife Mechtild of Saxony [Billung] ([961/62]-30 Mar 987, bur Ghent). 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' secondly (988 before 1 Apr, repudiated [991/92] ) as his first wife, ROBERT Associate-King of France, son of HUGUES Capet King of France & his wife Adelais d’Aquitaine (Orléans ([27 Mar] 972-Château de Melun 20 Jul 1031, b
2 CONC ur église de l'Abbaye royale de Saint-Denis). He succeeded his father in 996 as ROBERT II "le Pieux" King of France.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------
2 CONT ----------------
2 CONT
2 CONT https://finnholbek.dk/getperson.php?personID=I26527&tree=2
2 CONT
2 CONT Rozala Susanna de Provence, d'Italia, Gravinne van Vloandern, Reine de France
2 CONT
2 CONT Rozala of Italy (also known as Rozala of Provence, or Susannah of Italy) (c. 937–7 February 1003) was the daughter of King Berengar II of Italy. By her first marriage, she was Countess of Flanders; by her second, she was Queen of 
2 CONC France. She was a seventh generation descendant of Charlemagne.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her first marriage was to Count Arnulf II of Flanders (d. 988). They had three children: Baldwin IV of Flanders (980–1035); Eudes of Cambrai; and Mathilda (d. 995). On her husband's death, she acted as regent for her young son.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 988 or 989, despite being over fifty years old, she married Robert the Pious, the Rex Filius of France; he was not particularly enthusiastic about the marriage, which had been arranged by his father, King Hugh of France. She br
2 CONC ought her husband Montreuil and Ponthieu as a dowry. Upon her marriage, she took the name of Susannah.
2 CONT
2 CONT When her father-in-law died, however, Robert repudiated her, desiring to marry Bertha of Burgundy in her place. Rozala then retired to Flanders, where she died and was buried. Robert retained control of her dowry.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rozala_of_Lombardy 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rozala_d%27Italie
2 CONT
2 CONT http://vls.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rozala-Suzanna_van_Ivrea
