2 CONC rn, king of Sweden.
2 CONT
2 CONT Styrbjorn's wife, Thyra Haraldsdotter,] was the daughter of Harold Bluetooth (king of Denmark and Norway). However, this pedigree may have been concocted to glorify his descendants, who later reigned in Denmark. Alternatively, Sax
2 CONC o Grammaticus reports he was son of a bear.
2 CONT
2 CONT He died at the Battle of Swold.
2 CONT
2 CONT His children were Ulf (d. 1027), the Earl of Canute the Great in Denmark and Danish steward, and Gytha Thorkelsdóttir who was to marry Godwin, Earl of Wessex.
