1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT ==Ulf Tostesson, jarl av Västergötland==
2 CONT
2 CONT * Ulf Tostesson was Jarl of Sweden. He was from Westrogothia and the son of the legendary viking Skogul Toste. He was the brother of Sigrid the Haughty, and his son Jarl Ragnvald Ulfsson was the father of Stenkil, who was elected 
2 CONC king when the old dynasty died out.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Project MedLands, Sweden Kings==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''KINGS of SWEDEN 1060-[1111] (FAMILY of STENKIL)'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Skoglar" TOSTE, son of ---.  In Svithjod.  Snorre records that Harald "Grenske" was welcomed in Svithjod by "Toste…often in battle…therefore called Skoglar-Toste" and lived five years with him[68]. 
2 CONT m ---.  
2 CONT
2 CONT The name of Toste's wife is not known. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Toste & his wife had two children: 
2 CONT * 1.         '''ULF'''.  According to Snorre[69], he was the brother of Sigrid "Storråda/the Haughty".  m ---.  The name of Ulf's wife is not known.  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''ULF & his wife had one child:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * a)         RAGNVALD Ulfsson .  Snorre names "Earl Ragnvald, Ulf's son" when recording his [first] marriage[70].  Jarl in Västergötland.  Snorre records that Ragnvald accompanied Ingegerd to Russia and was installed as Earl of La
2 CONC doga[71].  '''married  firstly INGEBORG Trygvesdatter, daughter of TRYGVE Olavsson of Norway & his wife Åstrid Eiriksdatter.''' Snorre records the marriage of Ingebjorg, Trygve's daughter, King Olaf's sister and Earl Ragnvald, Ulf
2 CONC 's son"[72].   '''married  secondly [as her first husband,] ASTRID Njalsdotter, daughter of NJAL & his wife.'''  The primary source which confirms her parentage and two marriages has not yet been identified.  [She married secondly
2 CONC  as his second wife, Emund Slemme den Gamle/the Old King of Sweden.  Her supposed second marriage to Ragnvald may be nothing more than a guess based on Adam of Bremen recording that nepos eius [=rex Sueonum Emund] Stinkel succeede
2 CONC d on the death of Emund[73].]  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Jarl Ragnvald & his first wife had two children:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>* i)          '''ULF''' Snorre names "Earl Ulf and Earl Eilif" as the sons of Ragnvald & his wife[74]. 
2 CONT >>>>* ii)         '''EILIF''  names "Earl Ulf and Earl Eilif" as the sons of Ragnvald & his wife[75]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Jarl Ragnvald & his second wife had one child:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>* iii)       ''' STENKIL Ragnvaldson''' (-1066).  The primary source which confirms his parentage has not yet been identified.  He succeeded [his stepfather] in 1060 as STENKIL King of Sweden.   
2 CONT
2 CONT * 2.         '''SIGRID "Storråda/the Haughty'''.  Snorre names Sigrid as daughter of "Skoglar" Toste and refers to her '''marriage to "the Swedish king, Eirik the Victorious'''  Saxo Grammaticus names "Syritha" as mother of "Erici
2 CONC  filius Olavus"[77].  The Fagrskinna names Sigrid, mother of King Olof, as daughter of Skoglar-Tosta[78].  Morkinskinna names "Sigridr en stórráda" as mother of “the lady Ástrídr…sister of two kings, Knútr the Great and Óláfr the 
2 CONC Swede” who married “Jarl Úlfr sprakaleggr”[79].  '''married firstly ([before 985]) ERIK "Segersäll/the Victorious" King of Sweden, son of [EMUND Erikson King of Sweden]''' (-Uppsala [994/95]). '''married secondly ([1000]) as his s
2 CONC econd wife, SVEND I "Tveskæg/Forkbeard" King of Denmark, son of HARALD I "Blåtand/Bluetooth" King of Denmark & his first wife Gunhild''' ([960]-Gainsborough 3 Feb 1014, bur in England, later removed to Roskilde).   
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source''' Project MedLands, Sweden Kings - https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SWEDEN.htm#IngeIdied1111
2 CONT
