1 OCCU князь Курский (1125—1129), Полоцкий (1129—1132), Туровский (1132—1134), Волынский (1135—1142), Переяславский (1142—1146) и великий князь Киевский (1146—1149, 1150, 1151
1 TITL Grand Duke
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Iziaslav II Mstislavich''' ('''Изяслав II Мстиславич''' in Russian), born about 1097, died November 13, 1154.
2 CONT
2 CONT Prince of Pereyaslav (1132), Princ of Turov (1132–1134), Prince of Rostov, (1134- )Prince of Vladimir and Volyn (1134–1142), Pereyaslavl (1143–1145), Velikiy Kniaz (Grand Prince) of Kiev (1146–1149 1151–1154), oldest son of Mstisl
2 CONC av Vladimirovich, Kniaz' (Prince) of Novgorod, and Christina Ingesdotter of Sweden.
2 CONT
2 CONT Married:
2 CONT #Agnes, daughter of King Conrad III of Germany, who took the name Liubava after her marriage. She died in 1151. 
2 CONT #Unknown daughter of King Demetre I of Georgia, married for only a few months in 1154 before his death.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Iziaslav II Mstislavich and Agnes Liubava:
2 CONT #Mstislav II of Kiev
2 CONT #Yaroslav II of Kiev
2 CONT #Yaropolk, Prince of Shumsk
2 CONT #Evdokia, married Mieszko III the Old, High Duke of Poland.
2 CONT
