2 CONT >>i)          [http://www.geni.com/people/Sigurd-II-Hlodvesson/6000000001041474621?through=6000000001045422816  SIGURD] "Digri/the Stout", son of [HLODVIR Torfinnsson Jarl of Orkney & his wife Eithne of Ireland] ([965/70]-killed i
2 CONC n battle Clontarf 23 Apr 1014).  Orkneyinga Saga names “Sigurd the Stout” as the son of Hlodvir and his wife, adding that he “took over the earldom” after his father died[856].  Snorre names "Sigurd the Thick" as the son of Hlodve
2 CONC r[857].  His birth date is estimated from the fact that his older sons were already sufficiently mature in 1014 to be placed in charge of Orkney by their father when he left for war in Ireland.  He succeeded his father in [988] as
2 CONC  Jarl of Orkney and Caithness.  He defeated Findlaech Mormaer of Moray before 995 at the second battle of Skidmoor in Caithness, consolidating his power on the Scottish mainland.  Orkneyinga Saga records Sigurd´s battle against “a
2 CONC  Scottish earl called Finnleik”[858].  Orkneyinga Saga records that “[http://www.geni.com/people/Olav-Tryggvason/6000000003867333182 Olaf Tryggvason]” pressured Sigurd to accept baptism and returned to Norway with Sigurd´s son as 
2 CONC a hostage[859].  Orkneyinga Saga records that Sigurd went to Ireland “five years after the Battle of Svoldur” to support “King [http://www.geni.com/people/Sitric-I-King-of-Dublin/6000000002043182790?through=6000000003645985234 Sig
2 CONC trygg Silk-Beard]” against “[http://www.geni.com/people/Brian-B%C3%B3ruma-mac-Cenn%C3%A9tig/6000000002043263223  King Brian] of Ireland”, and left “his elder sons in charge of the earldom”, but was killed in the battle in which Ki
2 CONC ng Brian was killed[860].  Snorre records that "Sigurd the Thick" went to Ireland and fell "in Brian's battle"[861].  [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SCOTTISH%20NOBILITY.htm#_Toc268450047 (Cawley's Medlands)]
