2 CONC “in charge of the earldom” when he left for Ireland and that they divided the earldom between them after he was killed[869].  Snorre names "Sumarlide, Bruse and Einar Rangmund" as "older sons" of "Sigurd the Thick", recording that
2 CONC  they succeeded on the death of their father when the country was divided into three parts[870].  He succeeded his father 1014 as Jarl of 1/3 Orkney, and disputed the share of his deceased brother Einar with his half-brother Thorf
2 CONC inn.  Orkneyinga Saga records the death of “Brusi”, dated from the context to after the death of Malcolm II King of Scotland[871].  m ---.  The name of Brusi´s wife is not known.  Brusi & his wife had one child:  [http://fmg.ac/Pr
