2 CONT >f)          [http://www.geni.com/people/Hlodver-Thorfinnsson/6000000001045422816  HLODVIR Torfinnsson] ([945/50]-[988], bur Hofn, Caithness).  Orkneyinga Saga names (in order) “Arnfinn…Havard the Fecund…Hlodvir…Ljot…Skuli” as the
2 CONC  five sons of Thorfinn[844].  Snorre names "the Earls Hlodver, Arnfid, Ljot and Skule, the sons of Thorfin Hausakljufer" as rulers in Orkney when [http://www.geni.com/people/Gunhild-Ossursdotter/6000000005049052310 Queen Gunhild] 
2 CONC  and her sons returned to Orkney[845].  In a later saga, Snorre names (in order) "Arnfin, Havard, Hlodver, Liot and Skule" as sons of Thorfin "Hausakljufer"[846].  Orkneyinga Saga records that “after Ljot´s death, Hlodvir took cha
2 CONC rge of the earldom”, presumably indicating Ljot´s brother but this is not explicitly stated in the text, recording that “he died in his bed” and was buried “in a burial mound at Ham in Caithness”[847]. 
