2 CONT ==Medieval Lands==
2 CONT Bethóc was the wife of Crínán:  [http://www.geni.com/people/Cr%C3%ADn%C3%A1n-of-Dunkeld/6000000002236747331  CRINAN] "the Thane", son of --- (-killed in battle 1045).  Abthane of Dule.  Lay abbot of Dunkeld.  Steward of the Wester
2 CONC n Isles.  Mormaer of Atholl.  He was killed fighting King Macbeth.  m ([1000]) '''[http://www.geni.com/people/Bethoc-ingen-Mail-Coluim-meic-Cin%C3%A1eda/6000000002236872569?through=6000000002236747331  BETHOC], daughter of [http:/
2 CONC /www.geni.com/people/Malcolm-II-The-Destroyer-King-of-Scots/6000000000013017126?through=6000000002236872569  MALCOLM II] King of Scotland & his wife ---.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT The "Genealogy of King William the Lyon" dated 1175 names 
2 CONT >"Betoch filii Malcolmi" as parent of "Malcolmi filii Dunecani"[131]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The Chronicle of the Scots and Picts dated 1177 names
2 CONT > "Cran Abbatis de Dunkelden et Bethok filia Malcolm mac Kynnet" as parents of King Duncan[132]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The Chronicle of John of Fordun records that King Malcolm II had 
2 CONT >"an only daughter…Beatrice who married Crynyne Abthane of Dul and Steward of the Isles…in some annals, by a blunder of the writer…abbot of Dul"[133].  
2 CONT
2 CONT Lady of Atholl. [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SCOTTISH%20NOBILITY.htm#_Toc268450047 (Cawley's Medlands)]
2 CONT
2 CONT Crinan & Bethoc had two children:
2 CONT >i) [http://www.geni.com/people/Duncan-I-the-Gracious-King-of-Scots/6000000005037689063?through=6000000002236747331   DUNCAN] ([1001]-killed in battle either Bothganowan/Pitgaveny, near Elgin, or Burghead 14 Aug 1040, bur Isle of 
2 CONC Iona). His parentage is confirmed by the Annals of Ulster which record the death of "Donnchad son of Crínán, king of Scotland" in 1040[209]. The Chronicle of John of Fordun names "Duncan" as son of "Crynyne Abthane of Dul and Stew
2 CONC ard of the Isles" and his wife[210]. He succeeded in 1018 as King of Strathclyde. He succeeded his maternal grandfather in 1034 as DUNCAN I King of Scotland. [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SCOTLAND.htm  (Cawley’s Medlands)]
2 CONT
2 CONT >ii) [http://www.geni.com/people/Maldred-mac-Cr%C3%ADn%C3%A1n/6000000000769899955?through=6000000002236747331   MALDRED] (-killed in battle [1045]). His parentage is confirmed by Simeon of Durham who records the marriage of "Maldr
2 CONC ed the son of Crinan"[211]. Lord of Allerdale. Regent of Strathclyde 1034/35. [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SCOTLAND.htm  (Cawley’s Medlands)]
2 CONT
