2 CONT 3.         HVORFLAED [Hvafleda  or Gormflaeth/Gormlath] (before 1134-).  Orkneyinga Saga records that “Hvarflod, the daughter of Earl Malcolm of Moray” was the second wife of Earl Harald[14].  The Chronicle of John of Fordun (Cont
2 CONC inuator - Annals) records that "Harald the earl" was "goaded on by his wife, the daughter of Mached" to rebel against King William in 1196[15].  m as his second wife, HARALD Maddadsson Jarl of Orkney, son of MADDAD [of Scotland] E
2 CONC arl of Atholl & his second wife Margaret of Orkney (1134-1206).  http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SCOTTISH%20NOBILITY%20LATER.htm#Mal
2 CONT
