1 OCCU 1st Lord of the Isles; 8th Thane/Regulus/Lord of Argyll, Lord of Cantyre, Lord of the Hebrides; Norse King of the Sudreys, King of Isle of Man 1158-1164, Warlord
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Somerled son of Gilbert (Somhairle mac Gillebride) 1st Lord/King of the Isles===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''''Gillebride, or Gilbert''''', who is mentioned by the oldest Highland genealogist as "rig eilean Shidir," that is, King of the Sudereys or Southern Isles. 
2 CONT Gilbert's unnamed daughter was the wife of Wymund MacHeth, Earl of Moray. 
2 CONT Gilbert was called Gillebride na h-Uamh, from the fact that during a certain period of his depressed fortunes he lived in a cave in the district of Morvern. 
2 CONT From Gillebride descends the Clans Donald, Dougall, MacLachlan, MacEwin of Otter, and others. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Gilbert's s son was Somhairle Mor MacGillebhride [Somerled rex insularum], known today as
2 CONT Somerled 1st Lord/King of the Isles.
2 CONT
2 CONT Reference: '''''Source: "The Clan Donald" Vol 3, page 178.''''' ]
2 CONT
2 CONT Somerled, a Celtic chief, acquired the Western Isles in the mid-1100s and assumed the title “King of the Isles”.  His son reginald (Ragnall mac Somhairle) was the first whose title "Lord of the Isles" is attested to in a contempor
2 CONC ary document.  Although his grandson Angus mac Donald 4th Lord of the Isles was the first to acknowledge the subjection of the Isles to the kings of Scotland, no 'Scottish peerage' (as recognized by the Scottish monarchy) over the
2 CONC  region was created until 1476 - though this is based on a biased modern Scottish/British dismissal of the existence of nobility before the present "official" lineages. The title "Lord of the Isles" was later one which was vested 
2 CONC in the first-born son (heir apparent) of the king of Scotland, which now is vested in the heir apparent (the Prince of Wales) to the Crown of the United Kingdom of Great Britain.
2 CONT
2 CONT [reference: *http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SCOTTISH%20NOBILITY.htm#ReginaldsonSomerledB
2 CONT
2 CONT Brother [and sister], parents not known: 
2 CONT *1.        '' '''[https://www.geni.com/people/Somerled-King-of-the-Isles/6000000002043212109 SOMERLED] (-killed in battle 1164).  [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/James_Balfour_Paul Balfour Paul]:'' 
2 CONT The first reference to Somerled records him as living in the district of Morven with his father Gillebride, but he does not cite the precise source[1019].  Lord of Argyll. He acquired control of the Western Isles and assumed the t
2 CONC itle "King of the Isles".  ''The Chronicle of Melrose'' records that Somerled Lord of Argyll landed at Renfrew in 1164 with a large army from Ireland after 12 years of rebellion against Malcolm IV King of Scots, but was defeated a
2 CONC nd killed with his son. The ''Extracta ex Cronicis Scocie'' records that "Sumerlendus regulus Ergadie (Somerled King of Argyll)" rebelled against King Malcolm for 12 years, landed at Renfrew from Ireland, and was killed "et filium
2 CONC  suum Gillecolanem (and his son Gilliecolum)", among passages dealing with events in 1164. 
2 CONT ''The Annals of Ulster'' record that "Somharlidh Mac Gilla-Adhamhnain and his son were killed" in 1164.
2 CONT The ''Book of Clanranald'' records that no battle was fought and that Somerled was killed in his tent, after which his followers dispersed.  
2 CONT MARRIAGE: the illegitimate daughter of Olav King of [the Isle of] Man & his mistress ''[https://www.geni.com/people/Ragnhildr-%C3%93l%C3%A1fsd%C3%B3ttir-of-Man/6000000019032360275?through=6000000002043212109 --- of Man]''.
