2 CONT Chapter 9.    ARGYLL
2 CONT
2 CONT Arregaithel or Argyll was previously the kingdom of Dalriada in the west of Scotland.  It was added as a province in the 10th century and at that time covered the whole western coast of Scotland as far north as Caithness.  It is u
2 CONC nclear whether the rulers of the province originally used the title Mormaer or were throughout referred to as Lord.  Following the defeat of Somerled Lord of Argyll in 1164, it was nearly three centuries before James II King of Sc
2 CONC otland created the earldom of Argyll, with Colin Campbell Lord Campbell as 1st Earl of Argyll, in 1457.  He and his descendants are outside the scope of this work. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Brother and sister, parents not known: 
2 CONT
