2 CONT
2 CONT b)         REGINALD .  The Chronicon Manniæ et Insularum names “Dulgallum, Reginaldum, Engus et Olavum” as the four sons of “Sumerledo regulo Herergaildel” and his wife the daughter of Olav King of Man[354].  The Chronicon Manniæ 
2 CONC et Insularum records that Engus, son of Somerled, defeated his brother Reginald in 1192[355]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT -        LORDS of the ISLES. 
