1 OCCU Clan Chief of Clan MacDougall. Also known as: Dougall (Dufgall) MacSumarlidsson, King of Innesgall.
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Dugall was the eldest son of King Somerled of the Hebrides. He founded the clan of MacDougalls when his father was killed in battle against the King of Scots, in 1164. Somerled was of mixed Celtic-Norse royal blood
2 CONC . Dugall, (Dubhgall) took over the heartland what is now called Argyll. His title being, King in the South Isles, Lord of Lorn. The surname MacDougall means Son of Dougall, the gaelic words Dubhgall, means black stranger or foreig
2 CONC ner, so "son of black stranger" is a known expression for MacDougall.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SCOTTISH%20NOBILITY.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT Chapter 9. ARGYLL
2 CONT
2 CONT Arregaithel or Argyll was previously the kingdom of Dalriada in the west of Scotland. It was added as a province in the 10th century and at that time covered the whole western coast of Scotland as far north as Caithness. It is unc
2 CONC lear whether the rulers of the province originally used the title Mormaer or were throughout referred to as Lord. Following the defeat of Somerled Lord of Argyll in 1164, it was nearly three centuries before James II King of Scotl
2 CONC and created the earldom of Argyll, with Colin Campbell Lord Campbell as 1st Earl of Argyll, in 1457.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. SOMERLED (-killed in battle 1164). Lord of Argyll. He acquired control of the Western Isles and assumed the title King of the Isles. The Chronicle of Melrose records that Somerled Lord of Argyll landed at Renfrew in 1164, after
2 CONC  12 years of rebellion against Malcolm IV King of Scotland, with a large army from Ireland but was defeated and killed with his son[351].
2 CONT
2 CONT m --- of Man, illegitimate daughter of OLAV King of Man & his mistress ---. The name of Somerled´s wife is not known. The Chronicon Manniæ et Insularum records that “Olavus filius Godredi Crovan” had many concubines by whom he fat
2 CONC hered “filios tres…Reignaldum, Lagmannum et Haraldum et filias multas”, adding that one daughter married “Sumerledo regulo Herergaildel”[352]. Somerled & his wife had five children: [ONE OF WHICH WAS DUGALD]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''[https://www.geni.com/people/Dougal-MacRory-1st-of-Dunollie-and-of-Lorn/6000000005398287081 DUGALD], son of SOMERLED Lord of Argyll & his wife --- of Man (-after 1175).  The Chronicon Manniæ et Insularum names “Dulgallum, Regin
2 CONC aldum, Engus et Olavum” as the four sons of “Sumerledo regulo Herergaildel” and his wife the daughter of Olav King of Man[1042].  The Obituario of Durham records that "Dusgal filius Sumerledi et Stephanus capellanus suus et Adam d
2 CONC e Stanford" donated two gold rings to St Cuthbert in 1175[1043].  The Liber Vitæ of Durham names "Dunegal filius Sumerledi, et filii sui, Olaf et Dunechal et Raynald et Adam de Stanford. Stephanus Capellanus"[1044]. m [https://www
2 CONC .geni.com/people/Unknown-Wife-MacDougall/6000000001828593786?through=6000000005398287081 ---].  The name of Dugald’s wife is not known. Dugald & his wife had four children:''' 
