2 CONT Sofia of Minsk
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Sofia of Minsk or Sophie of Polotzk (born around 1140, possibly between 1138 and 1141-1198), was a Danish mediavel queen, Queen consort of King Valdemar I of Denmark.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit]Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT She was half-sister of Canute V of Denmark and daughter of Dowager Queen Rikissa of Sweden from her marriage with a father called "Valador" King in Poloni Lands. Several speculations have been put forward as to exactly who her fat
2 CONC her was, but his identity is still uncertain.
2 CONT
2 CONT As a widow, Sofia married Louis III, Landgrave of Thuringia in about 1184, but was repudiated very soon after the marriage.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children and family
2 CONT
2 CONT Sofia married Valdemar I of Denmark (c 1131-1182), and they had the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT King Canute VI of Denmark (1163-1202)
2 CONT
2 CONT King Valdemar II of Denmark (1170-1241)
2 CONT
2 CONT Sophie, (1159 –1208), married Siegfried III, Count of Orlamünde
2 CONT
2 CONT Margareta and Maria, nuns at Roskilde
2 CONT
2 CONT Rikissa of Denmark (died 1220), married King Eric X of Sweden
2 CONT
2 CONT Helen (died 1233), married William, Duke of Brunswick-Luneburg
2 CONT
2 CONT Ingeborg (1175-1236), married King Philip II of France
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Sofia of Minsk
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Sofia of Minsk or Sophie of Polotzk (born around 1140, possibly between 1138 and 1141-1198), was a Danish mediavel queen, Queen consort of King Canute V of Denmark.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit]Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT She was half-sister of Canute V of Denmark and daughter of Dowager Queen Rikissa of Sweden from her marriage with a father called "Valador" King in Poloni Lands. Several speculations have been put forward as to exactly who her fat
2 CONC her was, but his identity is still uncertain.
2 CONT
2 CONT As a widow, Sofia married Louis III, Landgrave of Thuringia in about 1184, but was repudiated very soon after the marriage.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit]Children and family
2 CONT
2 CONT Sofia married Valdemar I of Denmark (c 1131-1182), and they had the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT King Canute VI of Denmark (1163-1202)
2 CONT
2 CONT King Valdemar II of Denmark (1170-1241)
2 CONT
2 CONT Sophie, (1159 –1208), married Siegfried III, Count of Orlamünde
2 CONT
2 CONT Margareta and Maria, nuns at Roskilde
2 CONT
2 CONT Rikissa of Denmark (died 1220), married King Eric X of Sweden
2 CONT
2 CONT Helen (died 1233), married William, Duke of Brunswick-Luneburg
2 CONT
2 CONT Ingeborg (1175-1236), married King Philip II of France
