1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Margareta (Margit) Erengislesdotter / Fot=
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT * Daughter of Erengissle Gjordsson / Fot and Ingrid
2 CONT * In 1498, Margareta Erengislesdotter donated a mill F that yielded 2 barrels to Skänninge Monastery upon her daughter Karin Ulfsdotter's entry there (Rääf 1:140).
2 CONT * In 1552, the mayor of Vadstena, Ulf Petersson, sold to Gustav I his inheritance from his maternal uncle, Erengisle Ulfsson, including a mill under Graby in Fström (Rääf 1:167, see DMS 4:5 p 82f). In 1565, Olof Gustavsson (Stjärn
2 CONC bjälke) certified that the sale was illegal, since this mill had been given to Skänninge Monastery by Margareta Erengislesdotter (see 1498) (Rääf 1:182).
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://www.diva-portal.org/smash/get/diva2:1197266/FULLTEXT01.pdf Band 4 SMÅLAND: 5 Tjust, Västerviks stad]
2 CONT
2 CONT {{https://www.geni.com/media/proxy?media_id= 6000000225649373830&size=large}}  
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=vadstena&FacettFilter=register_facet%24Brev%2FSDHK+(medeltidsbrev)%3A&page=135&postid=sdhk_33472&tab=post SDHK number: 33472]
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Dating: 1497 February 16, Place of issue: Vadstena''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''The Swedish Diplomatarium's main index of medieval letters'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Per Nilsson, citizen of Vadstena , certifies that Ulf Skräddare in Jönköping sold "Guærmanshulth" near Jönköping to Bengt Åkesson at Nygård, etc.
2 CONT
2 CONT * Sources: Original:  Or. perg. Skoklostersaml. RA 0107.14
2 CONT
