1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Cristiern Nilsson Vasa=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Son of Nils Kettilsson (Vasa) and Cristina Jonsdotter (Rickeby) 
2 CONT * Krister Vasa, governor (chief white man) in Visborg 1417, king of Sweden 1435, national high priest 1436. 
2 CONT
2 CONT =Vasa Nobility=
2 CONT
2 CONT Cristiern Nilsson born 1365, died 1442-04-29 at Viborg Castle and was buried so. June 29 in Stockholm's gray brothers convent. Chief white man at Viborg. Knights, national council and drots. '''Married 1st with Margareta Johansdot
2 CONC ter,''' † in Uppsala and buried 1413-08-07 in Vadstena monastery. Daughter of the knight Johan Moltke and Katarina Glysingsdotter ''' Married 2nd: 1426 to Margareta Eriksdotter,''' born 1390, † 1451-06-09 and was buried in Gråbröd
2 CONC raklostret in Stockholm, in her 2nd marriage . Her 1st marriage to Ture Stensson Bielke . Daughter of the Danish National Council Erik Krummedigeand Beata von Thienen.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children with Margareta Johansdotter=
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Cristina Cristiernsdotter,''' probably around 1430. Married 1st with the governor of Karl Stensson Sten Lalason's family . Married 2nd: with the knight and the governor Bengt Jönsson Oxenstierna .
2 CONT * '''Karl Cristiernsson,''' † 1440-08-08 in Reval and buried so. October 4 in the Gråbrödraklosteret / A. Chief white man at Viborg. Married about 1426-1432 with Ebba Eriksdotter Krummedige , † 1465-08-24 at Hov, Hovs sn in Göstri
2 CONC ngs Härad / E. In her 2nd marriage . She was the sister of her husband's stepmother. Her 1st marriage to the knight and the chief white man Tymme Jonsson , † about 1425. Her 3rd marriage about 1442-1449 to the knight, the council 
2 CONC and the lawyer Erik Nipertz . Daughter of the Danish national council Erik Krummedige and Beata von Thienen .
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children with Margareta Eriksdotter=
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Johan Cristiernsson,''' † 1477-04-06 at Rydboholm / C and was buried in Stockholm gray brothers monastery. Knights, council. Married 1st between 1452 and 1461-01-02 with Birgitta Gustavsdotter , † in cot 1472 before September
2 CONC  5 at Rydboholm which she inherited and buried in Östra Ryd's church. She also inherited land in Lagunda and Trögds herald. Daughter of the knight and the national council Gustav Sture and Birgitta Stensdotter Bielke . Married 2nd
2 CONC  at the latest in 1474 with Birgitta Tordsdotter Bonde born about 1456, lived in 1520 when she, as a widow, had Penningby in Länna / C as a farm. in her 1st marriage . Her 2nd marriagewith the knight and the national council Erik 
2 CONC Ottesson Björnram from Västergötland , † probably 1495. Daughter of Marshal Tord Karlsson Bonde and Elin / Iliana Åkesdotter Tott
2 CONT * '''Birgitta Cristiernsdotter Vaasa,''' was born about 1420, † between 1472 and 1478. She is said to have been married three times. Married 1st: 1446 with his step brother, the knight and the national council Erik Turesson Bielke
2 CONC  , he † childless in 1450. Married 2nd: about 1454 with the knight and the national council Claus Rönnow .
2 CONT * '''Nils Cristiernsson,''' † 1464. Knights, council. Married to Birgitta Nilsdotter , daughter of the knight, the national council and the governor Nils Jönsson Oxenstierna and Katarina Karlsdotter Sture.
2 CONT
2 CONT * [https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Vasa#TAB_8 '''Source''' Royal Family of Vaasa] 
2 CONT
2 CONT =History=
2 CONT
2 CONT Krister Vasa, governor (chief white man) in Visborg 1417, king of Sweden 1435, national high priest 1436. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Krister was dubbed a knight as early as 1396. He stood high in favor of widow queen Margareta and even more so with foster son Erik, who for over 40 years was king over the three Nordic countries. kingdoms. As county governor he w
2 CONC as able to act quite independently, but was at the same time a reliable support for King Erik both militarily and within the Swedish national council. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Against Karl Knutsson Bonde, however, Krister eventually pulled the shortest straw and in the New Year 1439 the old drots were imprisoned on his farm Rävelsta in southern Uppland and forced to surrender their castles and counties 
2 CONC to Karl Knutsson Bonde. But he got the establishment of the new Union King Kristofer and died as county lord at Viborg 1442.
2 CONT
2 CONT Krister (Cristiern) Nilsson on Björnö in Frötuna called the German-Baltic nobleman Henrik Scherembeke his "om" (kinsman). Noteworthy is that in Sweden, the unusual first name Cristiern also appeared in the genus Scherembeke and th
2 CONC at Vasa's difficult-to-interpret weapons are very similar to the Scherembeke arms. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Krister Nilsson's son the Swedish Council, Karl Kristersson, died in 1440 became the father of Kettil Karlsson and Erik Karlsson. Karl Kristersson's half-brother the Swedish National Council Johan Kristersson (dead 1477) at Rydboh
2 CONC olm in Uppland was the father of the Swedish Krister Johansson (dead one of the years 1494-97) at Örby in Uppland and Erik Johansson. 
2 CONT
2 CONT (Source: Lars-Olof Larsson: Gustav Vasa - country father or tyrant? Etc.)
2 CONT
