1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plettenberg_(Adelsgeschlecht)
2 CONT
2 CONT Events
2 CONT
2 CONT • Fact: aka Heidophus 1187, Heidenricus 1189, Rabodo 1189, 1187-1189.
2 CONT
2 CONT • Events: Beurkundet, 1189.
2 CONT
2 CONT • Events: Ministeriale zu Plettenberg
2 CONT
2 CONT The first secured documentary mention took place in 1187 with the mention of '''Heidolphus de Plettenbrath''' in a document of the Archbishop of Cologne Philip I of Heinsberg. He was one of the archbishop's followers, who had also
2 CONC  become''' Duke of Westphalia''' in 1180. '''Heidolphus de Plettenbrath''' helped the archbishop to secure his territory from the neighbors, especially the Counts of the Mark.
2 CONT
