2 CONT * Son of Wilhelm von Jülich, IV Graf von Jülich and Richardis van Gelre
2 CONT * Gerhard V of Jülich (* before 1250 ; † 29 July 1328 ; according to another numbering: Gerhard VII [ 1 ] ) was Count of Jülich from 1297 until his death .
2 CONT * His illegitimate descendants include Heinrich von Jülich , papal legate and canon in various dioceses
2 CONT
2 CONT =Married=
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married: '''Elizabeth of Brabant Aarschot,''' daughter of Godfrey de Brabant, Seigneur d'Aerachat & de Vierzon and Jeanne de Vierzon, before 13 December 1299.1 Gerhard VI, Count of Juliers died circa 29 July 1328.1
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children with Elizabeth of Brabant Aarschot=
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Wilhelm I, Marquis & Duke of Juliers, Prince of the Empire, Earl Cambridge'''+ b. c 1299, d. 26 Feb 1361. Their son is often identified as Wilhelm (William), specifically named as Wilhelm I, Duke of Jülich (sometimes referred
2 CONC  to as Wilhelm VI or V).
2 CONT * '''Godfrey von Julich, Herr zu Bergheim''' + d. 3 May 1335
2 CONT * '''Maria von Julich''' +4,5 d. a 1367
2 CONT * '''Richardis von Julich''' +6,7 d. b 9 Jul 1353
2 CONT * '''Richarda von Julich''' + b. 7 Mar 1314, d. 7 Mar 1360
2 CONT * '''Elisabeth von Julich''' +8,9 b. c 1315, d. a 1380
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/FRANCONIA%20%28LOWER%20RHINE%29.htm#_Toc158651917 MEDLANDS FRANCONIA - LOWER RHINE, NOBILITY]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''GERHARD [V] von Jülich, son of WILHELM [III] Graf von Jülich & his wife Richardis van Gelre (-[29 Jul] 1328).'''  "Richarda comitissa Juliacensis, Walleranus Aquensis, Otto Traiectensis ecclesiarum prepositi et Gerardus fratres
2 CONC , filii eiusdem comitisse" submitted to Sifrid Archsbishop of Köln, with the intercession of "Godefrido comite Seynensi", by charter dated 14 Oct 1279[1787].  "Gerardus natus quondam…Wilhelmi comitis Juliacensis" bought property a
2 CONC t Woring, with the consent of "domine Richarde matris nostre, domini Walrami comitis Juliacensis prepositi Aquensis fratris nostri et Methildis puelle sororis nostre", by charter dated 30 Apr 1287[1788].  Herr von Kaster:  “Gerard
2 CONC us dominus de Blankenem” confirmed holding “castrum nostrum de Blankenem” from Jean I Duke of Brabant by charter dated late-Aug 1292, sealed by “Irmengardis domina de Blankenem nostræ consortis...ac...Gerardi de Iuliaco domini de 
2 CONC Castre nostri...consanguinei”[1789].  He succeeded as Graf von Jülich.  "Gerardus comes Iuliacensis" entered an alliance with "Reynaldum comitem Gelriæ…Francorum rege et…duce Brabantiæ", and named "Godefridum de Brabantia dominum 
2 CONC de Verzun et Arschot socerum nostrum", by charter dated 13 Dec 1299[1790].  "Gerardus comes Juliacensis" issued a charter dated 2 Feb 1297[1791].  "Gerardus comes Juliacensis…et coniux…nostra Elysabeth" confirmed the donation of "
2 CONC aream nostram jacentem in Colonia in parrochia s. Columbe…Berlinc", made by "felicis recordationis domina Rikardis mater nostra, dominus Walramus frater noster quondam comes Juliacensis", to the order of St Clara by charter dated 
2 CONC 26 Aug 1304[1792].  "Gerardus comes Juliacensis, Guillelmus eius primogenitus filius et Henricus de Machem prepositus Aquensis" confirmed arrangements between "nostrum consanguineum et dominum comitem Ghelrie" and "nostri consangu
2 CONC inei domini Guillielmi Hanonye et Hollandie comitis" by charter dated 3 Jul 1307[1793].  "Gerardus comes et Elisabeth comitissa nec non Wilhelmus eorum primogenitus filius dominus de Broughe" confirmed concessions granted to Averb
2 CONC oden by "domina Maria domina de Arschot et de Virsione comitissa Juliancensis nostræ prædicta Elisabeth soror", by charter dated 1320[1794].  "Johann von Montenak" transferred "domum in Kessenich", acquired from “seiner Ehefrau Jo
2 CONC hanna, der Tochter des Herrn Arnolds von Kessenich”, to Jülich by charter dated “vigilia Sti Martini” 1321[1795]. '''married firstly --- von Kessel, daughter of WILHELM Graf von Kessel & his wife ---.'''  This supposed first marri
2 CONC age of Graf Gerhard was proposed by Walther Möller, on the assumption that Gerhard’s son Wilhelm must have inherited Grevenbroich, a former Kessel possession, from the Kessel family[1796].  The theory was later adequately disprove
2 CONC d by Manfred Groten who demonstrated that Gerhard V Graf von Jülich occupied Grevenbroich after the death in 1304 of Walram Graf von Kessel, claiming that it was a fief of Jülich, and that the archbishopric of Köln (from whom Kess
2 CONC el held the fief) failed to challenge the occupation due to a vacancy in the archiepiscopal see in 1305[1797].]  '''married (before 13 Dec 1299) ELISABETH de Brabant, daughter of GODEFROI de Brabant Heer van Aarschot, Seigneur de 
2 CONC Vierzon & his wife Jeanne de Vierzon (-[1349/55]).'''  The date of her marriage is indicated by the charter dated 13 Dec 1299 under which "Gerardus comes Iuliacensis" entered an alliance with "Reynaldum comitem Gelriæ…Francorum re
2 CONC ge et…duce Brabantiæ", and named "Godefridum de Brabantia dominum de Verzun et Arschot socerum nostrum"[1798].  Her parentage and marriage are confirmed by a charter dated 2 Jul 1303 under which Marie Queen of France confirmed the
2 CONC  division of property between "Marie contesse de Julliers, Ysabiau fame Girart de Julliers, Aeliz fame Jehan de Harcourt et Blanche fame Bertaut de Maalinnes, filles et hoirs nostre…freire monseign. Godefroy de Braban jadis sires 
2 CONC d’Arscot" and heirs of "nostre…neveu Jehan de Braban jadis seign. de Vierson"[1799].  Heiress of Sichem 1203.  "Gerardus comes et Elisabeth comitissa nec non Wilhelmus eorum primogenitus filius dominus de Broughe" confirmed conces
2 CONC sions granted to Averboden by "domina Maria domina de Arschot et de Virsione comitissa Juliancensis nostræ prædicta Elisabeth soror", by charter dated 1320[1800].  She inherited Vierzon and Livry on the death of her sister Marie. 
2 CONC  Philippe VI King of France confirmed the inheritance by "Isabel contesse de Juliers, suer aisnee et hoir seule…de Marie iadis sa suer dame de Virzon, de Luri" of "la baronie et chastelerie de Virzon, de Luri", instead of "Aelis d
2 CONC ame de Harecourt et Loys de Touart" by charter dated 31 Jan 1331[1801]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Gerhard [V] & his wife’s had eight children:''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT 3em>1.         '''WILHELM [V]''' (-26 Feb 1362).  "…Wilhelmo primogenito comitis Juliacensis…" witnessed the charter dated 13 May 1275 under which "Theodericus dictus Luf, frater comitis Clivensis" granted Hesshausenwardt island t
2 CONC o "nostro filio Theoderico et eius legitimis heredibus"[1802].  That Wilhelm was the son of Elisabeth de Brabant is confirmed by the charter dated 6 Dec 1361 under which Jean II King of France stated that "les chasteaux de Vierzon
2 CONC  et Lury…appartiennent a nostre…cousin […Wilhelm II Duke of Jülich] comme son propre héritage", the castles in question having been inherited from Elisabeth de Brabant[1803].  "Gerardus comes Juliacensis, Guillelmus eius primogeni
2 CONC tus filius et Henricus de Machem prepositus Aquensis" confirmed arrangements between "nostrum consanguineum et dominum comitem Ghelrie" and "nostri consanguinei domini Guillielmi Hanonye et Hollandie comitis" by charter dated 3 Ju
2 CONC l 1307[1804].  Markgraf von Jülich 1336.  Duke of Jülich 1356.  "Wilhelm…hertzoge van Gulge, greue van Valkenborch und heirre van Monyoye" confirmed that "unse…swager…Reynart here van Schonuorst" had transferred to him "sloss Valk
2 CONC enborch" in return for "Valkenborch ind Monyoe" by charter dated 25 Mar 1357[1805].  The precise family relationship between Duke Wilhelm and Reinoud Mascherell Heer van Schoonvorst (see the document BRABANT, LOUVAIN) has not been
2 CONC  ascertained.  The term “swagher” suggests that it was by marriage, maybe through his wife or by marriage to a Jülich cousin.  It should be noted that Wilhelm’s son Gerhard also described Reinoud as his “swager” (see below).  “Swa
2 CONC ger” (or equivalents) was an imprecise term and the relationship could have been remote: Reinoud’s prominent position may have tempted many to highlight him as a family relation in contemporary documentation, however distant the c
2 CONC onnection.  '''Married (Köln 26 Feb 1324) [as her first husband,] JEANNE de Hainaut, daughter of GUILLAUME Comte de Hainaut, WILLEM III Count of Holland & his wife Jeanne de Valois-Capet ([1311/13]-1374).'''  "Guillaumes cuens de 
2 CONC Haynau, de Hollande, de Zeelande, et sires de Frize" and "Gherars cuens de Julers" agreed the marriage of "Jehane fille a…conte Guillaume" and "Guillaume fil a…conte Gherart" by charter dated 24 Jun 1317, witnessed by "…nos…cousin
2 CONC s Renaut conte de Ghelre et Renaut son filz…"[1806].  The Willelmi Capellani in Brederode Chronicon ("Procurator") records the betrothal of "Willelmus comes Hollandie binas filias", adding that "secunda" (unnamed) was betrothed to
2 CONC  "juveni…Juliacensis…comitis filio", dated to 1323 from the context[1807].  The same source records the marriages of the same two daughters taking place at Köln 26 Feb 1324[1808].  The History of Henricus Dapifer de Diessenhoven r
2 CONC ecords that "dominus Ludewicus et rex Anglie et marchio Iuliacensis" had married "tres…sorores…fillies comitis Hannonie sive Hollandie"[1809].  Froissart names "Jehane et…Issabiel" as the sisters of "Phelippe…roine d’Engleterre", 
2 CONC adding in a later passage that "Jehanne…estoit contesse de Jullers"[1810].  [She married secondly Baudouin [III] de Thiennes.  The primary source which confirms her supposed second marriage has not yet been identified.   The marri
2 CONC age is recorded by Gailliard who notes that "Baudouin de Luxembourg dit de Thiennes, seigneur de ce lieu, de Heuchin, la Planque, sénéchal héréditaire de Flandre" married "Jeanne de Hainaut veuve sans enfants de Gérard de Juliers 
2 CONC et fille de Guillaume-le-Bon comte de Hainaut et de Jeanne de Valois", implying that she was the mother of the son who is named in the same source (which would be incredible considering the date her first husband died)[1811].  No 
2 CONC primary source is cited, but given the number of errors in this short extract, it is suggested that Jeanne’s supposed second marriage should be viewed with caution until a more reliable source emerges.]  Wilhelm [V] & his wife had
2 CONC  six children:  
2 CONT 7em>a)         '''GERHARD [VI]''' ([1323/27]-18 May 1360).  Emperor Ludwig IV Duke of Bavaria granted "comitatu in Rauensbergh" to "Gerardus de Juliaco…Wilhelmi marchionis Juliacensis…affinis nostri…primogenitus" by charter dated 
2 CONC 10 Aug 1346[1812].  Graf von Berg und Ravensberg.  
2 CONT 7em>b)         '''WILHELM''' (1333-13 Dec 1393).  Emperor Ludwig IV Duke of Bavaria agreed with "Wilhelmo comiti Juliacensi affini suo" that "Wilhelmo secundo genito tuo, necnon Margarete conthorali sue" should succeed "Adolfus co
2 CONC mes Montensis" if he died childless, by charter dated 16 Aug 1336[1813].  Duke of Jülich.  Duke of Gelre 1372.  
2 CONT 7em>c)         '''REINOLD''' .  The primary source which confirms his parentage has not been identified.  
2 CONT 7em>d)         '''RICHARDIS''' (-[23 Feb 1374/5 Apr 1381]).  “Engelbracht Greve van der Marke” lent money to “Godeken van Hovele”, with the consent of “Rycharden unser...Husvrowen“, by charter dated 11 Oct 1354[1814].  "Gerart els
2 CONC te sun zoe Guilghe, greue van den Berghe ind van Rauesberg" renounced rights over tolls at Kaiserswerth in favour of "her Engelbrecht greue van Marke unse swagher ind unse...suster de greuinne van der Marke sine...vrowe" by charte
2 CONC r dated 1355[1815].  m (Papal dispensation 9 Dec 1348, before 11 Oct 1354) as his first wife, ENGELBERT [III] Graf von der Mark, son of ADOLF [II] Graf von der Mark & his wife Margareta von Kleve ([28 Feb] 1333-Wetter 22 Dec 1391)
2 CONC .  
2 CONT 7em>e)         '''JOHANNA''' (-[1357/62]).  Pope Clement VI granted dispensation for the marriage between “Wilhelmum comitem Wedensem” and “Iohannam natam Willelmi marchionis Iuliacensis Trever. et Colon. dioc.”, who were married 
2 CONC despite knowing the 4° consanguinity between them, dated 21 Nov 1351[1816].  m (before 21 Nov 1351, Papal dispensation 21 Nov 1351, contract 27 Jun 1354) as his second wife, WILHELM von Isenburg Graf von Wied, son of BRUNO [IV] vo
2 CONC n Isenburg Herr von Wied & his wife Heilwig von Katzenelnbogen (-17 Jul 1383).  
2 CONT 7em>f)          '''ELISABETH''' (-6 Jun 1411, bur Church of the Grey Friars, Winchester, Hampshire).  Pope Clement VI granted dispensation for the marriage between “Iohanne comite Cantie” and “Elizabet nata Wilhelmi comitis Iuliac
2 CONC ensis”, as part of the peace settlement between "Willelmum comitem Iuliacensem" and “Raynaldum ducem Gelrie consanguineum Iohannis comitis Cantie”, dated 3 Apr 1348[1817].  She took a vow of chastity at Waverley Abbey after the de
2 CONC ath of her first husband, but broke it to marry her second husband.  The will of "Elizabeth Juliers Countess of Kent", dated 20 Apr 1411, proved 29 Jun 1411, chose burial “in the church of the Friars Minors in the city of Winchest
2 CONC er in the tomb of John late Earl of Kent late my husband”, bequeathed property to “my...sister Alice Countess of Kent...Joan Countess of Kent”[1818].  m firstly (Papal dispensation 3 Apr 1348) JOHN Earl of Kent, son of EDMUND "of 
2 CONC Woodstock" Earl of Kent & his wife Margaret Wake, later Baroness Wake (posthumously Arundel Castle, Sussex 7 Apr 1330-26/27 Dec 1352, bur Church of the Grey Friars, Winchester, Hampshire).  m secondly (Wingham, Kent 29 Sep 1360) E
2 CONC USTACHE d’Aubréchicourt, son of NICOLAS Seigneur de Bugnicourt et d’Aubréchicourt[1819] & his wife --- (-Evreux soon after 1 Dec 1372).  
2 CONT 7em>g)         '''PHILIPPA''' (-24 Aug 1390).  "Wilhelm…hertzoge van Guilge, greue zu Valkenburch ind here zu Monyoie, Gierhart elste sun zu Gulge, greue van den Berghe ind van Rauesberge, ind Diederich greue van Loen ind van Chin
2 CONC ey, herre zu Heynsberg ind zu Blankenberch" agreed the marriage of "Philippen doychter uns hertzogen ind suster unss greuen van den Berge" and "Goedarde van Heynsberg herren zu Dalenbroych, broyder sun unss greue van Loen" by char
2 CONC ter dated 7 Feb 1357[1820].  "Godevaert van Loen here zu Heynsberch" acknowledged "Eduwaert hertog van Gelre" as his suzerain for "onse borch van Heynsberch…die borch tot Geylenkerken…Dalenbroich", naming "[onse] vrouw Philippe va
2 CONC n Guylche vrouw van Heynsberg", by charter dated 14 Feb 1367[1821].  Heiress of ½ Jülich.  m (contract 7 Feb 1357, 1 Nov 1357) GOTTFRIED [II] von Heinsberg, son of JOHANN [I] Herr von Heinsberg, Heer van Dalenbroich & his wife Cat
2 CONC harina van Voorne (-1395).  
2 CONT 3em>2.         '''LUDWIG''' (-after 25 Feb 1311).  “Gerhardus comes Juliacensis” renounced rights to property “ex parte nostra et Lodewici filii nostri” in favour of Köln by charter dated 25 Feb 1311[1822].  
2 CONT 3em>3.         '''MARIA''' (-after 11 Nov 1363).  A charter dated 1 Sep 1306 records a settlement agreed by "Roprecht van Vyrnenburg, Symon van Spanheym, Heynrich van Solmeze gehezen van Spaunheym, greuen" concerning "der burg zo 
2 CONC Rymerzheym" [Ringsheim], relating to a marriage contract between “Gerharde deime greue van Guleghe…des vursprochgene greuen dochter van Guleghe” and “Ruprechtes des jungen van Virnenburg sun, die is encklin unses Roprechts des gre
2 CONC uen van Virnenburg”, by charter dated 1 Sep 1306[1823]: neither Robert [II] von Virneburg’s son nor Gerhard von Jülich’s daughter is named in this document (when they both must have been infants), and it is possible that they were
2 CONC  not Heinrich and Maria but other children who died young before the marriage was finalised.  The marriage contract between "Ruprecht greue van Virnembourgh unde Heinrich sin elste sun" and "Wilhelm und heren Godeuarde sinen soene
2 CONC n…vrouwen Marien van Guilge" is dated 7 Feb 1327[1824].  "Theodericus comes Cleuensis" relinquished further claim from "Walramus archiepiscopus Coloniensis" relating to the dowry on his marriage to "dominam Mariam sororem suam" by
2 CONC  charter dated 6 Dec 1340[1825].  Pope Benedict XII granted dispensation for the marriage between "nobili viro Theoderico de greve van Cleve milite" and “Maria nata quondam Gerardi dez greven van Culk” despite knowing that “prima 
2 CONC Theoderici uxor...Marie” was related to her in 3° consanguinity, dated 13 Apr 1341[1826].  Pope Clement VI granted another dispensation for the marriage between "nobilis viri Theoderici comitis Clevensis" and “nobilis mulieris Mar
2 CONC ie nate quondam Gerardi comitis Iuliacensis” notwithstanding their ignorance of their 3° consanguinity, dated 31 May 1342[1827].  “Konrad von Saffenberg und Maria von Jülich Frau zu Monreal” and “Graf Ruprecht von Virneburg, Johan
2 CONC n [von Virneburg] Propst zu Xanten, Adolf, Gerhard und Johann Söhne Graf Ruprechts” reached agreement about Monreal by charter dated 2 Mar 1347 (O.S.)[1828].  Pope Clement VI granted dispensation for the marriage between “Conrado 
2 CONC de Saffinberg consanguineo archiepiscopi” and “Maria relicta quondam Theoderici comitis Clevensis”, despite the 3° consanguinity between Konrad and Graf Dietrich, dated 28 May 1350[1829].  "Johan…bischoff…zu Munster zu Westfalen, 
2 CONC Gerardt grave zu Virnembergh, und Adolff, alle gebruder von Virnembergh" confirmed "Pellentzen…die herre Heinrich selige unser…bruder und sie…versatzt hant" to "Marie von Gulich frauwe zu Monreau" by charter dated 11 Nov 1363[1830
2 CONC ].  m firstly (contract 7 Feb 1327) HEINRICH [II] von Virneburg, son of ROBERT [III] Graf von Virneburg & his first wife Agnes [von Westerburg] ([before 1 Sep 1306?]-1335, after 17 Feb).  m secondly (before 6 Dec 1340, Papal dispe
2 CONC nsations 13 Apr 1341 and 31 May 1342) as his second wife, DIETRICH [VII] Graf von Kleve, son of DIETRICH [VI] Graf von Kleve & his second wife Margareta von Habsburg (1291-7 Jul 1347).  m thirdly (before 2 Mar 1348, Papal dispensa
2 CONC tion 28 Mar 1350) KONRAD Herr von Saffenberg, son of JOHANN [I] Herr von Saffenberg & his wife Sophia van Heusden (-after 17 Sep 1377).  
2 CONT 3em>4.         '''GOTTFRIED''' (-3 May 1335, bur Münstercifel Stiftskirche).  Herr von Bergheim.  "Goidart van Guylge herre zu Bergheym" granted property to "Costantine van Lisenkirgen burgere zu Coillen" by charter dated 18 Dec 1
2 CONC 328, which names "unse…broidere heren Wilhelme den greuen van Guylge"[1831].  m (before Sep 1330, Papal dispensation 28 Sep 1330) as her first husband, ELISABETH von Kleve, daughter of DIETRICH LUF von Kleve Graf von Hülchrath & h
2 CONC is first wife Yolande de Looz (-1347).  Pope John XXII granted dispensation for the marriage between "nobilis viri Godefridi de Juliaco domini de Berchem" and “nobilis mulieris Elizabet nate...nobilis viri Theoderici dicti Luyf de
2 CONC  Cleve Colon. dioc.” despite not knowing of their 4° consanguinity, dated 28 Sep 1330[1832].  She married secondly (1336) as his second wife, Willem [VI] van Horne.  The testament of "Willem heer van Hoern, van Altena ende Gaesbee
2 CONC k" is dated Oct 1342 and names "onsen…oudsten soene Geeraert van Hoern riddere…vrou Else van Cleve onser…vrouwen…onse…nichte Beatrix van Lovene"[1833].  Gottfried & his wife had two children:  
2 CONT 7em>a)         '''son''' (before 2 Aug 1332-young).  
2 CONT 7em>b)         '''YOLANDE von Bergheim''' (-31 Oct 1387).  "Emiche greue zu Lyningen und…Jolenta von Bergheim greuinne zu Lyningen, desseluen greuen Emichen…wyfe" sold "die burg…Oede…die vaidie van Kempen…" to "Wilhelme deme march
2 CONC greuen van Guilge…oheimen unser Jolenten vorgenant" by charter dated 3 Nov 1348[1834].  "Wilhelmus…marchio Juliacensis" sold "castrum de Oyde, advocatiam Kempensem…", bought from "Emichone comite et Yolenta de Bercheim consanguine
2 CONC a nostra comitissa de Lyningen, coniugibus", to Walram Archbishop of Köln by charter dated 5 Jan 1349[1835].  m (before 3 Nov 1348) [as his second wife,] FRIEDRICH [IX] Graf von Leiningen-Dagsburg, son of FRIEDRICH [VII] Graf von 
2 CONC Leiningen-Dagsburg & his wife --- (-1397).  
2 CONT 3em>5.         '''WALRAM''' ([1303/04]-Paris 14 Jul 1349, bur Köln Cathedral).  Archbishop of Köln 1332.  Levoldus’s mid-14th century Chronica Comitum de Marka records the death in 1349 of “archiepiscopus Coloniensis dominus Walra
2 CONC mus de Iuliaco” in Paris and his burial “in maiori ecclesia”[1836].  
2 CONT 3em>6.         '''JOHANN''' (-after 1327).  Canon at Liège St Jean.  Butkens names "Jean tué en combat en l’abbaye de Stavelo" as the youngest son of Gerhard [V] Graf von Jülich and his wife Elisabeth de Brabant without indicating
2 CONC  the primary source on which this information is based[1837].  
2 CONT 3em>7.         '''ELISABETH''' (-after 1364).  Pope John XXII granted dispensation for the marriage between "Iohanni comiti Seynensi" and “nobilis mulieri Elisabeth nate quondam Gherardi comitis Iuliacensis Colon. dioc.” who was b
2 CONC etrothed aged 10, and married after reaching marriageable age, despite not knowing of “impedimentum”, dated 29 Sep 1330[1838].  Pope John XXII granted another dispensation for the marriage between the same parties which specified 
2 CONC their 4° consanguinity, dated 30 Oct 1330[1839].  "Willem…marchgreue zu Gulge und Johanna marchgreuynne unse…vrauwe" purchased rights to "der burg zu Brunsberg…und…dat dorp Brule uf dem Ryne" from "unsen zwager den greue Johanne v
2 CONC an Seyne und Elyzabet greuynne sin…vrauwe, unse…suster" by charter dated 21 Aug 1337[1840].  m firstly (before Sep 1330, Papal dispensation 29 Sep and 30 Oct 1330) JOHANN [II] Graf zu Sayn, son of JOHANN [I] Graf von Sayn & his wi
2 CONC fe Elisabeth von Hessen (-after 25 Dec 1360).  m secondly (before 15 May 1364) GOTTFRIED von Hatzfeld, son of --- (-1371).  
2 CONT 3em>8.         '''RICHARDIS''' (7 Mar 1314-7 Mar 1360, bur Seligenthal).  The primary source which confirms her date of birth has not yet been identified.   The necrology of Seligenthal records the death "Non Mar 1360" of "nobilis
2 CONC  domina Richardis ducissa Bawarie comitissa palatina Reni"[1841].  m (1330) OTTO IV Duke of Lower Bavaria, son of STEFAN I "der Ältere" joint Duke of Lower Bavaria & his wife Jutta von Schweidnitz [Piast] (3 Jan 1307-Munich 14 Dec
2 CONC  1334, bur Seligenthal).   
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Gerhard [V] had one illegitimate child by an unknown mistress:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT 3em>9.         '''HEINRICH''' von Jülich .  Pope John XXII granted dispensation to "Henrico de Juliaco nato quondam Gerardi comitis Iuliacensis clerico Coloniensis diocesis" to hold office despite “defectu natalium”, dated 24 Jan 
2 CONC 1329[1842].  
2 CONT
