0 @N6000000005599214198@ NOTE Welf (as Guelph) was appointed Duke by Emperor Henry IV in 1071.  He w as the ancestor of a branch of the House of Este, established in Germa ny, through which descends the male line of the House of Hanover.  Lat er, he became a l
1 CONC eader of the opposition to the Emperor and a supporte r of Rudolph of Swabia.  He joined an army of Crusaders in 1101 but di ed shorthly after having reached Jerusalem.
1 CONT
1 CONT (ref: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Welf_IV) Welf I (died about 9 Novem ber 1101, Paphos) was duke of Bavaria from 1070 to 1077 and from 1096t o his death. He was the first member of the Welf branch of the Houseo f Este. In the Wel
1 CONC f genealogy he is counted as Welf IV. Welf was theso n of Azzo II of Este and his wife Chuniza of Altdorf. When Welf's mate rnal uncle, Welf, Duke of Carinthia (also known as Welf III), died chi ldless, Welf inherited his property
1 CONC .  Welf married Ethelinde, daughte r of Otto II, Duke of Bavaria. When Duke Otto had become an enemy ofKi ng Henry IV, Welf divorced Ethelinde, and soon thereafter (in 1070)wa s appointed duke of Bavaria in Otto's stead. During th
1 CONC e InvestitureCon troversy, Welf sided with Pope Gregory VII, and in March 1077 supporte d the election of Rudolf of Rheinfelden as anti-king. In May 1077,he w as banned by the king.
1 CONT
1 CONT In 1089, Welf's son Welf married Matilda of Tuscany, thus strengthenin g relationships with the pope. After the younger Welf divorced Matild a in 1095, Welf made amends with King Henry IV and was reappointed asd uke of Bavaria. Af
1 CONC ter the death of his father Azzo in 1097, Welf trie d to acquire his father's property south of the Alps, but did not succ eed against his younger half-brother Fulco.  In 1099, Welf joined theC rusade of 1101. He died while return
1 CONC ing from the crusade in Cyprus in 1101 and was buried in Weingarten Abbey. He was succeeded as duke of B avaria by his son Welf.  Welf had the following children from his marr iage with Judith of Flanders, daughter of Baldwin IV, 
1 CONC Count of Flander s:
1 CONT 1.) Welf, born 1072; 2.) Henry; 3.) Kunizza, died 6 March 1120, marrie d Frederick Rocho, Count of Dießen
