0 @N6000000001540805277@ NOTE Baldwin IV, Count of Flanders
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT (Redirected from Baldwin IV of Flanders)
1 CONT Jump to: navigation, search
1 CONT Baldwin IV of Flanders (980?May 30, 1036), known as the Bearded, was Count of Flanders from 988 until his death. He was the son of Arnulf II of Flanders. His mother was Rozala of Lombardy. He was a seventh-generation descendant of
1 CONC  Charlemagne through his father and an eighth-generation one through his mother.
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] History
1 CONT In contrast to his predecessors Baldwin turned his attention to the east and north, leaving the southern part of his territory in the handsof his vassals the counts of Guînes, Hesdin, and St. Pol.
1 CONT
1 CONT To the north of the county Baldwin was given Zeeland as a fief by theHoly Roman Emperor Henry II, while on the right bank of the Scheldt river he received Valenciennes (1013) and parts of the Cambresis and Hainaut.
1 CONT
1 CONT In the French territories of the count of Flanders, the supremacy of the Baldwini remained unchallenged. They organized a great deal of colonization of marshland along the coastline of Flanders and enlarged the harbour and city of
1 CONC  Brugge.
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] Family
1 CONT Baldwin first married Ogive of Luxembourg, by whom he had a son and heir Baldwin V.
1 CONT
1 CONT He later married Eleanor of Normandy (or perhaps Ainor or Judith), widow of Duke Welf of Bavaria and daughter of Richard II of Normandy, bywhom he had at least one daughter Judith. This daughter married Tostig Godwinson, Earl of N
1 CONC orthumberland.[1] These family connections demonstrate the political interests of the Flemish counts, both in the Kingdom of France, England and the Holy Roman Empire.
1 CONT
1 CONT His granddaughter, Matilda of Flanders, would go on to marry William the Conqueror, therefore starting the line of Anglo-Norman Kings of England.
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] References
1 CONT ^ "Tostig, Earl of Northumbria". Dictionary of National Biography 19:998?1001.?
