0 @N6000000003615386114@ NOTE Baldwin IV (1160-85), Latin king of Jerusalem (1174-85), son and successor of Amalric I. During his reign, the Crusader kingdom was weakened by dissension between rival factions. Incapacitated by leprosy in 1183, Baldwin entrusted
