1 CONC f Waltheof, Earl of Northumberland , at the battle of Carham (c. 1016); he not only confirmed the Scottis h hold over the land between the rivers Forth and Tweed but also secur ed Strathclyde about the same time, defeating the Dan
1 CONC es in 1017. He la ter had a code of laws published. Eager to secure the royal successio n for his daughter's son Duncan, he triedto eliminate possible rival c laimants, but Macbeth, with royal connections to both Kenneth II and K 
1 CONC enneth III, survived to challenge the succession.  He was murdered 25 November 1034. [ Ref: Encyclopaedia Britannica CD, 1997, MALCOLM II; R oderick W. Stuart,Royalty for Commoners,3rd ed., Genealogical Publishi ng Company,Baltimo
