1 CONT Máel Coluim first appears in the historical record in 1057 when variou s chroniclers report the death of Mac Bethad at Máel Coluim's hand, pr obably on 15 August 1057 at Lumphanan, between Aboyne and Banchory. Ma c Bethad was succ
1 CONC eeded by his step-son Lulach mac Gille Coemgáin, whow as crowned at Scone, probably on 8 September 1057. Lulach was killedb y Máel Coluim, "by treachery," near Huntly on 23 April 1058. After thi s, Máel Coluim became king, perhaps
