0 @N6000000000269749583@ NOTE BIOGRAPHY: Jean JOURDAN van Cabriere, was 'n Franse Hugenoot wat omstreeks 1660 gebore is en in 1688 op Berg China in SA aangekom het. Hy was die broer van Pierre en het later eienaar van La Motte in Franschoek geword. Hy is oorle
1 CONC de in 1698. Hy was getroud in 1690 met Isabeau le LONG en het 3 seuns en een dogter gehad:
1 CONT
1 CONT BIOGRAPHY: 1. Jan x 19 Maart 1724 Susanna Jourdan 2. Paul ~ 25 Sep 1695 x Rachel Nel 3. Louis ~ 15 Jul 1697, burger Drakenstein, x 11 Apr 1728 Petronella van Staden xx 18 Okt 1739 Maria Guillaumet van Languedoc 4. Johanna ~ 18 Jan
1 CONC  1699, gebore na sy dood, x Daniel Krynauw xx 31 Okt 1734 Andries Hesselbaart van Halle in Sakse
1 CONT
1 CONT Ancestral File Number:<AFN> progenitor-a Jean Jourdan, from Cabrières-d'Aigues (France), born 1660. Arrives in 1688 on the ship Berg China, with his brother Pierre and his mother, the widow Jeanne Marthe Jourdan, born ca. 1628. He
1 CONC  was later the owner of the farm "La Motte" in Franschhoek (La Motte was a town close to Cabrieres). He died before January 1699. Married Elisabeth of Isabeau le Long (4 children).1  ARVL 2  DATE 1688 2  PLAC Kaap, aan boord van d
1 CONC ie "Berg China" 2  QUAY 0
0 @N6000000001634193366@ NOTE <!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC "-//W3C//DTD XHTML 1.0 Transitional//EN"
1 CONT           "http://www.w3.org/TR/xhtml1/DTD/xhtml1-transitional.dtd">
1 CONT <html  xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xml:lang="en" lang="en"><head>
1 CONT <title></title>
1 CONT <meta http-equiv="content-type" content="text/html;charset=utf-8"/>
1 CONT <meta http-equiv="Content-Style-Type" content="text/css"/>
1 CONT </head>
1 CONT <body>
1 CONT <div align="left"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><span style="font-size:9pt">Stamvader 2.</span></font></div>
1 CONT <div align="left"><br /></div>
1 CONT <div align="left"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><span style="font-size:9pt"><b>Jean JOURDAN</b> van Cabriere, was 'n Franse Hugenoot, van Saint-Martin de la Brasque (let 
1 CONT wel nie van Cabriere d'Aigues nie). Hy was gebore 1660 die kind van Pierre Jourdan en Jeanne 
1 CONT Marthe. Hy het by die Kaap aangekom in 1688 op <i>Berg China</i>. Hy was die broer van Pierre en 
1 CONT het later eienaar van Languedoc en Rhone in Groot Drakenstein vanaf 1708 (oorgedra deur sy 
1 CONT stiefpa Jacques Mallan). Hy is oorlede in 1698. Hy was getroud in 1690 met <b>Isabeau le LONG 
1 CONT </b>en het 3 seuns en een dogter gehad.</span></font></div>
1 CONT </body>
1 CONT </html>
0 @N6000000000234293921@ NOTE Arrived from Saint Martin de la Brasque, Province, on th e "Berg China" in 1668, later owner of the farm "La Motte " in Franschoek.
0 @N6000000001634203691@ NOTE <!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC "-//W3C//DTD XHTML 1.0 Transitional//EN"
1 CONT           "http://www.w3.org/TR/xhtml1/DTD/xhtml1-transitional.dtd">
1 CONT <html  xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xml:lang="en" lang="en"><head>
1 CONT <title></title>
1 CONT <meta http-equiv="content-type" content="text/html;charset=utf-8"/>
1 CONT <meta http-equiv="Content-Style-Type" content="text/css"/>
1 CONT </head>
1 CONT <body>
1 CONT <div align="left"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><span style="font-size:9pt">The children are given as found in the Inventory and Deceased<br />
1 CONT Estate Accounts of their mother, dated May 1755.<br />
1 CONT </span></font><img src="HTS_1.PNG" width="10" height="4" border="0" alt="graphic"/><br />
1 CONT <font face="Verdana" size="1"><span style="font-size:9pt">In the above accounts are listed various properties. The farm<br />
1 CONT Drogevalij in the Paardeberg would seem, from the furnishings,<br />
1 CONT to have been their main home, but they also had a well furnished<br />
1 CONT house in the Table Valley of Cape Town, and five other farms:<br />
1 CONT Voorspoed in Riebeek Casteel, Bruijntjes Rivier at Klipheuvel,<br />
1 CONT Keurbooms Rivier in that area, Vette Rivier situated on that river<br />
1 CONT and another called Vette Rivier not far from the first. They also<br />
1 CONT owned a grave plot or vault ('een grafsteede) in the church at<br />
1 CONT Swartland.<br />
1 CONT </span></font><img src="HTS_2.PNG" width="10" height="4" border="0" alt="graphic"/><br />
1 CONT <font face="Verdana" size="1"><span style="font-size:9pt">The inventory of the estate suggest they were very comfortably<br />
1 CONT off, with two slaves in the Cape Town house and 32 slaves on<br />
1 CONT the farms, a quantity of gold and silver objects, a total of 305<br />
1 CONT cattle, 2000 sheep and 36 horses.<br />
1 CONT </span></font><img src="HTS_3.PNG" width="10" height="4" border="0" alt="graphic"/><br />
1 CONT <font face="Verdana" size="1"><span style="font-size:9pt">The house at the Cape and that at Drogevallij both consisted of<br />
1 CONT a Voorhuis (main room) with a room on each side and a kitchen,<br />
1 CONT but the farmhouse had also a Corn store, a workshop, a cellar,<br />
1 CONT a stable and a yard.<br />
1 CONT </span></font><img src="HTS_4.PNG" width="10" height="4" border="0" alt="graphic"/><br />
1 CONT <font face="Verdana" size="1"><span style="font-size:9pt">The farm Drooge Valliej was bought from the deceased estate<br />
1 CONT of Maria van der Westhuisen for 5000 gulden, 23 Nov. 1734.</span></font></div>
1 CONT </body>
1 CONT </html>
0 @N6000000000234220934@ NOTE Boer in die Roodesand-gedeelte van Drakenstein.
