1 CONT
1 CONT Judith of Brittany
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT This biographical article does not cite any references or sources. (October 2007)
1 CONT
1 CONT Judith of Brittany (982 – 1017) was the daughter of Conan I, Duke of Brittany and the mother of Robert the Magnificent.
1 CONT
1 CONT She was the first wife of Richard the Good, Duke of Normandy, whom she married in 996. They had six children:
1 CONT
1 CONT    1. Richard the Third, succeeded his father in the dukedom;
1 CONT    2. Robert, who succeeded his elder brother;
1 CONT    3. William, called William of Normandy, who became a monk in the Abbey of Fécamp, and died very young in 1025;
1 CONT    4. Alice, married to Renauld, earl of Burgundy;
1 CONT    5. Eleanor, to Baldwin, earl of Flanders;
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT The duchess Judith died in 1017 and was buried in the abbey of Bernay, which she had founded.
1 CONT
1 CONT ==========
0 @N6000000000269768337@ NOTE Judith de Bretagne1 F, #102170, b. circa 982, d. 1017
1 CONT
1 CONT Judith de Bretagne|b. c 982\nd. 1017|p10217.htm#i102170|Conon I de Rennes, Duc de Bretagne|b. b 970\nd. 992|p10482.htm#i104812|Ermengarde d'Anjou|b. b 963|p289.htm#i2881|Judhael de Rennes, Comte de Rennes|d. a 969|p398.htm#i3980|G
1 CONC eberge (?)||p399.htm#i3981|Geoffrey I. d'Anjou, 4th Comte d'Anjou|d. 21 Jul 987|p399.htm#i3982|Adelais de Vermandois|b. c 950\nd. a 975|p399.htm#i3983|
1 CONT
1 CONT Last Edited=7 Apr 2007
1 CONT      Judith de Bretagne was born circa 982.1 She was the daughter of Conon I de Rennes, Duc de Bretagne and Ermengarde d'Anjou.1 She married Richard II, 4th Duc de Normandie, son of Richard I, 3rd Duc de Normandie and Gunnor de Cr
1 CONC êpon, circa 1000.1 She died in 1017.1 Children of Judith de Bretagne and Richard II, 4th Duc de Normandie William de Féchamp d. 10251 Adelaide de Normandie+ d. 27 Jul 10371 Eleonora de Normandie+ 1 Matilda de Normandie d. 10332 Ri
1 CONC chard III, 5th Duc de Normandie b. b 1008, d. 6 Aug 1027 Robert I, 6th Duc de Normandie+ b. c 1008, d. 22 Jun 1035 Citations [S106] Royal Genealogies Website (ROYAL92.GED), online <ftp://ftp.cac.psu.edu/genealogy/public_html/royal
1 CONC /index.html>. Hereinafter cited as Royal Genealogies Website. [S130] Wikipedia, online www.wikipedia.org. Hereinafter cited as Wikipedia.
