1 CONT
1 CONT Marriage and Children
1 CONT
1 CONT She was the first wife of Richard the Good, Duke of Normandy, whom she married in 996. They had six children:
1 CONT Richard the Third, succeeded his father in the dukedom;
1 CONT Robert, who succeeded his elder brother;
1 CONT William, called William of Normandy, who became a monk in the Abbey of Fécamp, and died very young in 1025;
1 CONT Alice, married to Renauld, earl of Burgundy;
1 CONT Eleanor, to Baldwin, earl of Flanders;
1 CONT The duchess Judith died in 1017 and was buried in the abbey of Bernay, which she had founded
