0 @N6000000002187570201@ NOTE Richard II of Normandy
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.
1 CONT
1 CONT Richard II, known as Richard The Good, (in French, "le Bon"), was the son and heir of Richard I the Fearless and the Duchess Gunnora. Succeeded his father as Duke of Normandy in 996. Richard held his own against a peasant insurrec
1 CONC tion, and helped Robert II of France against the duchy of Burgundy. He also repelled an English attack on the Cotentin Peninsula that was led by the Anglo-Saxon King Ethelred II the Unready. He pursued a reform of the Norman monas
1 CONC teries.
1 CONT
1 CONT He married firstly (in 996) Judith (d.1017), daughter of Conan I, Duke of Brittany, by whom he had the following issue:
1 CONT
1 CONT Richard, duke of Normandy 
1 CONT Robert, duke of Normandy 
1 CONT William, monk at Fécamp, d.1025 
1 CONT Adélaide, married Renaud I, Count of Burgundy 
1 CONT Eleanor (or perhaps Ainor or Judith), married Count Baldwin IV of Flanders 
1 CONT Matilda, d.1033 
1 CONT He married secondly on Papia, by whom he had the following issue:
1 CONT
1 CONT Mauger, Archbishop of Rouen 
1 CONT William, count of Arques 
1 CONT
1 CONT Preceded by:
1 CONT Richard I Duke of Normandy
1 CONT 996–1026 Succeeded by:
1 CONT Richard III 
0 @N6000000003615761531@ NOTE Duke of Normandy
0 @N6000000003949642309@ NOTE byname RICHARD The GOOD, French RICHARD le BON (d. 1026/27), duke of Normandy (996-1026/27), son of Richard I the Fearless. He held his own against a peasant insurrection, helped Robert II of France against the duchy of Burgundy, 
1 CONC and repelled an English attack on the Cotentin Peninsula that was led by the Anglo-Saxon king Ethelred II the Unready. He also pursued a reform of the Norman monasteries. [Encyclopaedia Britannica CD '97]
