0 @N6000000000337179117@ NOTE (Research):Robert I Encyclopædia Britannica Article    died July 1035, Nicaea   byname Robert The Magnificent, or The Devil,  French Robert Le Magnifique, or Le Diable duke of Normandy (1027-35), the younger son of Richard II of N
1 CONC ormandy and the father, by his mistress Arlette, of William the Conqueror of England. On the death of his father (1026/27), Robert contested the duchy with his elder brother Richard III, legally the heir, until the latter's opport
1 CONC une death a few years later. A strong ruler, Robert succeeded in exacting the obedience of his vassals. On the death of Robert II the Pious, king of France (1031), a crisis arose over the succession to the French throne. The Duke 
1 CONC gave his support to Henry I against the party favouring his younger brother; in reward for his services he demanded and received the Vexin Français, a territory not far north of Paris. A patron of the monastic reform movement, he 
1 CONC died while returning from a pilgrimage to Jerusalem.
