0 @N6000000001956371042@ NOTE
1 CONT Baldwin Of Lille, French Baudouin De Lille, Dutch Boudewijn Van Rijselcount of Flanders who became one of the most influential figures of 11th-century Europe. He wasan active, enterprising man and greatly extended his power by war
1 CONC s and alliances. He obtained from the Holy Roman emperor Henry IV the territory between the Scheldt and the Dender as an imperial fief, as well as the margravate of Antwerp. So powerful had he become that on the decease of Henry I
1 CONC  of France he was appointed regent during the minority of Philip I (1060–66). Before his death he saw his eldest daughter Matilda (d. 1083) sharing the English throne with William the Conqueror; saw his eldest son, Baldwin of Mons
1 CONC , in possession of Hainaut in right of his wife Richilde, heiress of Regnier V (d. 1036); and saw his second son, Robert the Frisian, regent (voogd) of the county of Holland.
0 @N6000000001540958238@ NOTE Baldwin V, Count of Flanders
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT (Redirected from Baldwin V of Flanders)
1 CONT Jump to: navigation, search
1 CONT Baldwin V of Flanders (died September 1, 1067) was Count of Flanders from 1036 until his death.
1 CONT
1 CONT He was the son of Baldwin IV of Flanders, who died in 1035. He, in turn, was a descendant of Ælfthryth, daughter of Alfred the Great, SaxonKing of England.
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] History
1 CONT In 1028 Baldwin married Adèle of France in Amiens, daughter of King Robert II of France; at her instigation he rebelled against his father but in 1030 peace was sworn and the old count continued to rule until his death.
1 CONT
1 CONT During a long war (1046?1056) as an ally of Godfrey the Bearded, Dukeof Lorraine, against the Holy Roman Emperor Henry III, he initially lost Valenciennes to Hermann of Hainaut. However, when the latter died in 1049 Baldwin marrie
1 CONC d his son Baldwin VI to Herman's widow Richildisand arranged that the sons of her first marriage were disinherited, thus de facto uniting the County of Hainaut with Flanders. Upon the death of Henry III this marriage was acknowled
1 CONC ged by treaty by Agnes de Poitou, mother and regent of Henry IV.
1 CONT
1 CONT From 1060 to 1067 Baldwin was the co-Regent with Anne of Kiev for hisnephew-by-marriage Philip I of France, indicating the importance he had acquired in international politics.
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] Family
1 CONT Baldwin and Adèle had five children:
1 CONT
1 CONT Baldwin VI, 1030-1070
1 CONT Matilda, c.1031-1083 who married William the Conqueror
1 CONT Robert I of Flanders, c.1033?1093
1 CONT Henry of Flanders c.1035
1 CONT Sir Richard of Flanders c. 1050-1105
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] References
1 CONT Tanner, Heather J, Families, Friends and Allies: Boulogne and Politics in Northern France and England, C.879-1160
