1 CONT In 1028 Baldwin married Adèle of France </wiki/Adela_of_France,_Countess_of_Flanders> in Amiens, daughter of King Robert II of France </wiki/Robert_II_of_France>; at her instigation he rebelled against his father but in 1030 peace
1 CONC  was sworn and the old count continued to rule until his death.
1 CONT During a long war (1046-1056) as an ally of Godfrey the Bearded </wiki/Godfrey_the_Bearded>, Duke of Lorraine </wiki/Duchy_of_Lorraine>, against the Holy Roman Emperor </wiki/Holy_Roman_Emperor> Henry III </wiki/Henry_III,_Holy_Ro
1 CONC man_Emperor>, he initially lost Valenciennes to Hermann of Hainaut </w/index.php?title=Hermann_of_Hainaut&action=edit&redlink=1>. However, when the latter died in 1051 Baldwin married his son Baldwin VI to Herman's widow Richildis
1 CONC  </w/index.php?title=Richildis&action=edit&redlink=1> and arranged that the sons of her first marriage were disinherited, thus de facto uniting the County of Hainaut </wiki/County_of_Hainaut> with Flanders. Upon the death of Henry
1 CONC  III this marriage was acknowledged by treaty by Agnes de Poitou </wiki/Agnes_de_Poitou>, mother and regent of Henry IV </wiki/Henry_IV,_Holy_Roman_Emperor>.
1 CONT From 1060 to 1067 Baldwin was the co-Regent </wiki/Regent> with Anne of Kiev </wiki/Anne_of_Kiev> for his nephew-by-marriage Philip I of France </wiki/Philip_I_of_France>, indicating the importance he had acquired in international
1 CONC  politics.
1 CONT Baldwin and Adèle had five children:
1 CONT Baldwin VI </wiki/Baldwin_VI,_Count_of_Flanders>, 1030-1070
1 CONT Matilda </wiki/Matilda_of_Flanders>, c.1031-1083 who married William the Conqueror </wiki/William_I_of_England>
1 CONT Robert I of Flanders </wiki/Robert_I,_Count_of_Flanders>, c.1033-1093
1 CONT Henry of Flanders c.1035
1 CONT Sir Richard of Flanders </w/index.php?title=Richard_of_Flanders&action=edit&redlink=1> c. 1050-1105
0 @N6000000000232595886@ NOTE ==========
1 CONT
1 CONT Baldwin V, Count of Flanders
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT   (Redirected from Baldwin V of Flanders)
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT Baldwin V of Flanders (died September 1, 1067) was Count of Flanders from 1036 until his death.
1 CONT
1 CONT He was the son of Baldwin IV of Flanders, who died in 1035. He, in turn, was a descendant of Ælfthryth, daughter of Alfred the Great, Saxon King of England.
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] History
1 CONT
1 CONT In 1028 Baldwin married Adèle of France in Amiens, daughter of King Robert II of France; at her instigation he rebelled against his father but in 1030 peace was sworn and the old count continued to rule until his death.
1 CONT
1 CONT During a long war (1046–1056) as an ally of Godfrey the Bearded, Duke of Lorraine, against the Holy Roman Emperor Henry III, he initially lost Valenciennes to Hermann of Hainaut. However, when the latter died in 1049 Baldwin marri
1 CONC ed his son Baldwin VI to Herman's widow Richildis and arranged that the sons of her first marriage were disinherited, thus de facto uniting the County of Hainaut with Flanders. Upon the death of Henry III this marriage was acknowl
1 CONC edged by treaty by Agnes de Poitou, mother and regent of Henry IV.
1 CONT
1 CONT From 1060 to 1067 Baldwin was the co-Regent with Anne of Kiev for his nephew-by-marriage Philip I of France, indicating the importance he had acquired in international politics.
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] Family
1 CONT
1 CONT Baldwin and Adèle had five children:
1 CONT
1 CONT     * Baldwin VI, 1030-1070
1 CONT     * Matilda, c.1031-1083 who married William the Conqueror
1 CONT     * Robert I of Flanders, c.1033–1093
1 CONT     * Henry of Flanders c.1035
1 CONT     * Sir Richard of Flanders c. 1050-1105
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] References
1 CONT
1 CONT     * Tanner, Heather J, Families, Friends and Allies: Boulogne and Politics in Northern France and England, C.879-1160
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT ==========
